  1486,Noncommutative Geometry and Fundamental Physics,"https://alainconnes.org/wp-content/uploads/ncgphysics.pdf",alainconnes.org,math-ph,math-ph math.OA math.QA math.FA physics mathematics noncommutative-geometry mathematical-physics functional-analysis nonstandard-analysis survey,null,null,null,"Noncommutative Geometry and Fundamental Physics. Alain Connes' landmark survey detailing: - **Quantum Variables:** Real variables correspond to self-adjoint operators in Hilbert space; infinitesimals correspond to compact operators. - **Metric Structures:** Distance formula $d(p, q) = \\sup \\{|f(p) - f(q)| : \\|[D, f]\\| \\le 1\\}$, where the line element $ds = D^{-1}$ is the fermion propagator. - **Thermodynamics & Time:** Noncommutativity implies a canonical 1-parameter automorphism group $\\delta_t \\in \\operatorname{Out}(\\mathcal{A})$ via the Tomita–Takesaki KMS condition. - **Bost-Connes System:** Exhibits spontaneous symmetry breaking at critical temperature $\\beta = 1$ with the Riemann zeta function $\\zeta(\\beta)$ as the partition function."
