  1559,"Geometry of the Adele Class Space: Part I","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=69-_otYjClg",youtube.com,math.NT,math.NT math.AG math.CT mathematics adeles schemes topos-theory algebraic-geometry etale-cohomology youtube,null,null,null,"Geometry of the Adele Class Space: Part I. Alain Connes' lecture exploring: - **Number Fields & Schemes:** Unifying number rings $\\mathcal{O}_K$, function fields $\\mathbb{F}_q(C)$, and Riemann surfaces as 1-dimensional regular schemes. - **Galois Theory & Etale Topology:** Separable algebras, traces, finite étale morphisms, and why $\\operatorname{Spec} \\mathbb{Z}$ behaves as a simply connected 3-manifold where primes are knots. - **Topos Semantics:** Topoi allow groups/monoids to act naturally. The topos $([0, \\infty) \\rtimes \\mathbb{N}^\\times)$ computes points over the Boolean semifield $\\mathbb{B} = \\{0,1\\}$, recovering the adèle class space."
  1560,"Geometry of the Adele Class Space: Part II","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XPVfElqM264",youtube.com,math.NT,math.NT math.AG mathematics adeles topos-theory tropical-geometry algebraic-number-theory youtube,null,null,null,"Geometry of the Adele Class Space: Part II. Alain Connes' second lecture: - **Adèles & Global Fields:** Global fields sit discretely and cocompactly in their locally compact adèle rings $\\mathbb{A}_K$. - **Trace Formulas & Absorption Spectra:** The scaling action on $K_v$ has Schwartz kernel $\\delta(y - \\lambda x)$ with trace $\\int \\delta(x - \\lambda x)\\,dx = 1/|1-\\lambda|$. Zeros of $L$-functions emerge as an absorption spectrum, explaining the minus sign in explicit formulas. - **The Arithmetic Site:** The topos $(\\mathbb{N}^\\times, \\mathbb{Z}_{\\max})$ over the tropical semifield $\\mathbb{R}_{\\max}$ exhibits Frobenius automorphisms $\\operatorname{Fr}_\\lambda(x) = x^\\lambda$, establishing an explicit Riemann–Roch theorem for number fields."
