  2592,Hybrid Post-Quantum Key Exchange for TLS 1.3 - セキュリティエンジニアリング特論 第11回,"https://github.com/junkurihara/lecture-security_engineering/blob/master/slides2025-11.pdf",github.com,cs.CR,cs.CR computer-science security-and-privacy slides github,null,2026,null,"Hybrid Post-Quantum Key Exchange for TLS 1.3 - セキュリティエンジニアリング特論 第11回. Beamer slides, 2026; 40 pages. Part of Security Engineering: Lecture slides and some program sources of a lecture Security Engineering'' at University of Hyogo from 2020--2025 Fall program. Sections: ML-KEM; Hybrid PQ KX. Subsections include Hybrid PQ KX Framework in TLS 1.3, and Hybrid PQ KX in TLS 1.3: ECDHE-MLKEM. Slides cover ྉͷҐஔ ͚, ίϯβϡʔλ, తʹͳͬͨΒରԠ͢Ε ͍͍ͷ͔ʁ, ML -KEM, ͷඪ४Խ, NIST FIPSͱͳͬͨ Round 3 Finalists, ͱ͍͏Θ͚ͰɼML-KEM ʹয Λ ͯΔ, ΧΎηϧԽ (Key Encapsulation Mechanism) ͱ ʁ, Forward Secrecy Λ༗͢Δ (EC)DHE15ఆ͞Ε͍ͯΔɽ16, and ަݤKey Exchange; KX) : (EC)DHࣜ."
  2593,"Енергія електричного поля: Лекції з електрики та магнетизму","https://github.com/sergiokapone/ElMagLectures/blob/main/ElEnergy/ElEnergy.pdf",github.com,cs.RO,cs.RO computer-science robotics slides github,null,2026,null,"Енергія електричного поля: Лекції з електрики та магнетизму. Beamer slides, 2026; 25 pages, in Ukrainian. Part of Лекції з дисципліни \"Електрика та магнетизм\": 1. Постійне електричне поле в вакуумі 2. Subject (translated): robotics. Sections: Електрична ємність; Енергія електричного поля; Пондеромоторні сили. Slides cover Зміст, Ємність провідника, Конденсатори, З'єднання конденсаторів, Задачі, Взаємна ємність двох куль, Взаємна енергія системи зарядів, Електростатична енергія тіл, Енергія електричного поля в конденсаторі, and Енергія електричного поля (загальне виведення)."
  2594,"lion-logo CTAN: Auf dem Weg zu Release 3","https://gitlab.com/comprehensive-tex-archive-network/dante-2026/-/blob/main/2026-ctan-dante.pdf",gitlab.com,math.AG,math.AG math.CA math.RT mathematics geometric-langlands real-analysis slides gitlab,Gerd Neugebauer,2026,null,"lion-logo CTAN: Auf dem Weg zu Release 3. Beamer slides by Gerd Neugebauer, 2026; 33 pages, in German. Part of Presentation for DANTE Frühjahrstagung 2026: https://www.dante.de/veranstaltungen/dante2026/. Sections: CTAN; Release 3; Release 2 betreiben; CDN-Dispatcher; Fragen. Subsections include Prozesse, Team und Aufgaben, Projektrisiko, Client-Arbeiten, Server-Entwicklung, Online-Hilfe, Teaser für Pakete und Themen, I18N für Pakete und Themen, I18N für Pakete, and Integrationstests. Slides cover Was macht CTAN?, Das Team hat viel zu tun, Das CTAN-Team und die Aufgabenbereiche, Ich sollte etwas Unterstützung bekommen, Was macht der Web-Master eingentlich?, Die Architektur für Release 3 ist fertig, Die Arbeiten an Release 3 sind im Gange, Das Aussehen kann der Nutzer beeinflussen, Das Aussehen wurde überarbeitet, and Beschreibung der Oberfläche ist fortgeschritten."
  2595,Lecture 01 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2026-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-01.pdf",gitlab.com,math.LO,math.LO mathematics mathematical-logic lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2026,null,"Lecture 01 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2026; 55 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2026-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: dm 0.2 Mathematical Statements. Subsections include Atomic and Molecular Statements, Implications, Converses and Contrapositives, Necessity and Sufficiency, and Predicates and Quantifiers. Slides cover Assignments1, Why Should I Care About Logic?, Statements, Examples of Non-Statements, Logic Connectives, Notations of Logical Connectives, Implications, True or False?, Implication Does Not Mean Causality, and Converses."
  2596,Lecture 03 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2026-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-03.pdf",gitlab.com,math.LO,math.LO cs.PL math.PR mathematics computer-science mathematical-logic programming-languages random-matrix-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2026,null,"Lecture 03 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2026; 70 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2026-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: dm 1.3 Rules of Logic. Subsections include Truth Tables, Xor — Exclusive-or, Logical Equivalence, Deductions — How to Argue with Logic, and Beyond Propositions. Slides cover Assignments1, A Proposition About Monopoly, Truth Tables, Logic and Modern Compilers, Knights and Knaves Puzzles, Truth Table to Help, Exercise, Logical Equivalence, Basic Logical Equivalences (1), and Basic Logical Equivalences (2)."
  2597,Lecture 04 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2026-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-04.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.NT mathematics combinatorics number-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2026,null,"Lecture 04 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2026; 75 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2026-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: dm 1.4 Proofs. Subsections include What Is a Mathematical Proof?, Direct Proof, Proof by Contrapositive, Proof by Contradiction, Proof by Counterexample, Proof by Cases, and Proof of If and Only If. Slides cover Assignments1, What Is a Mathematical Proof?, Euclid’s Proof, Critiquing a Proof: What Went Wrong?, Direct Proofs, Proof by Contradiction, The Pigeonhole Principle — Example 1.4.17, A Special Case of Proof by Contradiction, A Formula for Primes?, and Proof by Cases."
  2598,Lecture 06 — Test of Convergence - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2026-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-06.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA mathematics real-analysis lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2026,null,"Lecture 06 — Test of Convergence - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2026; 65 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2026-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ec 9.2 Test of Convergence. Subsections include Sequences Differ in Finitely Many Places, Monotone Bounded Test (for Sequences), Comparison Test (for Sequences), n-th Term Test (for Series), and Ratio Test (for Series). Slides cover Assignments1, Google’s PageRank: Guaranteed Convergence, Sequences Differ in Finitely Many Places, Make a Guess, Impact of Finite Changes on Limits, Example: Bounded Sequence, Bounded Sequence, Convergence and Boundedness, Monotone Sequence, and Monotone Bounded Test."
  2599,Lecture 07 — Alternating Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2026-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-07.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA mathematics real-analysis lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2026,null,"Lecture 07 — Alternating Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2026; 68 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2026-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ec 9.2 Test of Convergence (Continued); ec 9.3 Alternating Series. Subsections include Integral Test (for Series), p-Series Test (for Series), Comparison Test (for Series), Limit Comparison Test (for Series), Telescoping Series Test (for Series), Properties of Convergent Series, Alternating Series Test, and Absolute and Conditional Convergence. Slides cover Assignments1, Proof of the Integral Test — Divergent Case, Proof of the Integral Test — Convergent Case, Why a Decreasing Function?, Example 9.10, Comparison Test (for Series), Limit Comparison Test (for Series), Example 9.12, Telescoping Series Test, and Properties of Convergent Series."
  2600,Lecture 08 — Power Series and Taylor Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2026-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-08.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA mathematics real-analysis lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2026,null,"Lecture 08 — Power Series and Taylor Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2026; 69 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2026-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ec 9.4 Power Series; ec 9.5 Taylor Series. Subsections include Interval of Convergence, Differentiation and Integration, Taylor's Formula, and Approximate a Function. Slides cover Assignments1, Cheating ?, Power Series, Interval of Convergence, Example 9.17, Differentiation and Integration, Example 9.20, Review — Big-ONotation, Remainder Theorem, and Review — Fundamental Theorem of Calculus (ftc) II."
  2601,"Lecture 09— Strings, Sets, and Binomial Coefficients (1) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01)","https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2026-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-09.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AR,cs.AR math.CO math.RT math.RA computer-science mathematics combinatorics computer-architecture quiver-representations lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2026,null,"Lecture 09— Strings, Sets, and Binomial Coefficients (1) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2026; 50 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2026-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 2 Strings, Sets, and Binomial Coefficients. Subsections include 2.1 Strings, 2.2 Permutations, and 2.3 Combinations. Slides cover Assignments1, Strings, Examples of Strings, Example: My Breakfast, Strings and CPU (What does “64-bit” mean?), An Ancient Chinese Combinatorial Problem, Example: My Lunch, Strings with Restrictions, Good and Bad Passwords, and Letters From a Bag."
