  2603,Lecture 12 — Induction - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2026-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-12.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2026,null,"Lecture 12 — Induction - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2026; 69 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2026-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 3.4 Binomial Coefficients Revisited; ac 3.5 Solving Combinatorial Problems Recursively; ac 3.8 Proof by Induction. Subsections include A Game of, Tiling a Grid, Ternary Strings, What Is Induction, Example Proofs by Induction, A More Interesting Example of Induction, and Strong Induction. Slides cover Assignments1, An Experiment, Example 3.3 — The Proof, A Recursive Formula, The Initial Value, Example 3.6 — Ternary Strings, Example 3.6 — The Recursive Formula, What Is Induction, Proof by Induction, and Proposition 3.14 (ac)."
