  2605,Lecture 15— Generating Functions (1) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2026-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-15.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics combinatorics formalization lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2026,null,"Lecture 15— Generating Functions (1) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2026; 62 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2026-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 8.1 Basic Notions and Terminology. Subsections include Gfs Are Not Functions, and A Taste of Formalization of gfs. Slides cover Assignments1, Why Generating function (gf)?, What Is a generating function (gf), The Advantage of Generating Functions, Equality of Two Gfs, Review — Multiply Polynomials, Multiply gfs, Multiplicative Inverse of gf, Composition of gfs, and Example of Closed Forms."
