  2611,Lecture 22 — Trees - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2026-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-22.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics graph-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2026,null,"Lecture 22 — Trees - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2026; 56 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2026-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: dm 2.2 Trees. Subsections include Definitions of Trees, Properties of Trees, Rooted Trees, Bipartite Graphs, Spanning Trees, and Cut Edges. Slides cover Assignments1, Acyclic Graphs, Forests, Wooclap, Proposition 2.2.2, Proposition 2.2.4 (dm), Proposition 2.2.5, Exercise, Where to Put the Root?, and Bipartite Graphs."
