  2613,Lecture 25 — Graph Colouring (1) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2026-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-25.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.AT mathematics graph-theory chromatic-homotopy-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2026,null,"Lecture 25 — Graph Colouring (1) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2026; 62 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2026-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 5.4 Graph Colouring. Subsections include Motivational Example, Chromatic Number, Chromatic Number of Specific Graphs, Chromatic Number of Cycles, and Chromatic Number of Bipartite Graphs. Slides cover Assignments1, Colours to Help, Can We Do Better?, Chromatic Number, Chromatic Number of Specific Graphs, Complete Graphs, Not So Simple!, Even Cycle, Chromatic Number of Bipartite Graphs, and The Mysterious K1."
  2614,Lecture 26 — Graph Colouring (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2026-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-26.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.AT mathematics graph-theory chromatic-homotopy-theory extremal-combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2026,null,"Lecture 26 — Graph Colouring (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2026; 45 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2026-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 5.4.2 Cliques and Chromatic Number. Subsections include Cliques and Clique Number, Proof of Proposition 5.25 (ac) by J. Kelly and L. Kelly, and Proof of Proposition 5.25 (ac) by J. Mycielski. Slides cover Assignments1, Review — Induced Subgraphs, Clique Number and Chromatic Number, Proposition 5.25 (ac) — Can χ(G) be much larger than ω(G)?, Proof of Proposition 5.25 (ac) by J. Kelly and L. Kelly, Proposition 5.24 (ac) — Generalized Hole Principle, Proof of Proposition 5.25 (ac) by Kelly and Kelly — A Sketch, Construct Gt+1, Verify Gt+1 is -free, and Proof of Proposition 5.25 (ac) by J. Mycielski."
  2615,Lecture 27 – Graph Colouring (3) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2026-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-27.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO cs.DS math.AT mathematics computer-science graph-theory algorithms chromatic-homotopy-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2026,null,"Lecture 27 – Graph Colouring (3) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2026; 62 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2026-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 5.4.2 Cliques and Chromatic Number; ac 5.4.3 Can We Determine Chromatic Number?. Subsections include Cliques and Clique Number, First-Fit Algorithm, Maximum Degrees and Chromatic Numbers, Interval Graphs, Perfect Graphs, and Strong Perfect Graph Theorem. Slides cover Assignments1, Cliques in a Graph, Wooclap, First-Fit Algorithm, Example — First-Fit Algorithm, The Maximum Degree, Theorem 4.4.5 (dm) — Brooks’ Theorem, Perfect Graphs, Can you see why every interval graph is perfect?, and Definition — Hole."
  2616,Lecture 28 — Planar Graphs - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2026-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-28.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics graph-theory lecture-notes slides problem-list gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2026,null,"Lecture 28 — Planar Graphs - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2026-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2026; 50 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2026-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 5.5 Planar Graphs. Subsections include Definitions of Planar Graphs, Euler's Formula, Is This Planar? — A Simple Check, Kuratowski's Theorem, and Four Colour Theorem. Slides cover Required Reading and Exercises, Planar Graphs, Euler’s Formula, Faces of a Planar Graph, Theorem 5.32 (ac) — Euler’s Formula, Euler’s Formula — Induction Step (Case 1), Euler’s Formula — Induction Step (Case 2), An Inequality, Theorem 5.33 (ac) — Applications, and Kuratowski’s Theorem."
