  2703,Statistical analysis of tensor variate data,"https://github.com/StatPal/tensor-variate-data-analysis-lectures/blob/main/final_class_presentation.pdf",github.com,math.RA,math.RA math.NA math.ST math.FA mathematics linear-algebra statistics functional-analysis lecture-notes slides github,Subrata Pal,2025,null,"Statistical analysis of tensor variate data. Beamer slides by Subrata Pal, 2025; 80 pages. Part of Statistical Analysis of Tensor-Variate Data: Lecture slides from two guest lectures on tensor-variate data analysis, delivered in STAT 5010: Multivariate Statistical Methods, Spring 2025, Iowa State University (instructed by Prof. Ranjan Maitra). Sections: Tensor?? What's that!; Enter Tensor Variate Regime; How to Estimate??; Tensor on Tensor (Time series) Regression; Future Work. Subsections include Tensor Diagrams, Reshaping/Flattening, Tensor Multiplication, Tensor variate Distribution, Tensor Decompositions, A few more things, and Computational Simplifications!. Slides cover Tensor?? What’s that!, The journey of Multivariate statistics, Matrix data?, Scalar to Vector to Matrix to Tensor, Tensor Diagrams, Reshape a tensor to a matrix/vector, Reshaping (contd.), Matrix/Tensor times Vector, Confused?, and Little bit more: Multiplication with tensors."
  2704,Distributed Systems,"https://github.com/SuperPung/TJU-CourseSharing/blob/main/2440186_%E5%88%86%E5%B8%83%E5%BC%8F%E7%B3%BB%E7%BB%9F/%E8%AF%BE%E4%BB%B6/2025-2026_%E5%89%91%E6%A1%A5_%E5%88%86%E5%B8%83%E5%BC%8F%E7%B3%BB%E7%BB%9F_PPT.pdf",github.com,cs.DC,cs.DC computer-science distributed-systems concurrency lecture-notes slides github,null,2025,null,"Distributed Systems. Beamer slides, 2025; 523 pages. From the course-materials archive SuperPung/TJU-CourseSharing. Sections: Models of distributed systems; Time, clocks, and ordering of events; Broadcast; Replication; Replica consistency; Consensus and total order broadcast; Eventual consistency. Slides cover The second half of Concurrent and Distributed Systems, Two models of concurrency, Achieving high availability: fault tolerance, Generals who might lie, Quartz clocks, Monotonic and time-of-day clocks, Lamport clocks example, Causal broadcast, Retrying state updates, and Quorum (2 out of 3)."
  2705,Линейные вмешательства в представлениях больших языковых моделей для снижения отказов по этическим причинам,"https://github.com/amkatrutsa/nla2025_masters/blob/main/projects/slides/ethic_limit.pdf",github.com,math.NA,math.NA cs.CL math.RA cs.AI mathematics computer-science large-language-models linear-algebra numerical-analysis lecture-notes slides github,null,2025,null,"Линейные вмешательства в представлениях больших языковых моделей для снижения отказов по этическим причинам. Beamer slides, 2025; 18 pages, in Russian. Part of Numerical linear algebra course, AI Masters, Fall 2025. Slides cover Новый этап элайнмента: отказ на основе этических оценок в LLM, Таксономия методов снятия семантических блокировок, Основная гипотеза: низкоразмерное пространство отказа, Как мы измеряем эффект: ASR, UPR и Perplexity, Два подхода: как они видят структуру отказа, Два подхода: как они вмешиваются и чего ожидать на практике, Глобальная картина: Attack vs Utility для всех моделей, Qwen + SOM: локальный трэйд-офф атаки и полезности, Траектории по силе вмешательства: Qwen vs Llama, SOM против Refusal Reduction: два взгляда на disalignment, Сравнение моделей, Анализ перплексии атакованных моделей, Тепловая карта перплексии по моделям и конфигурациям, and Лучшие конфигурации: Pareto-баланс атаки и полезности."
  2706,Исследование способов улучшения стабильности методов калмановской фильтрации,"https://github.com/amkatrutsa/nla2025_masters/blob/main/projects/slides/stable_kalman.pdf",github.com,eess.SY,eess.SY math.NA math.OC math.RA electrical-engineering mathematics control-theory linear-algebra numerical-analysis lecture-notes slides github,null,2025,null,"Исследование способов улучшения стабильности методов калмановской фильтрации. Beamer slides, 2025; 21 pages, in Russian. Part of Numerical linear algebra course, AI Masters, Fall 2025. Slides cover Калмановская фильтрация, Extended Kalman Filtering (EKF) I, Extended Kalman Filtering (EKF) II, Гипотеза, Задачи, Улучшение 1 - Метод Джозефа, Улучшение 2 - Устойчивые методы вычисления S−1, Улучшение 3 - Корневая модификация I, Улучшение 3 - Корневая модификация II, Модель: движение объекта I, Модель: движение объекта II, and Модель: система наблюдений I."
  2707,"Conversions: Part 5","https://github.com/arnaud-m/algo-prog-R/blob/master/latex/05-conversions/05-conversions.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS computer-science algorithms lecture-notes survey slides github,Arnaud Malapert and Marie Pelleau,2025,null,"Conversions: Part 5. Beamer slides by Arnaud Malapert, and Marie Pelleau, 2025; 8 pages, in French. From a repository described as: This repository hosts the source files of the website and the lectures given in the course [[http://www.i3s.unice.fr/~malapert/R][Algorithmique & Programmation avec R]]. The course is an introduction to R programming targeted for beginners. Slides cover Épluchage d'un entier chiffre à chiffre, Épluchage récursif d'un entier, Épluchage binaire d'un entier, Variante : bit de poids fort, Épluchage d'un nombre fractionnaire, and Surprise ! Le calcul fractionnaire n'est pas exact !."
  2708,Nombres réels approchés,"https://github.com/arnaud-m/algo-prog-R/blob/master/latex/06-nombres-approches/06-nombres-approches.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS computer-science algorithms lecture-notes survey slides github,Arnaud Malapert and Marie Pelleau,2025,null,"Nombres réels approchés. Beamer slides by Arnaud Malapert, and Marie Pelleau, 2025; 16 pages, in French. From a repository described as: This repository hosts the source files of the website and the lectures given in the course [[http://www.i3s.unice.fr/~malapert/R][Algorithmique & Programmation avec R]]. The course is an introduction to R programming targeted for beginners. Subject (translated): algorithms and data structures. Sections: Annexe. Slides cover Nombres rationnels, Représentation des nombres réels, Égalité entre nombres flottants, Autres problèmes avec les nombres flottants, Exemple : approximation de $\\sqrt{r}$, Algorithme d'approximation de $\\sqrt{r}$, Programme d'approximation de $\\sqrt{r}$, Répartition de flottants 6 bits sur la droite réelle, Tableau des flottants 6 bits, and Quelques erreurs catastrophiques."
  2709,Chaînes de caractères,"https://github.com/arnaud-m/algo-prog-R/blob/master/latex/09-chaines/09-chaines.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS cs.PL computer-science algorithms programming-languages lecture-notes survey slides github,Arnaud Malapert and Marie Pelleau,2025,null,"Chaînes de caractères. Beamer slides by Arnaud Malapert, and Marie Pelleau, 2025; 20 pages, in French. From a repository described as: This repository hosts the source files of the website and the lectures given in the course [[http://www.i3s.unice.fr/~malapert/R][Algorithmique & Programmation avec R]]. The course is an introduction to R programming targeted for beginners. Subject (translated): programming languages. Sections: Annexe. Slides cover Les chaînes de caractères, Apostrophes et guillemets, Une chaîne est une suite de caractères, Création d'une chaîne, Extraction d'une tranche de sous-chaîne, Éclatement d’une chaîne, Expressions régulières, Autres méthodes sur des chaînes, Accumulation dans une chaîne de caractères, and Renverser un nombre dans une chaîne."
  2710,"Les séquences: vecteurs","https://github.com/arnaud-m/algo-prog-R/blob/master/latex/10-vecteurs/10-vecteurs.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS computer-science algorithms lecture-notes survey slides github,Arnaud Malapert and Marie Pelleau,2025,null,"Les séquences: vecteurs. Beamer slides by Arnaud Malapert, and Marie Pelleau, 2025; 24 pages, in French. From a repository described as: This repository hosts the source files of the website and the lectures given in the course [[http://www.i3s.unice.fr/~malapert/R][Algorithmique & Programmation avec R]]. The course is an introduction to R programming targeted for beginners. Slides cover Accès par rang aux éléments d'une séquence, Accès par contenu, Arithmétique des vecteurs, Construction d'une nouvelle séquence, Extraction d'une tranche de séquence, Pré-allocation de mémoire, Modification d'un vecteur, Conditions et tests vectorisés !, Recherche des bornes d'un vecteur, Recherche dans un vecteur : which, Recherche dans un vecteur : match, Fonctions all et any sur un vecteur logique, Tri d'un vecteur : sort, and Méthodes usuelles sur les vecteurs."
