  2713,Représentation des nombres,"https://github.com/arnaud-m/algo-prog-R/blob/master/latex/F1-nombres/F1-nombres.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS cs.PL computer-science algorithms programming-languages lecture-notes survey slides github,Arnaud Malapert,2025,null,"Représentation des nombres. Beamer slides by Arnaud Malapert, 2025; 46 pages, in French. From a repository described as: This repository hosts the source files of the website and the lectures given in the course [[http://www.i3s.unice.fr/~malapert/R][Algorithmique & Programmation avec R]]. The course is an introduction to R programming targeted for beginners. Subject (translated): algorithms and data structures; programming languages. Sections: Système positionnel; Multiplication et division égyptiennes; Arithmétique binaire; Représentation des nombres en machine. Subsections include Entiers naturels, and Nombres fractionnaires. Slides cover Cours en AUTOFORMATION, Table des matières, Utilisation d’une base b, Traduction vers la base 10, Traduction entre des puissances de 2, Exercices, Traduction vers une base quelquonque, Multiplication égyptienne : x × y, Division égyptienne : x ÷ y, and Division dont le résultat est fractionnaire."
  2714,"Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture 21: Unsupervised Learning I Hierarchical Agglomerative Clustering (HAC)","https://github.com/asifehmad/Machine-Learning-Lecture-Slides-ES-442/blob/main/03-Unsupervised-Learning/Lecture-21-Unsupervised-Learning-I-Hierarchical-Agglomerative-Clustering-%28HAC%29.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning lecture-notes survey slides github,Asif Ahmad,2025,null,"Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture 21: Unsupervised Learning I Hierarchical Agglomerative Clustering (HAC). Beamer lecture slides by Asif Ahmad, 2025; 18 pages. Part of Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture Slides: Instructor: Asif Ahmad Institution: Faculty of Engineering Sciences, GIK Institute Semester: Fall 2025. Sections: Introduction to Unsupervised Learning; Hierarchical Agglomerative Clustering (HAC); HAC Worked Example. Slides cover Recap: Supervised vs. Unsupervised Learning, What is Clustering?, Applications of Clustering, The Core of Clustering: Measuring Distance, Types of Clustering, How to Measure Cluster Distance? (Linkage Criteria), Visualizing Results: The Dendrogram, HAC Example: The Data, HAC Example: Steps 1 & 2, and HAC Example: Step 3."
