  2725,"Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture 32: Reinforcement Learning VIII Exploration Strategies","https://github.com/asifehmad/Machine-Learning-Lecture-Slides-ES-442/blob/main/04-Re-Inforcement-Learning/Lecture-32-Re-Inforcement-Learning-VIII-Exploration-Strategies.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning reinforcement-learning online-learning-and-bandits lecture-notes slides github,Asif Ahmad,2025,null,"Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture 32: Reinforcement Learning VIII Exploration Strategies. Beamer lecture slides by Asif Ahmad, 2025; 10 pages. Part of Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture Slides: Instructor: Asif Ahmad Institution: Faculty of Engineering Sciences, GIK Institute Semester: Fall 2025. Sections: The Exploration-Exploitation Trade-off; Strategy 1: -Greedy; Strategy 2: Softmax (Boltzmann); Strategy 3: Upper Confidence Bound (UCB); Decaying Schedules. Slides cover The Fundamental Dilemma, Example: The Multi-Armed Bandit, ε-Greedy Exploration, Softmax Exploration, Optimism in the Face of Uncertainty, From Exploration to Exploitation, and Summary of Exploration."
  2726,"Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture 33: Reinforcement Learning IX Function Approximation","https://github.com/asifehmad/Machine-Learning-Lecture-Slides-ES-442/blob/main/04-Re-Inforcement-Learning/Lecture-33-Re-Inforcement-Learning-IX-Function-Approximation.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning reinforcement-learning lecture-notes slides github,Asif Ahmad,2025,null,"Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture 33: Reinforcement Learning IX Function Approximation. Beamer lecture slides by Asif Ahmad, 2025; 10 pages. Part of Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture Slides: Instructor: Asif Ahmad Institution: Faculty of Engineering Sciences, GIK Institute Semester: Fall 2025. Sections: The Limits of Tabular RL; Linear Function Approximation; The Substitution Challenge; Feature Construction; Stability Issues. Slides cover The Problem with Tables, Solution: Function Approximation, Linear Methods, Gradient Descent Updates, The Target Value U, Designing Features, and The Deadly Triad."
  2727,"Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture 34: Reinforcement Learning X Deep Reinforcement Learning (DQN)","https://github.com/asifehmad/Machine-Learning-Lecture-Slides-ES-442/blob/main/04-Re-Inforcement-Learning/Lecture-34-Re-Inforcement-Learning-X-Deep-Reinforcement-Learning-%28DQN%29.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning reinforcement-learning algorithms lecture-notes slides github,Asif Ahmad,2025,null,"Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture 34: Reinforcement Learning X Deep Reinforcement Learning (DQN). Beamer lecture slides by Asif Ahmad, 2025; 10 pages. Part of Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture Slides: Instructor: Asif Ahmad Institution: Faculty of Engineering Sciences, GIK Institute Semester: Fall 2025. Sections: From Q-Learning to Deep Q-Learning; Stabilizing Deep RL; The DQN Algorithm; Applications and Success Stories. Slides cover Recap: Function Approximation, The DQN Architecture, Innovation 1: Experience Replay, Innovation 2: Target Networks, The Deep Q-Network Algorithm, DQN Success: Atari Games, and Summary of Deep Q-Learning."
  2728,"Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture 35: Reinforcement Learning XI Policy Gradient Methods: REINFORCE & Actor-Critic","https://github.com/asifehmad/Machine-Learning-Lecture-Slides-ES-442/blob/main/04-Re-Inforcement-Learning/Lecture-35-Re-Inforcement-Learning-XI-Policy-Gradient-Methods-REINFORCE-And-Actor-Critic.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG cs.AI computer-science reinforcement-learning machine-learning optimization algorithms lecture-notes slides github,Asif Ahmad,2025,null,"Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture 35: Reinforcement Learning XI Policy Gradient Methods: REINFORCE & Actor-Critic. Beamer lecture slides by Asif Ahmad, 2025; 11 pages. Part of Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture Slides: Instructor: Asif Ahmad Institution: Faculty of Engineering Sciences, GIK Institute Semester: Fall 2025. Sections: Value-Based vs. Policy-Based RL; The Policy Gradient Theorem; The REINFORCE Algorithm; Actor-Critic Methods. Slides cover Two Approaches to RL, Advantages of Policy Gradients, Optimizing the Policy, REINFORCE (Monte Carlo Policy Gradient), Reducing Variance with a Critic, Actor-Critic Architecture, Why Actor-Critic Works, and Method Mechanism Key Feature."
  2729,"Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture 36: Reinforcement Learning XII Case Studies & Applications","https://github.com/asifehmad/Machine-Learning-Lecture-Slides-ES-442/blob/main/04-Re-Inforcement-Learning/Lecture-36-Re-Inforcement-Learning-XII-Case-Studies-And-Applications.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML cs.AI computer-science statistics machine-learning reinforcement-learning robotics ai-agents lecture-notes slides github,Asif Ahmad,2025,null,"Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture 36: Reinforcement Learning XII Case Studies & Applications. Beamer lecture slides by Asif Ahmad, 2025; 12 pages. Part of Machine Learning (ES-442) - Lecture Slides: Instructor: Asif Ahmad Institution: Faculty of Engineering Sciences, GIK Institute Semester: Fall 2025. Sections: Case Study 1: AlphaGo; Case Study 2: Robotics; Case Study 3: Autonomous Driving; Case Study 4: Recommender Systems; Course Conclusion. Slides cover From Theory to Practice, The Challenge of Go, AlphaGo Architecture, The Result: Move 37, Robotics Control, Sim-to-Real Transfer, RL in Self-Driving Cars, Beyond ”Click-Through Rate”, and Course Wrap-Up."
  2730,"From Diffusion to Flow: Principles and Scientific Applications of Modern Generative Models","https://github.com/cam1681/CS25_Large_Foundation_model/blob/main/lectures/source/compiled_pdfs/class_pku.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML math.CO math.PR computer-science statistics mathematics machine-learning graph-theory probability computational-biology slides github,Pipi Hu,2025,null,"From Diffusion to Flow: Principles and Scientific Applications of Modern Generative Models. Beamer lecture slides by Pipi Hu, 2025; 69 pages. From a repository described as: 从数学走近生成式人工智能。本课程围绕大基础模型,介绍概率建模、训练算法、生成过程及其计算实现,并讨论世界模型、强化学习、推理、智能体和科学应用。. Sections: Understand diffusion models from a mathematical viewpoint; Flow Matching: Learning Probability Flows; Applications in AI for Science: From Sequence to structure prediction. Subsections include Score Matching: From Explicit Score Matching to Denoising Score Matching, Unified View: Score, x0, and Epsilon Models, Potential Score Matching, Diffusion Models: SMLD and DDPM, Continuous-Time Formulation, Probability Path and Coupling, Unified Interpretation: Diffusion and Flow Matching, Conditional Paths and Velocity Targets, and Flow Matching Training and Inference. Slides cover Feynman’s words, Molecular Dynamics (MD) is one kind of special sampling methods, Denoising Score Matching, Another insight: from the definition of the score S, Key Identity: Jacobian Switch (chain rule between x0 and xt), Experiments on first 1, 000 frames for LJ data, SMLD, The continuous version of SMLD, Training recipe, and Weak Form from Random Trajectories."
  2731,Large Foundation Models and Reasoning,"https://github.com/cam1681/CS25_Large_Foundation_model/blob/main/lectures/source/compiled_pdfs/lecture10_reasoning.pdf",github.com,math.LO,math.LO cs.CL cs.AI cs.LG mathematics computer-science mathematical-logic large-language-models survey slides github,Pipi Hu,2025,null,"Large Foundation Models and Reasoning. Beamer lecture slides by Pipi Hu, 2025; 31 pages. From a repository described as: 从数学走近生成式人工智能。本课程围绕大基础模型,介绍概率建模、训练算法、生成过程及其计算实现,并讨论世界模型、强化学习、推理、智能体和科学应用。. Sections: Introduction to Reasoning in Large Foundation Models; Chain-of-Thought Reasoning; Mathematical Reasoning; Logical Reasoning; Advanced Reasoning Techniques; Reasoning Evaluation; Future Directions. Slides cover Turing’s words, What is Reasoning?, Mathematical Formulation of CoT, Formal Mathematical Reasoning, First-Order Logic Reasoning, Self-Consistency, Reasoning Error Analysis, and Challenges in Reasoning."
  2732,"Agent Technologies in Large Language Models: Intelligent Systems Beyond Traditional AI","https://github.com/cam1681/CS25_Large_Foundation_model/blob/main/lectures/source/compiled_pdfs/lecture11_agent.pdf",github.com,cs.AI,cs.AI cs.CL cs.LG cs.MA computer-science ai-agents large-language-models real-analysis slides github,Pipi Hu,2025,null,"Agent Technologies in Large Language Models: Intelligent Systems Beyond Traditional AI. Beamer lecture slides by Pipi Hu, 2025; 44 pages. From a repository described as: 从数学走近生成式人工智能。本课程围绕大基础模型,介绍概率建模、训练算法、生成过程及其计算实现,并讨论世界模型、强化学习、推理、智能体和科学应用。. Sections: Introduction: LLM Agents vs Traditional AI; Mathematical Foundations of LLM Agents; LLM Agent Architectures; Multi-LLM Agent Systems; Tool Integration in LLM Agents; Reasoning and Planning in LLM Agents; Memory and Context in LLM Agents; LLM Agent Applications; Evaluation of LLM Agents; Challenges and Future Directions; Implementation Considerations. Slides cover The Evolution of AI Agents, What are LLM Agents?, LLM Agent Architecture, LLM Agent Prompt Engineering, LLM Agent Processing Pipeline, and LLM Agent Collaboration Patterns."
  2733,"AI for Science: Bridging Machine Learning and Scientific Discovery","https://github.com/cam1681/CS25_Large_Foundation_model/blob/main/lectures/source/compiled_pdfs/lecture12_ai4science.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML hep-th math-ph computer-science statistics physics machine-learning bioinformatics computational-biology mathematical-physics slides github,Pipi Hu,2025,null,"AI for Science: Bridging Machine Learning and Scientific Discovery. Beamer lecture slides by Pipi Hu, 2025; 65 pages. From a repository described as: 从数学走近生成式人工智能。本课程围绕大基础模型,介绍概率建模、训练算法、生成过程及其计算实现,并讨论世界模型、强化学习、推理、智能体和科学应用。. Sections: Introduction: AI for Science; Physics-Informed Neural Networks (PINNs); Molecular Property Prediction; Climate and Environmental Modeling; Protein Folding and Structure Prediction; Materials Discovery; Scientific Computing and Simulation; Challenges and Future Directions; Selected papers. Slides cover Feynman’s words, What is AI for Science?, Example: Solving PDEs with PINNs, Tangent Space on the Stiefel Manifold, Conceptual Summary, Applications in Drug Discovery, Climate Change Detection, Crystal Structure Representation, Neural Operators, and Future Directions."
  2734,Understanding Flow Matching from a mathematical view,"https://github.com/cam1681/CS25_Large_Foundation_model/blob/main/lectures/source/compiled_pdfs/lecture2_Flow_matching.pdf",github.com,math.CO,math.CO cs.LG math.PR mathematics computer-science graph-theory machine-learning probability ode-and-dynamical-systems slides github,Pipi Hu,2025,null,"Understanding Flow Matching from a mathematical view. Beamer lecture slides by Pipi Hu, 2025; 41 pages. From a repository described as: 从数学走近生成式人工智能。本课程围绕大基础模型,介绍概率建模、训练算法、生成过程及其计算实现,并讨论世界模型、强化学习、推理、智能体和科学应用。. Sections: Mathematical motivation for Flow Matching; Connection with Diffusion Models; Conditional Paths and Velocity Targets; Flow Matching Training and Inference; Advanced Topics and Extensions; MeanFlow: Single-Step Generation; Summary and Future Directions. Slides cover Probability Path and Coupling, Weak Form from Random Trajectories, Practical Training Recipe (Per-Iteration), Isotropic diffusion: σ(x, t) = σ(t) IN, Mathematical derivation: probability flow ODE, Mathematical analysis of path choices, Mathematical foundation of inference, Conditional Flow Matching, Flow Matching in Latent Spaces, and MeanFlow: Motivation."
  2735,Understanding Variational Autoencoders from a mathematical view,"https://github.com/cam1681/CS25_Large_Foundation_model/blob/main/lectures/source/compiled_pdfs/lecture3_vae.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning quantum-field-theory slides github,Pipi Hu,2025,null,"Understanding Variational Autoencoders from a mathematical view. Beamer lecture slides by Pipi Hu, 2025; 36 pages. From a repository described as: 从数学走近生成式人工智能。本课程围绕大基础模型,介绍概率建模、训练算法、生成过程及其计算实现,并讨论世界模型、强化学习、推理、智能体和科学应用。. Sections: Introduction: The Problem of Generative Modeling; Variational Inference: The Foundation; VAE Variants and Extensions; Advanced Topics; Practical Considerations. Slides cover Feynman’s words, The Low-Dimensional Manifold Hypothesis, From Deterministic to Probabilistic: Variational Autoencoders, Latent Variable Generative Models, Variational Inference and the ELBO (Pointwise in x), Summarize VAE from the generative perspective, The VAE Architecture, Dataset Objective and Training, Analytical KL Divergence, and VQ-VAE: Vector Quantized VAE."
  2736,Understanding normalizing flows from a mathematical view,"https://github.com/cam1681/CS25_Large_Foundation_model/blob/main/lectures/source/compiled_pdfs/lecture4_normalizing_flow.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning curves large-language-models ode-and-dynamical-systems slides github,Pipi Hu,2025,null,"Understanding normalizing flows from a mathematical view. Beamer lecture slides by Pipi Hu, 2025; 47 pages. From a repository described as: 从数学走近生成式人工智能。本课程围绕大基础模型,介绍概率建模、训练算法、生成过程及其计算实现,并讨论世界模型、强化学习、推理、智能体和科学应用。. Sections: Introduction: Normalizing Flows in the Generative Modeling Landscape; Preliminary: Change of Variables and Jacobian; Autoregressive Flows; Coupling Layers; Continuous Normalizing Flows; CNFs: Conditional Normalizing Flows; Training and Applications; Comparison with Other Methods; Challenges and Future Directions. Slides cover Feynman’s words, Three perspectives so far, Proof of the Change of Variables Formula (Part 2), Autoregressive Transformations, TarFlow: Transformer-based Autoregressive Flow, TarFlow: Training Objective and Loss, TarFlow: Training for Conditional Generation, Real NVP: Real-valued Non-volume Preserving, Proof of Neural ODE Change of Variables Formula, and FFJORD: Free-form Jacobian of Reversible Dynamics."
  2737,Understanding Generative Adversarial Networks from a mathematical view,"https://github.com/cam1681/CS25_Large_Foundation_model/blob/main/lectures/source/compiled_pdfs/lecture5_GANs.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning optimization quantum-field-theory slides github,Pipi Hu,2025,null,"Understanding Generative Adversarial Networks from a mathematical view. Beamer lecture slides by Pipi Hu, 2025; 42 pages. From a repository described as: 从数学走近生成式人工智能。本课程围绕大基础模型,介绍概率建模、训练算法、生成过程及其计算实现,并讨论世界模型、强化学习、推理、智能体和科学应用。. Sections: Preliminary: Generative Modeling and Adversarial Training; Theoretical Foundations: Minimax Game and Nash Equilibrium; Loss Functions and Training Objectives; WGAN; GAN Architectures and Design Principles; Training Challenges and Solutions; Evaluation Metrics and Methods; The GAN is dead; long live the GAN! A Modern Baseline GAN (R3GAN); Open Questions and Future Research. Slides cover Feynman’s words, The Generative Modeling Problem, The Minimax Game Formulation, WGAN: What goes wrong with vanilla GANs?, WGAN: Optimization problem, StyleGAN: Style-Based Generator, Solutions to Training Problems, Qualitative Evaluation Methods, Why RpGAN helps: relative scoring removes bad minima, and Putting it together: the R3GAN objective & loop."
  2738,Understanding autoregressive models from a mathematical view,"https://github.com/cam1681/CS25_Large_Foundation_model/blob/main/lectures/source/compiled_pdfs/lecture6_autoregressive.pdf",github.com,cs.CL,cs.CL cs.LG cs.AI math.RA computer-science mathematics large-language-models linear-algebra machine-learning quantum-field-theory slides github,Pipi Hu,2025,null,"Understanding autoregressive models from a mathematical view. Beamer lecture slides by Pipi Hu, 2025; 77 pages. From a repository described as: 从数学走近生成式人工智能。本课程围绕大基础模型,介绍概率建模、训练算法、生成过程及其计算实现,并讨论世界模型、强化学习、推理、智能体和科学应用。. Sections: Preliminary: Autoregressive Models and Sequential Generation; Training Autoregressive Models: Maximum Likelihood; Architectures for Autoregressive Models; Rotational Positional Encoding (RoPE); Sampling and Generation Strategies; Evaluation and Challenges; Open Questions and Research Directions. Slides cover Feynman’s words, What are autoregressive models?, Cross-entropy loss and its interpretation, Multi-Head Attention (MHA), Matrix Multiplication: Row Picture, Attention Construction: Alignment & Masking, Attention Mechanism: Linear Combination of Values, Training Objective: From Token Matrix to MLE Loss, Linear and Kernelized Attention as Operator Approximation, and Idea of RoPE."
  2739,Understanding World Models in Machine Learning and AGI,"https://github.com/cam1681/CS25_Large_Foundation_model/blob/main/lectures/source/compiled_pdfs/lecture8_world_model.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning quantum-field-theory reinforcement-learning slides github,Pipi Hu,2025,null,"Understanding World Models in Machine Learning and AGI. Beamer lecture slides by Pipi Hu, 2025; 38 pages. From a repository described as: 从数学走近生成式人工智能。本课程围绕大基础模型,介绍概率建模、训练算法、生成过程及其计算实现,并讨论世界模型、强化学习、推理、智能体和科学应用。. Sections: Introduction: What are World Models?; Mathematical Foundations of World Models; World Models in Reinforcement Learning; World Models for AGI; Advanced World Model Architectures; Challenges and Future Directions; Applications and Case Studies; Theoretical Foundations; Implementation Considerations; Conclusion and Future Work. Slides cover Feynman’s words, The Concept of World Models, The World Model Learning Problem, Planning with World Models, Hierarchical World Models, Diffusion World Models, Current Challenges in World Models, and World Models in Game AI."
  2740,1cm Causal Inference (overview),"https://github.com/cfgranda/ps4ds/blob/main/slides/causal_inference_overview.pdf",github.com,math.PR,math.PR math.ST stat.ME mathematics statistics probability survey book slides problem-list video github,null,2025,null,"1cm Causal Inference (overview). Beamer slides, 2025; 146 pages. Part of Code repository for Probability and Statistics for Data Science: Code for the book Probability and Statistics for Data Science. A free preprint, videos, code, slides and solutions to exercises are available at https://www.ps4ds.net. Sections: Potential outcomes; Confounding factors; Adjusting for confounders. Slides cover Key question, New drug, Probabilistic modeling, Grades in a Portuguese school, Unemployment in Spain, Fundamental problem of causal inference, Independence is essential, Binary outcome / treatment, 3-point shooting, and Nonbinary outcome nonbinary treatment."
  2741,1cm The Curse of Dimensionality and Naive Bayes,"https://github.com/cfgranda/ps4ds/blob/main/slides/multiple%20discrete%20variables/naive_bayes.pdf",github.com,math.PR,math.PR math.ST stat.ME mathematics statistics probability book slides problem-list video github,null,2025,null,"1cm The Curse of Dimensionality and Naive Bayes. Beamer slides, 2025; 17 pages. Part of Code repository for Probability and Statistics for Data Science: Code for the book Probability and Statistics for Data Science. A free preprint, videos, code, slides and solutions to exercises are available at https://www.ps4ds.net. Slides cover These slides are based on the book Probability and Statistics for Data, Precipitation in Oregon, Empirical joint pmf (%), What if we have 134 stations?, US weather dataset, Possible solution, Classification, Probabilistic modeling, Predicting political affiliation, Probabilistic model, Naive assumption, Bayes rule, Model, and Applying the model."
