  2760,Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning - Introduction,"https://github.com/marl-book/slides/blob/main/marl-book-ch1-ch2-intro-rl.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG cs.AI cs.MA cs.SE computer-science ai-agents machine-learning reinforcement-learning book slides github,Stefano V. Albrecht and Filippos Christianos and Lukas Schäfer,2025,null,"Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning - Introduction. Beamer slides by Stefano V. Albrecht, Filippos Christianos, and Lukas Schäfer, 2025; 59 pages. Part of Slides for MIT Press textbook \"Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning: Foundations and Modern Approaches\": This repository contains slides for the MIT Press textbook \"Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning: Foundations and Modern Approaches\" by Stefano V. Albrecht, Filippos Christianos, and Lukas Schäfer. Sections: Part 1: Introduction; Part 2: Reinforcement Learning Basics. Slides cover The MARL Book, Lecture Outline, Mutli-Agent Systems, Why MARL?, Challenges of MARL, Challenges of Multi-Agent Learning, What is Reinforcement Learning?, MDP Assumptions, Mars Rover MDP Example, and State-Value Functions."
  2761,"Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning - Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning in Games: First Steps and Challenges: Marl Book Ch5 Marl in Games","https://github.com/marl-book/slides/blob/main/source/marl-book-ch5-marl-in-games.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG cs.AI cs.MA cs.SE computer-science ai-agents reinforcement-learning machine-learning real-analysis book slides github,Stefano V. Albrecht and Filippos Christianos,2025,null,"Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning - Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning in Games: First Steps and Challenges: Marl Book Ch5 Marl in Games. Beamer slides by Stefano V. Albrecht, and Filippos Christianos, 2025; 45 pages. Part of Slides for MIT Press textbook \"Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning: Foundations and Modern Approaches\": This repository contains slides for the MIT Press textbook \"Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning: Foundations and Modern Approaches\" by Stefano V. Albrecht, Filippos Christianos, and Lukas Schäfer. Sections: MARL Learning Framework; Central Learning; Independent Learning; MARL Challenges. Slides cover MARL Learning Process, Inputs of Policies Depend on Game Model, Convergence, Single-Agent RL Reductions, Central Q-Learning, Independent Q-learning, IQL and CQL in Level-Based Foraging, Modes of Operation in MARL, Non-Stationarity, and Non-Stationarity in Multi-Agent Settings."
  2762,"Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning - Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning: Foundational Algorithms: Marl Book Ch6 Marl Algorithms","https://github.com/marl-book/slides/blob/main/source/marl-book-ch6-marl-algorithms.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG cs.AI cs.DS cs.MA computer-science ai-agents algorithms machine-learning reinforcement-learning book slides github,Stefano V. Albrecht and Filippos Christianos and Lukas Schäfer,2025,null,"Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning - Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning: Foundational Algorithms: Marl Book Ch6 Marl Algorithms. Beamer slides by Stefano V. Albrecht, Filippos Christianos, and Lukas Schäfer, 2025; 68 pages. Part of Slides for MIT Press textbook \"Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning: Foundations and Modern Approaches\": This repository contains slides for the MIT Press textbook \"Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning: Foundations and Modern Approaches\" by Stefano V. Albrecht, Filippos Christianos, and Lukas Schäfer. Slides cover Dynamic Programming for Games: Value Iteration, Value Iteration Pseudocode, Obtaining Minimax Policies for the Stochastic Game, From Dynamic Programming to Temporal-Difference Learning, Temporal-Difference Learning for Games: Joint-Action Learning, Joint-Action Learning with Game Theory, JAL-GT Pseudocode, Minimax-Q, Nash-Q, CE-Q, Example: Minimax-Q in Grid Soccer (Littman, 1994), Agent Modeling & Best Response, Agent Modeling, Policy Reconstruction & Best Response, Fictitious Play, and Fictitious Play Convergence."
