  2766,Visualizing and Quantifying Eigenvalues of –Hermite ensemble in Julia,"https://github.com/mitmath/18338/blob/master/projects/2025/yu_rosen_visualizing_hermite_ensemble/yurosen_155367_5943043_18338_Final_Project_presentation-1.pdf",github.com,math.RA,math.RA math.NA math.PR math.ST mathematics linear-algebra random-matrix-theory statistics algorithms lecture-notes slides github,Rosen Yu,2025,null,"Visualizing and Quantifying Eigenvalues of –Hermite ensemble in Julia. Beamer slides by Rosen Yu, 2025; 20 pages. Part of 18.338: Eigenvalues of random matrices, Fall 2025: This is the repository for public materials for the MIT course 18.338, Eigenvalues of random matrices, for the Fall 2025 semester. Sections: Website: Strum Histogramming + Estimator; Quantifying ``Repulsiveness\". Slides cover Strum Histogramming + β Estimator, Compute Bottleneck with Histogramming, Solution: Sturm Sequences [Albrecht et al., 2009], From Determinants to Ratios, The “Shift” and The Histogram, Sturm Histogramming Algorithm, Algorihm Runtime Validation, β-Estimation via Wigner Surmise, What is ”Repulsiveness”?, and Literature that discussed quantifying DPP."
