  2768,14 重构生命之树,"https://github.com/wang-q/lecture-slides/blob/master/slides/ch-14.slides.pdf",github.com,q-bio.GN,q-bio.GN q-bio.QM quantitative-biology bioinformatics lecture-notes slides github,null,2025,null,"14 重构生命之树. Beamer slides, 2025; 37 pages, in Chinese. Part of Markdown to lecture slides: The slides directory contains slides for my course \"General Biology\". Sections: 14.1 演化理论赋予分类学新的目标; 14.2 系统发生树的构建; 14.3 单系类群, 并系类群和多系类群; 14.4 重建系统发生面临的挑战. Slides cover 14. 1演化理论赋予分类学新的目标, Figure 2. 自然的阶梯 (the ladder of nature), 精心挑选的特征, Figure 6. 树的结构, Figure 7. 维利・亨尼希 (Willi Hennig), 支序分类学之父, Figure 8. 同源相似性, Figure 10. 同功相似性, 游泳的动物, and 排除同功相似性 (趋同演化) 后, 所有可用的特征都是等价."
  2769,"GNU/Linux: Linux Intro - B","https://github.com/wx672/lecture-notes/blob/master/linux/linux_intro/linux_intro-b.pdf",github.com,cs.OS,cs.OS math.HO computer-science mathematics operating-systems economics-and-finance history-of-mathematics high-performance-computing book slides github,null,2025,null,"GNU/Linux: Linux Intro - B. Beamer slides, 2025; 27 pages. Sections: A Short History; Open Source; Facts; How to learn. Slides cover Desktop Market Share, OS Market Shares, What are clouds made of?, Supercomputer Top500, No Textbook, Homework, What’s GNU/Linux?, A Short History of GNU/Linux and Open Source, Meet The Parents, and How Is GNU/Linux?."
  2770,Network Basics,"https://github.com/wx672/lecture-notes/blob/master/network_basics/net-b.pdf",github.com,cs.NI,cs.NI math.AG computer-science mathematics networking stacks survey book slides github,Wang Xiaolin,2025,null,"Network Basics. Beamer slides by Wang Xiaolin, 2025; 195 pages. Sections: How The Internet Works; Transport Protocols; Application Layer Protocols. Subsections include What's A Computer Network?, Past and Future, The Internet, Network Classification, Basic Hardware Components, Network Architecture, TCP/IP Overview, Terminology, Ethernet, and ARP. Slides cover Textbooks, ó Homework, What’s A Computer Network?, Danger, TCP/IP Protocol Stack, ARP References, IP Route Table, Why Subnetting?, Two-Level vs. Multi-Level Network, and Simplification."
  2771,Operating Systems (wx672/lecture-notes),"https://github.com/wx672/lecture-notes/blob/master/os/slides/os-b.pdf",github.com,cs.OS,cs.OS computer-science operating-systems computer-architecture distributed-systems statistics book slides github,null,2025,null,"Operating Systems (wx672/lecture-notes). Beamer slides, 2025; 458 pages. Sections: Process And Thread; Memory Management; File Systems. Subsections include What's an Operating System, OS Services, Hardware, Bootstrapping, Interrupt, System Calls, Processes, Threads, Process Synchronization, and CPU Scheduling. Slides cover Textbooks, óHomework, Part I, Interrupt Timeline, Threads, Producer-Consumer Problem, Semaphores, Message Passing, Process Classification, and Four Conditions For Deadlocks."
  2772,"sysugreenDCS5718 最优化理论与方法: blue第一章: 凸集、凸函数与凸优化问题","https://github.com/ysyisyourbrother/SYSU_Notebook/blob/master/%E8%AF%BE%E7%A8%8B%E8%B5%84%E6%96%99/%E6%9C%80%E4%BC%98%E5%8C%96%E7%90%86%E8%AE%BA%E4%B8%8E%E6%96%B9%E6%B3%95-2025/opt_chapter1.pdf",github.com,math.OC,math.OC cs.LG mathematics computer-science optimization lecture-notes slides github,null,2025,null,"sysugreenDCS5718 最优化理论与方法: blue第一章: 凸集、凸函数与凸优化问题. Beamer lecture slides, 2025; 126 pages, in Chinese. From the course-materials archive ysyisyourbrother/SYSU_Notebook. Subject (translated): optimization. Sections: 基础知识; 凸函数; 凸优化问题. Slides cover 参考书目, 最优化简介, 最优化的发展简史, 梯度和海瑟矩阵, 优化中的一些基本概念, 凸集的例子, 凸集的保凸运算, 凸函数的扩展:重要例子, 重要的凸函数, and 保凸运算:逐点最大."
  2773,"sysugreenDCS5718 最优化理论与方法: blue第二章: 对偶理论","https://github.com/ysyisyourbrother/SYSU_Notebook/blob/master/%E8%AF%BE%E7%A8%8B%E8%B5%84%E6%96%99/%E6%9C%80%E4%BC%98%E5%8C%96%E7%90%86%E8%AE%BA%E4%B8%8E%E6%96%B9%E6%B3%95-2025/opt_chapter2.pdf",github.com,math.OC,math.OC cs.LG mathematics computer-science optimization lecture-notes slides github,null,2025,null,"sysugreenDCS5718 最优化理论与方法: blue第二章: 对偶理论. Beamer lecture slides, 2025; 76 pages, in Chinese. From the course-materials archive ysyisyourbrother/SYSU_Notebook. Subject (translated): optimization. Sections: Lagrange 函数与对偶函数; Lagrange 对偶问题; Lagrange 对偶的几种解释; 最优性条件; 敏感性分析(Perturbation Analysis); 利用对偶理解“启发式”方法. Slides cover 一般优化问题, 拉格朗日(Lagrange)函数, 对偶函数计算:线性约束的最小二乘问题, 对偶性的强弱, 例:线性约束的最小二乘问题, Slater’s condition 与强对偶性, 几何解释(续), 鞍点解释, 鞍点解释(续), and 最优性条件:研究最优解所要满足的条件。."
  2774,"sysugreenDCS5718 最优化理论与方法: blue第三章: 无约束优化算法","https://github.com/ysyisyourbrother/SYSU_Notebook/blob/master/%E8%AF%BE%E7%A8%8B%E8%B5%84%E6%96%99/%E6%9C%80%E4%BC%98%E5%8C%96%E7%90%86%E8%AE%BA%E4%B8%8E%E6%96%B9%E6%B3%95-2025/opt_chapter3.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS math.OC cs.LG computer-science mathematics algorithms optimization lecture-notes slides github,null,2025,null,"sysugreenDCS5718 最优化理论与方法: blue第三章: 无约束优化算法. Beamer lecture slides, 2025; 78 pages, in Chinese. From the course-materials archive ysyisyourbrother/SYSU_Notebook. Subject (translated): algorithms and data structures; optimization. Sections: 线搜索; 梯度类算法; 梯度下降法的扩展; 牛顿类算法. Slides cover 在本章,我们将从连续可微无约束优化问题出发,认识并学习优化算法。, 回顾(大多数)迭代算法的基本框架, 非精确线搜索:Armijo rule, Grippo 准则, 基于线搜索的算法收敛性, 梯度利普希茨连续, 分析固定步长的梯度下降法, 坐标下降法, 邻近梯度法, and Nesterov 第一加速方法."
  2775,"sysugreen DCS5718 最优化理论与方法: blue第四章: 约束优化算法","https://github.com/ysyisyourbrother/SYSU_Notebook/blob/master/%E8%AF%BE%E7%A8%8B%E8%B5%84%E6%96%99/%E6%9C%80%E4%BC%98%E5%8C%96%E7%90%86%E8%AE%BA%E4%B8%8E%E6%96%B9%E6%B3%95-2025/opt_chapter4.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS math.OC cs.LG computer-science mathematics algorithms optimization lecture-notes slides github,null,2025,null,"sysugreen DCS5718 最优化理论与方法: blue第四章: 约束优化算法. Beamer lecture slides, 2025; 67 pages, in Chinese. From the course-materials archive ysyisyourbrother/SYSU_Notebook. Subject (translated): optimization; algorithms and data structures. Sections: 罚函数法; 增广拉格朗日乘子法; 交替方向乘子法; 分布式优化简介; 扩展:线性规划内点法简介; 扩展:对偶算法在最优传输上的应用. Slides cover 约束优化问题, 等式约束优化问题, 二次罚函数法的局限, ALM 的构造思想, 案例:基追踪问题, 一般约束问题的ALM, 与邻近点算法的联系, 问题背景, 交替方向乘子法(ADMM), and 求解LASSO 原问题."
  2776,"sysugreen DCS5718 最优化理论与方法: blue第五章: 随机梯度法及其变形","https://github.com/ysyisyourbrother/SYSU_Notebook/blob/master/%E8%AF%BE%E7%A8%8B%E8%B5%84%E6%96%99/%E6%9C%80%E4%BC%98%E5%8C%96%E7%90%86%E8%AE%BA%E4%B8%8E%E6%96%B9%E6%B3%95-2025/opt_chapter5.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS math.OC cs.LG computer-science mathematics algorithms optimization lecture-notes slides github,null,2025,null,"sysugreen DCS5718 最优化理论与方法: blue第五章: 随机梯度法及其变形. Beamer lecture slides, 2025; 39 pages, in Chinese. From the course-materials archive ysyisyourbrother/SYSU_Notebook. Subject (translated): optimization; algorithms and data structures. Sections: 问题背景; 随机梯度法; 随机梯度法的变形; 应用举例; 收敛性分析; 方差减小技术. Slides cover 有限和形式优化问题, 实际计算时,样本的选取方式可以灵活多样,可完全随机抽取,也可以每一, 动量方法, Nesterov 加速算法, AdaGrad 算法, AdaDelta 算法, 线性最小二乘回归, 一般凸函数下SGD的收敛性, and 可微强凸函数下SGD 的收敛性."
  2777,"ВведениевС++: Лекция1","https://gitlab.com/Wanaphi/cs-cpp-lectures-2025-2026/-/blob/main/lectures/presentations/00_basics.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.PL,cs.PL computer-science programming-languages slides gitlab,null,2025,null,"ВведениевС++: Лекция1. Beamer lecture slides, 2025; 120 pages, in Russian. Part of Курс С++ МФТИ ИВТ 2025-2026: Правила курса - Разбалловка и дедлайны - Дополнительные семинары. Subject (translated): programming languages and compilers. Sections: История; Терминология; Первая программа; Пространства имен; Алиасы; Ссылки; Динамическая память; Функции; Преобразования. Slides cover BjarneStroustrup, Немноготерминологии, Пространстваимен, АлиасытиповвС++, СсылкивС++, Ссылкивдругимитипами, Висячиессылки, ПараметрыпоумолчаниювС, Перегрузкифункций, and Тонкостиперегрузок."
  2778,Oxygen production from dissociation of Europa’s water-ice surface,"https://gitlab.com/aqfort-s/msu/english/-/blob/main/presentation-1/presentation.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.CL,cs.CL physics.flu-dyn cs.AI cs.LG computer-science physics aerospace-engineering large-language-models survey slides gitlab,Rinat Valiev,2025,null,"Oxygen production from dissociation of Europa’s water-ice surface. Beamer slides by Rinat Valiev (Moscow State University), 2025; 10 pages. Sections: Europa's structure; Overview of Europa fly-by and plasma observations. Subsections include PUI and O 2 generation, Relevant parameters derived from Juno data, and Jupiter Icy Moon Explorer. Slides cover Europa's picture, PUI and O 2 generation, Relevant parameters derived from Juno data, Jupiter Icy Moon Explorer - JUICE spacecraft, and Thank you for your attention."
  2779,Feasibility of keeping Mars warm with nanoparticles,"https://gitlab.com/aqfort-s/msu/english/-/blob/main/presentation-2/presentation.pdf",gitlab.com,math.AG,math.AG math.CT math.FA mathematics condensed-mathematics slides gitlab,Rinat Valiev,2025,null,"Feasibility of keeping Mars warm with nanoparticles. Beamer slides by Rinat Valiev (Moscow State University), 2025; 16 pages. Sections: Current Mars; Challenge; Solution. Subsections include Too cold for liquid water (avg. 202K), Existing methods (greenhouse gases) require rare resources (e.g., fluorine), and Engineered nanoparticles to trap heat efficiently. Slides cover Key Problem, Greenhouse Effect, Proposed Solution, Climate Modeling Results, Annual Average Temperatures (K) Control Simulation Without Nanorods, Annual Average Temperatures (K) Control Simulation With Nanorods, Benefits & Feasibility, Fe & Al Comparison, Orientation dependence of the optical properties of a 9 -long, $\\sim60:1$, and Challenges & Uncertainties."
  2780,Lecture 01 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2025-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-01.pdf",gitlab.com,math.LO,math.LO mathematics mathematical-logic lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2025,null,"Lecture 01 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2025; 67 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2025-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: dm 0.2 Mathematical Statements. Subsections include Atomic and Molecular Statements, Implications, Converses and Contrapositives, Necessity and Sufficiency, and Predicates and Quantifiers. Slides cover Assignments1, Why should I care about logic?, Statements, Examples of Non-statements, Logic Connectives, Implications, True or False?, Implication Does Not Mean Causality, Contrapositives, and Necessity and Sufficiency."
  2781,Lecture 03 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2025-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-03.pdf",gitlab.com,math.LO,math.LO cs.PL math.PR mathematics computer-science mathematical-logic programming-languages random-matrix-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2025,null,"Lecture 03 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2025; 67 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2025-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: dm 3.1 Propositional Logic. Subsections include Truth Tables, Xor — Exclusive-or, Logical Equivalence, Deductions — How to argue with logic, and Beyond Propositions. Slides cover Assignments1, The Game of Monopoly, Truth Tables, Logic and Modern Compiler, Knights and Knaves Puzzles, Solving the Puzzle with a Truth Table, Wooclap, Exercise, Example — Snow and Rain, and Example 3.1.4 — Negation of an Implication."
  2782,Lecture 04 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2025-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-04.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.HO math.NT physics.hist-ph mathematics physics combinatorics number-theory philosophy-of-mathematics lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2025,null,"Lecture 04 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2025; 69 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2025-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: dm 3.2 Proofs. Subsections include What Is a Mathematical Proof?, Direct Proof, Proof by Contrapositive, Proof by Contradiction, Proof by (Counter) Example, Proof by Cases, and Proof of If and Only if. Slides cover Assignments1, What Is a Mathematical Proof?, Theorem 3.2.1 — The Infinity of Primes, Euclid’s Proof, Direct Proof, Proof by Contrapositive, Prove by contrapositive that for all integers aand b, if a+ bis, Proof by contradiction, The Pigeonhole Principle: If more than nfly into npigeon, and A Special Case of Proof by Contradiction."
  2783,Lecture 06 — Test of Convergence - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2025-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-06.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA mathematics real-analysis lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2025,null,"Lecture 06 — Test of Convergence - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2025; 59 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2025-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ec 9.2 Test of Convergence. Subsections include Sequences Differ in Finitely Many Places, Monotone Bounded Test (for Sequences), Comparison Test (for Sequences), n-th Term Test (for Series), and Ratio Test (for Series). Slides cover Assignments1, Does it Converge?, Make a Guess, Impact of Finite Changes on Limits, Example: Bounded Sequence, Bounded Sequence, Convergence and Boundedness, Monotone Sequence, Monotone Bounded Test, and Monotone Bounded Test (Compact Form)."
  2784,Lecture 07 — Alternating Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2025-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-07.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA mathematics real-analysis lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2025,null,"Lecture 07 — Alternating Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2025; 63 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2025-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ec 9.2 Test of Convergence (Continued); ec 9.3 Alternating Series. Subsections include Integral Test (for Series), p-series Test (for Series), Comparison Test (for Series), Limit Comparison Test (for Series), Telescope Series Test (for Series), Properties of Convergent Series, Alternative Series Test, and Absolute and Conditional Convergence. Slides cover Assignments1, Proof of Integral Test: Divergent Case, Proof of Integral Test: Convergent Case, Example 9.10, Comparison Test (for Series), Example 9.11, Limit Comparison Test, Telescope, Partial Fraction Decomposition, and Alternating Series."
  2785,Lecture 08 — Power Series and Taylor Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2025-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-08.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA mathematics real-analysis lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2025,null,"Lecture 08 — Power Series and Taylor Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2025; 68 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2025-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ec 9.4 Power Series; ec 9.5 Taylor Series. Subsections include Interval of Convergence, Differentiation and Integration, Taylor's Formula, and Approximate a Function. Slides cover Assignments1, Cheating ?, Power Series, Interval of Convergence, Example 9.16, Differentiation and Integration, Example 9.19, Taylor’s Formula, Example 9.25, and Review: Big-ONotation."
  2786,"Lecture 09— Strings, Sets, and Binomial Coefficients (1) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01)","https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2025-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-09.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.RT math.RA mathematics combinatorics quiver-representations lecture-notes survey slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2025,null,"Lecture 09— Strings, Sets, and Binomial Coefficients (1) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2025; 51 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2025-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 1 An Introduction to Combinatorics; ac 2 Strings, Sets, and Binomial Coefficients. Subsections include 2.1 Strings, 2.2 Permutations, and 2.3 Combinations. Slides cover Assignments1, Applications in Computer Science, Strings, Examples of Strings, Example: My Breakfast, An Ancient Chinese Combinatorial Problem, Example: My lunch, Strings with Restrictions, Good and Bad Password, and Letters From a Bag."
  2787,"Lecture 10— Strings, Sets, and Binomial Coefficients (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01)","https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2025-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-10.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2025,null,"Lecture 10— Strings, Sets, and Binomial Coefficients (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2025; 57 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2025-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 2.4 Combinatorial Proofs; ac 2.5 The Ubiquitous Nature of Binomial Coefficients. Subsections include Summation formulas, Combinatorial Identities, and Integer Composition. Slides cover Assignments1, Combinatorial Identities, Example 2.19, Exercise: Combinatorial Identities, The Argument, The General Formula, When Are Allowed to Be Empty-handed, When There Are a Bit More, Counting with Bijection, and Inverse Function and Bijection."
  2788,Lecture 12 — Induction - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2025-01/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-12.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2025,null,"Lecture 12 — Induction - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2025-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2025; 69 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2025-01): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 3.4 Binomial Coefficients Revisited; ac 3.5 Solving Combinatorial Problems Recursively; ac 3.8 Proof by Induction. Subsections include A Game of, Tiling a Grid, Ternary Strings, What Is Induction, Example Proofs by Induction, A More Interesting Example of Induction, and Strong Induction. Slides cover Assignments1, An Experiment, Example 3.3: The Proof, A Recursive Formula, Exercise, Example 3.6: Ternary String, Example 3.6: The Recursive Formula, How Dominoes Fall, Proof by Induction, and A More Interesting Example of Induction."
