  2827,"The random-to-random shuffles and their $q$-deformations: Alcove2025","https://gitlab.com/darijgrinberg/darijgrinberg.gitlab.io/-/blob/master/public/algebra/alcove2025.pdf",gitlab.com,math.GR,math.GR math.RA math.RT mathematics group-theory linear-algebra p-adic-groups slides gitlab,Darij Grinberg and Patricia Commins and Franco Saliola,2025,null,"The random-to-random shuffles and their $q$-deformations: Alcove2025. Beamer slides by Darij Grinberg, Patricia Commins, and Franco Saliola, 2025; 92 pages. Part of Darij Grinberg's website: This is a mirror of my website, hosted at https://www.cip.ifi.lmu.de/~grinberg/ . The mirror can be found at https://darijgrinberg.gitlab.io/ . Sections: Random-to-random shuffles; Integrality \\ of eigenvalues; The Hecke algebra $\\mathcal{H}_{n}$; The recursion and commutativity. Slides cover \\ \\ \\ \\ Finite group algebras: Basics, \\ \\ \\ \\ Finite group algebras: $L\\left(a\\right)$ and $R\\left(a\\right)$, \\ \\ \\ \\ Finite group algebras: The antipode, \\ \\ \\ \\ Symmetric groups: Notations, \\ \\ \\ \\ The YJM elements, \\ \\ \\ \\ The card shuffling point of view, \\ \\ \\ \\ Bottom-to-random and random-to-bottom shuffles: definitions, \\ \\ \\ \\ Bottom-to-random and random-to-bottom shuffles: facts, \\ \\ \\ \\ Bottom-to-random and random-to-bottom shuffles: more, and \\ \\ \\ \\ Bottom-to-random and random-to-bottom shuffles: references."
