  2830,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 01: Digital Systems, FPGAs and HDL","https://gitlab.com/davide.cieri89/fpga-course-slides/-/blob/main/lesson01/lesson01.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AR,cs.AR math.LO computer-science mathematics computer-architecture mathematical-logic birational-geometry random-matrix-theory lecture-notes survey slides gitlab,Dr. Davide Cieri,2025,null,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 01: Digital Systems, FPGAs and HDL. Beamer slides by Dr. Davide Cieri (Max-Planck-Institut für Physik, Munich), 2025; 28 pages. From a repository described as: Lesson 1: Digital Systems, FPGAs and HDL - Lesson 2: VHDL Fundamentals - Lesson 3: Boolean Algebra and Look-up Tables - Lesson 4: Sequential Logic and Flip-Flops - Lesson 5: Types, Arrays and Arithmetic Functions - Lesson 6: VHDL Simulation - Lesson 7: Storing Data on FPGAs: RAMs and FIFOs - Lesson…. Slides cover Course Logistics, Course Programme, Analogue and Digital, Classification of Digital Devices, Integrated Circuits, Programmable Logic Devices, Field-Programmable Gate Arrays (FPGAs), Common FPGA Applications, FPGA vs. Microcontroller vs. ASIC, Major FPGA Vendors, AMD FPGA Families, Digilent Basys3 Board, Main Components of an FPGA, and Configurable Logic Blocks (CLBs)."
  2831,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 02: VHDL Fundamentals","https://gitlab.com/davide.cieri89/fpga-course-slides/-/blob/main/lesson02/lesson02.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AR,cs.AR computer-science computer-architecture birational-geometry concurrency mathematical-logic survey slides gitlab,Dr. Davide Cieri,2025,null,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 02: VHDL Fundamentals. Beamer slides by Dr. Davide Cieri (Max-Planck-Institut für Physik, Munich), 2025; 21 pages. From a repository described as: Lesson 1: Digital Systems, FPGAs and HDL - Lesson 2: VHDL Fundamentals - Lesson 3: Boolean Algebra and Look-up Tables - Lesson 4: Sequential Logic and Flip-Flops - Lesson 5: Types, Arrays and Arithmetic Functions - Lesson 6: VHDL Simulation - Lesson 7: Storing Data on FPGAs: RAMs and FIFOs - Lesson…. Slides cover VHDL Basics, VHDL building blocks, VHDL Types, Library Statements, The IEEE library, IEEE Packages, Buses and endianess, Straight Binary Code, Entity and Architecture syntax, Ports, Signal declaration, Advanced signal assignement, Concurrent Execution, and Module Instantiation."
  2832,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 03: Boolean Algebra, Look-up Tables and IOBs","https://gitlab.com/davide.cieri89/fpga-course-slides/-/blob/main/lesson03/lesson03.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AR,cs.AR math.LO computer-science mathematics computer-architecture mathematical-logic birational-geometry survey slides gitlab,Dr. Davide Cieri,2025,null,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 03: Boolean Algebra, Look-up Tables and IOBs. Beamer slides by Dr. Davide Cieri (Max-Planck-Institut für Physik, Munich), 2025; 17 pages. From a repository described as: Lesson 1: Digital Systems, FPGAs and HDL - Lesson 2: VHDL Fundamentals - Lesson 3: Boolean Algebra and Look-up Tables - Lesson 4: Sequential Logic and Flip-Flops - Lesson 5: Types, Arrays and Arithmetic Functions - Lesson 6: VHDL Simulation - Lesson 7: Storing Data on FPGAs: RAMs and FIFOs - Lesson…. Slides cover Boolean Algebra, Logic Gates, Combining Gates, The Look-Up Table, Xilinx 7-series LUTs, Pin Constraints, I/O Planning, XDC files, Specifying Physical Constraints, Useful XDC Commands, Where do I get information about the pin mapping?, and Setting Pin constraints for Basys3."
