  2834,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 05: Types, Arrays and Arithmetic Functions","https://gitlab.com/davide.cieri89/fpga-course-slides/-/blob/main/lesson05/lesson05.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AR,cs.AR computer-science computer-architecture birational-geometry combinatorics mathematical-logic survey slides gitlab,Dr. Davide Cieri,2025,null,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 05: Types, Arrays and Arithmetic Functions. Beamer slides by Dr. Davide Cieri (Max-Planck-Institut für Physik, Munich), 2025; 26 pages. From a repository described as: Lesson 1: Digital Systems, FPGAs and HDL - Lesson 2: VHDL Fundamentals - Lesson 3: Boolean Algebra and Look-up Tables - Lesson 4: Sequential Logic and Flip-Flops - Lesson 5: Types, Arrays and Arithmetic Functions - Lesson 6: VHDL Simulation - Lesson 7: Storing Data on FPGAs: RAMs and FIFOs - Lesson…. Slides cover Recap: VHDL Types, Type Conversion, Attributes of types and subtypes, Enumerated Types, Physical Types, Arrays, Default and Initial values, IEEE Data types, Accessing Vectors, Overflow / Underflow, Numeric type casting and conversion functions, Numeral and Bit-string literal values, VHDL Records, and Array of vectors."
  2835,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 06: VHDL Simulation","https://gitlab.com/davide.cieri89/fpga-course-slides/-/blob/main/lesson06/lesson06.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AR,cs.AR computer-science computer-architecture birational-geometry mathematical-logic survey slides gitlab,Dr. Davide Cieri,2025,null,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 06: VHDL Simulation. Beamer slides by Dr. Davide Cieri (Max-Planck-Institut für Physik, Munich), 2025; 28 pages. From a repository described as: Lesson 1: Digital Systems, FPGAs and HDL - Lesson 2: VHDL Fundamentals - Lesson 3: Boolean Algebra and Look-up Tables - Lesson 4: Sequential Logic and Flip-Flops - Lesson 5: Types, Arrays and Arithmetic Functions - Lesson 6: VHDL Simulation - Lesson 7: Storing Data on FPGAs: RAMs and FIFOs - Lesson…. Slides cover VHDL Simulation, VHDL Testbenches, VHDL Simulation Flow, Basic Testbench structure, Example: A simple Testbench, Example: Waveform, Discrete Event simulation, Delta Cycle example, Simulating the Clock Signal, Wait Statements, Synchronous reset signal, Stimulating data, Procedures, and Procedure Examples."
  2836,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 07: Storing Data on FPGAs","https://gitlab.com/davide.cieri89/fpga-course-slides/-/blob/main/lesson07/lesson07.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AR,cs.AR computer-science computer-architecture distributed-systems birational-geometry mathematical-logic survey slides gitlab,Dr. Davide Cieri,2025,null,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 07: Storing Data on FPGAs. Beamer slides by Dr. Davide Cieri (Max-Planck-Institut für Physik, Munich), 2025; 20 pages. From a repository described as: Lesson 1: Digital Systems, FPGAs and HDL - Lesson 2: VHDL Fundamentals - Lesson 3: Boolean Algebra and Look-up Tables - Lesson 4: Sequential Logic and Flip-Flops - Lesson 5: Types, Arrays and Arithmetic Functions - Lesson 6: VHDL Simulation - Lesson 7: Storing Data on FPGAs: RAMs and FIFOs - Lesson…. Slides cover Storing data on FPGAs, What's a RAM?, RAM on FPGAs, CLBs, Slices, SLICEL and SLICEM, Slice Control and Clock signals, Distributed RAM Configuration, Block RAM, RAMs in VHDL, Force the RAM type, Example: Single-Port Distributed RAM with asynchronous read, Example: Dual-Port BRAM with single clock, and ROMs."
  2837,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 08: Packages, Libraries and Parametrisation","https://gitlab.com/davide.cieri89/fpga-course-slides/-/blob/main/lesson08/lesson08.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AR,cs.AR computer-science computer-architecture birational-geometry mathematical-logic survey slides gitlab,Dr. Davide Cieri,2025,null,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 08: Packages, Libraries and Parametrisation. Beamer slides by Dr. Davide Cieri (Max-Planck-Institut für Physik, Munich), 2025; 18 pages. From a repository described as: Lesson 1: Digital Systems, FPGAs and HDL - Lesson 2: VHDL Fundamentals - Lesson 3: Boolean Algebra and Look-up Tables - Lesson 4: Sequential Logic and Flip-Flops - Lesson 5: Types, Arrays and Arithmetic Functions - Lesson 6: VHDL Simulation - Lesson 7: Storing Data on FPGAs: RAMs and FIFOs - Lesson…. Slides cover Introduction to VHDL Packages, Structure of VHDL Packages, Functions and procedures in packages, Using VHDL Libraries, Design Parametrisation, VHDL Generics, Generics Usage (Constants), Generics Usage (Generate Statements), If Generate Statement, If generate statement, Case Generate Statement, For generate statement, and Parametrise Memories and Counters."
  2838,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 09: Finite State Machines","https://gitlab.com/davide.cieri89/fpga-course-slides/-/blob/main/lesson09/lesson09.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AR,cs.AR computer-science computer-architecture birational-geometry mathematical-logic survey slides gitlab,Dr. Davide Cieri,2025,null,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 09: Finite State Machines. Beamer slides by Dr. Davide Cieri (Max-Planck-Institut für Physik, Munich), 2025; 15 pages. From a repository described as: Lesson 1: Digital Systems, FPGAs and HDL - Lesson 2: VHDL Fundamentals - Lesson 3: Boolean Algebra and Look-up Tables - Lesson 4: Sequential Logic and Flip-Flops - Lesson 5: Types, Arrays and Arithmetic Functions - Lesson 6: VHDL Simulation - Lesson 7: Storing Data on FPGAs: RAMs and FIFOs - Lesson…. Slides cover Finite State Machines, States, Transitions and Actions, Moore vs Mealy, Define FSM States in VHDL, State Encoding Implementation, Binary Encoding, One-Hot Encoding, Gray Encoding, Implementing FSMs in VHDL, Single Sequential Process Example, Multiple-Process FSM Example, and State Machine Best Practices."
  2839,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 09a: The 7-Segment Display","https://gitlab.com/davide.cieri89/fpga-course-slides/-/blob/main/lesson09a/lesson09a.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AR,cs.AR computer-science computer-architecture birational-geometry mathematical-logic survey slides gitlab,Dr. Davide Cieri,2025,null,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 09a: The 7-Segment Display. Beamer slides by Dr. Davide Cieri (Max-Planck-Institut für Physik, Munich), 2025; 7 pages. From a repository described as: Lesson 1: Digital Systems, FPGAs and HDL - Lesson 2: VHDL Fundamentals - Lesson 3: Boolean Algebra and Look-up Tables - Lesson 4: Sequential Logic and Flip-Flops - Lesson 5: Types, Arrays and Arithmetic Functions - Lesson 6: VHDL Simulation - Lesson 7: Storing Data on FPGAs: RAMs and FIFOs - Lesson…. Slides cover Introduction to the 7-Segment Display, 7-Segment Display Basics, How to illuminate a segment?, INTRODUCTION TO THE 7-SEGMENT DISPLAY, 7-SEGMENT DISPLAY BASICS, HOW TO ILLUMINATE A SEGMENT?, LAB 15: DESIGN A STOP WATCH [2 HOURS], and The figures in these slides are taken from."
  2840,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 10: IP Blocks","https://gitlab.com/davide.cieri89/fpga-course-slides/-/blob/main/lesson10/lesson10.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AR,cs.AR computer-science computer-architecture birational-geometry mathematical-logic survey slides gitlab,Dr. Davide Cieri,2025,null,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 10: IP Blocks. Beamer slides by Dr. Davide Cieri (Max-Planck-Institut für Physik, Munich), 2025; 13 pages. From a repository described as: Lesson 1: Digital Systems, FPGAs and HDL - Lesson 2: VHDL Fundamentals - Lesson 3: Boolean Algebra and Look-up Tables - Lesson 4: Sequential Logic and Flip-Flops - Lesson 5: Types, Arrays and Arithmetic Functions - Lesson 6: VHDL Simulation - Lesson 7: Storing Data on FPGAs: RAMs and FIFOs - Lesson…. Slides cover What are IP Blocks, IP Generation, IP Documentation, IP Generated Files, IP Instantiation in VHDL, Another Example: Block RAM, User IPs, User IP Creation, IP Integrator, and Block Design Example."
  2841,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 11: Timing on FPGAs","https://gitlab.com/davide.cieri89/fpga-course-slides/-/blob/main/lesson11/lesson11.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AR,cs.AR computer-science computer-architecture birational-geometry mathematical-logic survey slides gitlab,Dr. Davide Cieri,2025,null,"Introduction to FPGA Programming: Lesson 11: Timing on FPGAs. Beamer slides by Dr. Davide Cieri (Max-Planck-Institut für Physik, Munich), 2025; 30 pages. From a repository described as: Lesson 1: Digital Systems, FPGAs and HDL - Lesson 2: VHDL Fundamentals - Lesson 3: Boolean Algebra and Look-up Tables - Lesson 4: Sequential Logic and Flip-Flops - Lesson 5: Types, Arrays and Arithmetic Functions - Lesson 6: VHDL Simulation - Lesson 7: Storing Data on FPGAs: RAMs and FIFOs - Lesson…. Slides cover Propagation Delays, Setup and Hold Times, Metastability, Fix Timing Errors, Double Flopping, Clock Domain Crossing (CDC), Double Flip-Flop Synchroniser, Handshaking Synchroniser, FIFO Synchroniser, Gray Code, Asynchronous FIFO Synchroniser, Clocking resources on 7-series AMD FPGA, Global Clocks (BUFG), and BUFH."
