  2851,"Timestamping with OpenTimestamps: DevConf.CZ, 2025","https://gitlab.com/drizzt/slides/-/blob/master/opentimestamps/opentimestamps.pdf",gitlab.com,math.AG,math.AG math.CA math.SG mathematics geometric-invariant-theory real-analysis survey slides gitlab,Timothy M. Redaelli,2025,null,"Timestamping with OpenTimestamps: DevConf.CZ, 2025. Beamer slides by Timothy M. Redaelli, 2025; 55 pages. Sections: Introduction to Timestamping; Timestamping and Blockchain; OpenTimestamps. Subsections include What is timestamping?, What is digital timestamping?, How can we use the Blockchain for timestamping?, Why the Blockchain?, Why OpenTimestamps?, Usage, Solving the PGP revocation problem with OpenTimestamps for git commits and tags, Possible integration in RPM, and Examples of OpenTimestamps usage. Slides cover Index, What is timestamping?, What is digital timestamping?, How can we use the Blockchain for timestamping?, Why the Blockchain?, Why OpenTimestamps?, Merkle Tree, Usage, Timestamp creation, and Timestamp verification."
  2852,"Linear Systems of Differential Equations: 01204215 Differential Equations and Linear Algebra (jittat/01204215-diffeq-linalg-slides)","https://gitlab.com/jittat/01204215-diffeq-linalg-slides/-/blob/main/slides/06-linear-systems.pdf",gitlab.com,math.DS,math.DS math.RA math.CA math.NA mathematics ode-and-dynamical-systems linear-algebra lecture-notes slides gitlab,Jittat Fakcharoenphol,2025,null,"Linear Systems of Differential Equations: 01204215 Differential Equations and Linear Algebra (jittat/01204215-diffeq-linalg-slides). Beamer slides by Jittat Fakcharoenphol (Kasetsart University), 2025; 96 pages. From the course-materials archive jittat/01204215-diffeq-linalg-slides. Slides cover Review, Linear algebra concepts, Linear systems of first-order differential equations, Example 1: Oscillation, Two visualizations, Phase plane, Example 2, More compactly, Example 3, Example 4, Equilibria, Review: singular matrix, Stability, and Straight line solutions."
  2853,Lin68 - 02a - Vectors,"https://gitlab.com/jittat/01204215-diffeq-linalg-slides/-/blob/main/slides/lin68-02a-vectors.slides.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2025,null,"Lin68 - 02a - Vectors. Beamer slides, 2025; 27 pages. From the course-materials archive jittat/01204215-diffeq-linalg-slides. Slides cover What is a vector?, What can be represented as a vector?, Applications in machine learning, Viewing vectors: vectors in R2, Viewing vectors: vectors in R3, Vector operations, Vector additions, and Vector additions, in picture."
  2854,Lin68 - 02b - Fields - Lightsout,"https://gitlab.com/jittat/01204215-diffeq-linalg-slides/-/blob/main/slides/lin68-02b-fields-lightsout.slides.pdf",gitlab.com,math.RA,math.RA math.NA mathematics linear-algebra lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2025,null,"Lin68 - 02b - Fields - Lightsout. Beamer slides, 2025; 32 pages. From the course-materials archive jittat/01204215-diffeq-linalg-slides. Slides cover Review: Linear combinations, Review: Span, Example 1, Example 3, A field, Another useful field: GF(2), 2 × 2 Lights out, Can you solve 2 × 2 Lights out?, Generators, Standard generators, Generators and spans, Hamming code, and Hamming code (encoding as matrix multiplication)."
  2855,Lin68 - 04b - Matrices,"https://gitlab.com/jittat/01204215-diffeq-linalg-slides/-/blob/main/slides/lin68-04b-matrices.slides.pdf",gitlab.com,math.RA,math.RA math.NA mathematics linear-algebra quantum-groups lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2025,null,"Lin68 - 04b - Matrices. Beamer slides, 2025; 116 pages. From the course-materials archive jittat/01204215-diffeq-linalg-slides. Slides cover What is a vector?, Linear combinations, What is a matrix?, Size, Matrix-Vector Multiplication, Matrix-Vector Multiplication by Columns, Two perspectives: Matrix-Vector multiplication, Document vector models, Dot products as a similarity measure, and Vector-matrix multiplication."
  2856,The Classical/NonClassical Decomposition of Quantum States,"https://gitlab.com/m-amin/conferences-and-workshops/-/blob/master/AMD-presentation.pdf",gitlab.com,math.PR,math.PR mathematics probability slides talk gitlab,Mustafa Amin,2025,null,"The Classical/NonClassical Decomposition of Quantum States. Beamer slides by Mustafa Amin, 2025; 33 pages. Part of Conferences and Workshops: A repository of my contributions (presentations, posters, etc.) to conferences and workshops. Slides cover Why would we want classical in the quantum?, The classical within - Part I: The classical limit, Problems, Too restrictive, A classical state corresponding to a quantum one, Where do classical probabilities come from?, How to calculate the classical probability?, The Van Vleck \"wavefunction\", and Example: With pictures."
  2857,"Classical Hilbert space, statistical mechanics, and gauge freedom","https://gitlab.com/m-amin/conferences-and-workshops/-/blob/master/CAPC2025-presentation.pdf",gitlab.com,math.FA,math.FA math.PR cond-mat.stat-mech math-ph mathematics physics functional-analysis statistical-mechanics operator-algebras slides talk gitlab,Mustafa Amin,2025,null,"Classical Hilbert space, statistical mechanics, and gauge freedom. Beamer slides by Mustafa Amin, 2025; 36 pages. Part of Conferences and Workshops: A repository of my contributions (presentations, posters, etc.) to conferences and workshops. Slides cover Heisenberg and Schr ̈odinger, Koopman and von Neumann, Gauged-KvN equation, Separating time / Stationary states, Separating q and p, Different gauges, different equations, “Superposable” states, and More details!."
  2858,Noncommutative Formulation of Classical Mechanics,"https://gitlab.com/m-amin/conferences-and-workshops/-/blob/master/TC17-presentation.pdf",gitlab.com,math-ph,math-ph physics.class-ph hep-th math.DS physics mathematics dynamics-and-vibrations mathematical-physics operator-algebras slides talk gitlab,Mustafa Amin,2025,null,"Noncommutative Formulation of Classical Mechanics. Beamer slides by Mustafa Amin, 2025; 25 pages. Part of Conferences and Workshops: A repository of my contributions (presentations, posters, etc.) to conferences and workshops. Slides cover Operators in CM?, Koopman-von Neumann (plus), The \"auxiliary\" variables, Commutators, Tilde-images / General map, Map of main operations, How is this different from QM?, and What’s it good for?."
  2859,"Modelo de apresentações PPGCA – UTFPR Curitiba: Universidade Tecnológica Federal do Paraná","https://gitlab.com/mokira3d48/ppgca-utfpr-curitib-slide/-/blob/master/main.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.PL,cs.PL computer-science programming-languages slides gitlab,Nome da pessoa autora,2025,null,"Modelo de apresentações PPGCA – UTFPR Curitiba: Universidade Tecnológica Federal do Paraná. Beamer slides by Nome da pessoa autora (Universidade Tecnológica Federal do Paraná Programa de Pós-Graduação em Computação Aplicad), 2025; 12 pages, in Dutch. Part of IF-BEAMER - Modelo de Apresentação Ifes - v1.0.1. Subject (translated): programming languages. Sections: Introdução; Metodologia; Resultados. Subsections include Contextualização, and Objetivos. Slides cover Programação, Contextualização, Motivação, Justificativa, Objetivo geral, Objetivos específicos, and Métodos de desenvolvimento."
  2860,"Introduction to Octopus: a real-space (TD)DFT code: Octopus 2025","https://gitlab.com/octopus-code/octopus-presentations/-/blob/master/benasque-2025/general_introduction/Octopus_2025.pdf",gitlab.com,math.NA,math.NA math.RA math.SG cs.NA mathematics computer-science linear-algebra numerical-analysis symplectic-geometry lecture-notes survey slides gitlab,Martin Lüders and Alex Buccheri and Heiko Appel and David Strubbe,2025,null,"Introduction to Octopus: a real-space (TD)DFT code: Octopus 2025. Beamer slides by Martin Lüders, Alex Buccheri, Heiko Appel, and David Strubbe, 2025; 94 pages. From the course-materials archive octopus-code/octopus-presentations. Slides cover Schedule, The Octopus code, The Octopus code: features and functionalities, The Octopus code: new features, Dissecting the animal, Pseudo-potentials, Real-space grid, Discretization of the Hamiltonian, The eigenvalue problem, and Boundary conditions."
  2861,"Introduction to Octopus: Maxwell systems: Octopus Maxwell","https://gitlab.com/octopus-code/octopus-presentations/-/blob/master/benasque-2025/octopus_maxwell/octopus_maxwell.pdf",gitlab.com,math.AP,math.AP mathematics pde lecture-notes survey slides gitlab,Heiko Appel and Franco Bonafé,2025,null,"Introduction to Octopus: Maxwell systems: Octopus Maxwell. Beamer slides by Heiko Appel, and Franco Bonafé, 2025; 25 pages. From the course-materials archive octopus-code/octopus-presentations. Slides cover First, why we are solving Maxwell: Maxwell-TDDFT, Maxwell’s equations, Maxwell’s equations in Riemann-Silberstein form, Maxwell’s equations in Schr ̈odinger form, Time-evolution of the electromagnetic field, Dispersive media, Drude dispersive media, Boundary regions, Absorbing boundaries and incident waves, Coupling of light and matter, The tutorials, Maxwell input file: simulation box, and Maxwell input file: initial EM field conditions."
  2862,Evaluation of EAP Usage for Authenticating Wi-Fi Enterprise Users in 5G Networks,"https://gitlab.com/oliveiraleo/wd-25/-/blob/main/Slides_IEEE_Wireless_Days__WD__2025.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.NI,cs.NI math.CA computer-science mathematics networking real-analysis slides gitlab,null,2025,null,"Evaluation of EAP Usage for Authenticating Wi-Fi Enterprise Users in 5G Networks. Beamer slides, 2025; 15 pages. Part of Wireless days 2025 slides: Archive of the PDF slides presented at 13th Wireless Days Conference. Sections: Results and Discussion; Closing Remarks. Slides cover Index, Context, Convergence Architecture, Open Issues, and Conclusion and Future Work."
  2863,"PySpike: Agile Co-Verification of RISC-V SoC's and Beyond","https://gitlab.com/siemens/opensource/-/blob/main/site/events/2025cn/slides/workshop/05_PySpike_LiuYu.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AR,cs.AR computer-science computer-architecture concurrency lecture-notes slides talk gitlab,null,2025,null,"PySpike: Agile Co-Verification of RISC-V SoC's and Beyond. Beamer talk slides, 2025; 38 pages. From the course-materials archive siemens/opensource. Sections: Notable Features; Real-World Examples; Our Open-Source Playbook; Remarks and Outlook. Slides cover Collaborative (concurrent) engineering 101, What Spike is all about, What Spike is all about (cont’d), Why Spike needs Python bindings, What PySpike has to offer, exactly, What PySpike has to offer, exactly (cont’d), PySpike in the big picture of co-verification, Case #1: Continuous test program verifier, Case #2: CPU trace log decoder and beyond, and Strategy #1: Extend, don’t modify."
  2864,Tout savoir sur l’alignement et recalage d’images. . . ou presque,"https://gitlab.com/spam-project/talks/-/blob/main/INRAE-MultiModal/multimodal-registration.pdf",gitlab.com,math.AG,math.AG mathematics algebraic-geometry schemes slides gitlab,Emmanuel Roubin,2025,null,"Tout savoir sur l’alignement et recalage d’images. . . ou presque. Beamer slides by Emmanuel Roubin, 2025; 44 pages. Slides cover Generalities on Digital Image/Volume Correlation, Registration : one point transformation, What to do with two modalities, Goal, issue and solution, The joint histogram, The likelihood, The “Kandinsky” joint histogram, and Pyramidal scheme."
  2865,Linux File and Directory Management,"https://gitlab.com/sreekanth.vk/latex-presentations/-/blob/main/gnu-linux/gnu-linux-d2.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.OS,cs.OS computer-science operating-systems slides gitlab,null,2025,null,"Linux File and Directory Management. Beamer slides (Centre for Information Technology Research and Automation National Institute of Technology), 2025; 31 pages. From a repository described as: To make it easy for you to get started with GitLab, here's a list of recommended next steps. Slides cover Changing Directory (cd), Relative vs Absolute Paths, Arguments and Options, Pipes and Redirection, Help and Documentation, File Types, Creating Files and Directories, Moving, Renaming, Copying, Deleting Files and Directories, Syncing with rsync, Links: Soft vs Hard, Viewing File Contents, and Monitoring with watch and journalctl."
  2866,"L3E: Libre, Linux, & LaTeX in Education","https://gitlab.com/sreekanth.vk/latex-presentations/-/blob/main/gnu-linux/gnu-linux.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.OS,cs.OS computer-science operating-systems survey slides gitlab,null,2025,null,"L3E: Libre, Linux, & LaTeX in Education. Beamer slides (Centre for Information Technology Research and Automation National Institute of Technology), 2025; 21 pages. From a repository described as: To make it easy for you to get started with GitLab, here's a list of recommended next steps. Sections: FOSS United; Introduction to Libre and Linux; Introduction to Ubuntu; Desktop Environment; Introduction to Users and Permissions; Setting Ubuntu. Slides cover About FOSS United, Introduction to (GNU)Linux, Who Creates Ubuntu?, Ubuntu Key Info, GNOME Desktop Environment, Exploring GNOME UI, Default Applications in Ubuntu, Alternative UI Options, Other Linux Distros, and Users and Permissions."
