  2868,Birth-death models for estimating speciation and epidemiological parameters,"https://gitlab.com/ttb2025-group/Taming-the-BEAST-2025-Beijing-Lectures/-/blob/main/S10_SG_Research.pdf",gitlab.com,q-bio.QM,q-bio.QM q-bio.PE quantitative-biology computational-biology slides talk gitlab,Alexandra ``Sasha'' Gavryushkina,2025,null,"Birth-death models for estimating speciation and epidemiological parameters. Beamer slides by Alexandra ``Sasha'' Gavryushkina, 2025; 47 pages. Part of Taming the BEAST Beijing 2025 Lectures: This repository (will) contain (most of) the lecture slides from the ninth Taming the BEAST workshop, held in Beijing, China, in July 2025. The tutorials are available elsewhere. Sections: Birth-death models; Identifiability of birth-death model parameters; Stratigraphic-range birth-death model. Slides cover Constant rate birth-death sampling (BDS) model, Piecewise constant BDS, Theoretical identifiability, Birth-death model with present sampling, Time-dependant BD model congruence classes (Louca & Pennell 2020), Birth-death-sampling model r = 1, ρ0 = 0, Birth-death sampling model re-parametrisation, Modelling fossil sampling in FBD, Mixed speciation stratigraphic range fossilised birth-death process, and Total evidence dating with SRFBD."
  2869,Model selection via marginal likelihood estimation,"https://gitlab.com/ttb2025-group/Taming-the-BEAST-2025-Beijing-Lectures/-/blob/main/S12.1_RY_model_selection_lecture.pdf",gitlab.com,math.ST,math.ST stat.ME mathematics statistics computational-biology topos-theory slides talk gitlab,Robert Haobo Yuan,2025,null,"Model selection via marginal likelihood estimation. Beamer lecture slides by Robert Haobo Yuan, 2025; 95 pages. Part of Taming the BEAST Beijing 2025 Lectures: This repository (will) contain (most of) the lecture slides from the ninth Taming the BEAST workshop, held in Beijing, China, in July 2025. The tutorials are available elsewhere. Sections: Model selection; Marginal likelihood estimation; Path and stepping-stone sampling; Nested sampling. Slides cover Why do we want to do model selection?, Bayesian inference of time-calibrated phylogenies, Site and substitution model, Tree topology, Root age of Indo-European languages, Tree model?, Likelihood and Marginal likelihood, Estimating ML is hard! Why?, Do we have alternatives to ML estimation?, and Path sampling: In theory."
  2870,Memory Hierarchy and Technologies,"https://gitlab.com/upes1/courses/-/blob/main/COA/COA_UNIT_IV.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AR,cs.AR computer-science computer-architecture category-theory slides gitlab,Srinivasan Ramachandran,2025,null,"Memory Hierarchy and Technologies. Beamer slides by Srinivasan Ramachandran, 2025; 41 pages. From a repository described as: To make it easy for you to get started with GitLab, here's a list of recommended next steps. Sections: Primary Memory; Cache Memory; Memory Organization; Emerging Memory Technologies. Slides cover Memory Hierarchy, Categories, How Everything Connects, RAM & ROM Chip Organization: Address Line Perspective, Static RAM (SRAM), Programmable ROM (PROM), Electrically Erasable PROM (EEPROM), Practice Problem 1, Cache Memory Principles, and Direct Mapped Cache."
