  2927,"Mathematics for Cryptography: Basic Notation and Groups: Part 1","https://github.com/BlockstreamResearch/zk-book/blob/main/presentations/1-math-animated.pdf",github.com,cs.CR,cs.CR math.LO math.GR cs.DC computer-science mathematics security-and-privacy mathematical-logic abstract-algebra distributed-systems lecture-notes slides github,null,2024,null,"Mathematics for Cryptography: Basic Notation and Groups: Part 1. Beamer slides, 2024; 122 pages. From a repository described as: This is a series of lectures on zero-knowledge conducted internally at Blockstream and Distributed Lab, in which we covered essentials for Research and Development in the field of zero-knowledge proofs and their applications. Sections: Some words about the course; Notation; Basic Group Theory; Polynomials. Subsections include Sets, Logic, Randomness and Sequences, Reasoning behind Groups, Group Definition and Examples, Subgroups, Cyclic Groups, Homomorphism and Isomorphism, Definition, and Roots and Divisibility. Slides cover About ZKDL, Why ZKDL?, Format, Sets, Operations on sets, Operations on sets: Examples, Defining sets, Cartesian Product, Cartesian Product Questions, and Basic Logic."
