  2937,Commitment Schemes,"https://github.com/BlockstreamResearch/zk-book/blob/main/presentations/5-commitments.pdf",github.com,math.AG,math.AG mathematics algebraic-geometry schemes distributed-systems lecture-notes survey slides github,null,2024,null,"Commitment Schemes. Beamer slides, 2024; 24 pages. From a repository described as: This is a series of lectures on zero-knowledge conducted internally at Blockstream and Distributed Lab, in which we covered essentials for Research and Development in the field of zero-knowledge proofs and their applications. Sections: Commitments Overview; Hash-based Commitments; Vector Commitments; Polynomial commitment. Subsections include Merkle Tree based Vector Commitment, Pedersen commitment, and Kate-Zaverucha-Goldberg (KZG). Slides cover Commitment Definition, Commitment Scheme Properties, Merkle Tree commitments, Merkle Tree Proof (MTP), Pedersen Commitment, Pedersen Commitment Aggregation, Pedersen Vector Commitment, KZG Commitment. Simplified example, and KZG Commitment."
  2938,"Introduction to Zero-Knowledge Proofs: Part 6: Intro Zk Animated","https://github.com/BlockstreamResearch/zk-book/blob/main/presentations/6-intro-zk-animated.pdf",github.com,cs.CR,cs.CR cs.DC computer-science distributed-systems security-and-privacy lecture-notes survey slides github,null,2024,null,"Introduction to Zero-Knowledge Proofs: Part 6: Intro Zk Animated. Beamer slides, 2024; 148 pages. From a repository described as: This is a series of lectures on zero-knowledge conducted internally at Blockstream and Distributed Lab, in which we covered essentials for Research and Development in the field of zero-knowledge proofs and their applications. Sections: Relations. Languages. NP Statements.; Interactive Proofs; Fiat-Shamir Heuristic. Subsections include Classical Proofs, Goal of the course, Language of true statements. Examples., P and NP Statements, Quadratic Residue Interactive Proof, Completeness and Soundness, Zero-Knowledge and Honest-Verifier Zero-Knowledge, Proof of Knowledge, Cryptographic Oracles, and Fiat-Shamir Transformation. Slides cover Classical Proofs, The most basic setting, Example to demonstrate the goal, Language, Language Example #1: Semiprimes, Language Example #2: Square Root, NP Statements: Demonstration, NP Statements, Question (aka Motivation), and Solution!."
