  2940,"Sigma Protocols: Part 7: Sigma Animated","https://github.com/BlockstreamResearch/zk-book/blob/main/presentations/7-sigma-animated.pdf",github.com,math.AG,math.AG cs.DC cs.LG mathematics computer-science algebraic-geometry schemes distributed-systems machine-learning lecture-notes slides github,null,2024,null,"Sigma Protocols: Part 7: Sigma Animated. Beamer slides, 2024; 130 pages. From a repository described as: This is a series of lectures on zero-knowledge conducted internally at Blockstream and Distributed Lab, in which we covered essentials for Research and Development in the field of zero-knowledge proofs and their applications. Sections: Schnorr Identification Protocol; Sigma Protocols; Sigma Protocols Examples; Coding Time!. Subsections include Recap, Motivation for $\\Sigma$-protocols, Interactive Protocol, Non-interactive Schnorr's Identification Protocol, Schnorr's Signature Scheme, Definition, Okamoto Representation Protocol, Chaum-Pedersen Protocol, Pre-image of a homomorphism $\\Sigma$-protocol, and Combining $\\Sigma$-Protocols. Slides cover Recap on Interactive Proofs, Problem Statement, Protocol Flow, Applying Fiat-Shamir Transformation, Schnorr's Signature Scheme, Generalization, Why $\\Sigma$?, Special Soundness, Okamoto's Protocol, and Okamoto's Protocol Flow."
