  2983,Principles of Formal Languages,"https://github.com/florian-rabe/Teaching/blob/master/Formal%20Systems/PFL_slides.pdf",github.com,cs.FL,cs.FL cs.DS cs.PL math.LO computer-science mathematics automata-and-formal-languages algorithms mathematical-logic programming-languages lecture-notes slides github,Florian Rabe,2024,null,"Principles of Formal Languages. Beamer slides by Florian Rabe (Computer Science, University Erlangen-Nürnberg, Germany), 2024; 303 pages. From a repository described as: This repository contains my course materials, specifically for Algorithms and Data Structures (AaDS) Secure and Dependable Systems (SaDS) various courses on logic. Sections: Syntax; Type Systems; Programming Languages; Ontology Languages; Concrete Data Languages; Deductive Languages; Narrative Languages. Slides cover Administrative Information, Language Layers, Context-Sensitive Syntax, Non-Recursive Data Types, Recursive Abstract Data Types, OWL-Style Ontology Languages, OWL-Style vs. SQL-Style Ontology Languages, Data Interoperability through Codecs, Typed First-Order Logic, and Semantics."
