  3023,Lecture 17 — Generating Function (3) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2024-01/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-17.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics combinatorics ode-and-dynamical-systems lecture-notes slides problem-list gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 17 — Generating Function (3) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 48 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2024-01): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University which started in January 2024. Sections: ac 8.5 Partition of an Integer; ac 8.6 Exponential Generating Function. Subsections include Integer Partition, Integer Partition with Restrictions, Partitions with Odd Parts and Distinct Parts, What is egf?, Example 8.17: egfs and Strings, and Ternary Strings. Slides cover Required Reading and Exercises, Integer Partition: An Example, Two Giants who Studied Integer Partitions, Paying for Lunch with Cash, Paying with $5 bills, Why Does This Work?, Exercise, Two Ways to Pay $n, Strings Consisting of Two Letters, and An Application of egf: Mixing Two Types of Strings."
  3024,Lecture 19 — Recurrence Equations (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2024-01/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-19.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics combinatorics lecture-notes slides problem-list gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 19 — Recurrence Equations (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 47 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2024-01): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University which started in January 2024. Sections: ac 9.4 Solving Advancement Operator Equations; ac 9.6 Using Generating Functions to Solve Recurrences; ac 9.7 Solving a Nonlinear Recurrence. Subsections include Nonhomogeneous Case. Slides cover Required Reading and Exercises, Finding One Solution, The general solution of (2), Example 9.15, Can you guess the next problem?, Example 9.16, Example 9.17, Example 9.25, Full Binary Tree, and Step 1: Find the generating function."
  3025,Lecture 20 — A Game! - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2024-01/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-20.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.LO mathematics combinatorics mathematical-logic lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 20 — A Game! - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 40 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2024-01): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University which started in January 2024. Sections: Logic; Sequences; Basic Combinatorics; Inclusion-Exclusion; Generating Functions. Slides cover Who is going to be the winner?, Choose Your Challenge, Strings, Sets and Binomial, A spider with shoes and socks, Peaceful rooks, Apples and bananas, Induction, A Flawed Proof!, Dividing a Square, and Problems of Integer Composition."
  3026,Lecture 21 — Basic Notation and Terminology for Graphs - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2024-01/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-21.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics graph-theory extremal-combinatorics lecture-notes slides problem-list gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 21 — Basic Notation and Terminology for Graphs - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 45 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2024-01): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University which started in January 2024. Sections: ac 5.1 Basic Notation and Terminology for Graphs; ac 5.2 Multigraphs: Loops and Multiple Edges. Subsections include Graphs in the Real World, Basic Notation and Terminology for Graphs, Subgraphs, Some Common Graphs, Moving Around in Graphs, Graph Isomorphism, and Connected Graphs. Slides cover Required Reading and Exercises, Metro Network as a Graph, Drawing graphs, Theorem 5.9 (ac), At a recent maths seminar, 9, Spanning Subgraphs, Complete Graph, Walks, Cycles, and Graph Isomorphism."
  3027,Lecture 22 — Trees - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2024-01/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-22.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.NT math.AG mathematics graph-theory arithmetic-geometry lecture-notes slides problem-list gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 22 — Trees - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-01). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 46 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2024-01): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University which started in January 2024. Sections: dm 4.2 Trees. Subsections include Definition of Trees, Properties of Trees, Rooted Trees, Bipartite Graphs, Spanning Trees, and Cut Edges. Slides cover Required Reading and Exercises, Acyclic Graphs, Forests, Example of trees and forests, Proposition 4.2.1, Proposition 4.2.3 (dm)/Proposition 5.11 (ac), Proposition 4.2.4, Rooted Trees, Where to Put the Root?, and Generations and Height."
