  3038,Lecture 04 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2024-08/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-04.pdf",gitlab.com,math.NT,math.NT math.CO math.HO physics.hist-ph mathematics physics number-theory combinatorics philosophy-of-mathematics lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 04 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-08). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 65 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2024-08): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: dm 3.2 Proofs. Subsections include What Is a Mathematical Proof?, Direct Proof, Proof by Contrapositive, Proof by Contradiction, Proof by (Counter) Example, Proof by Cases, and Proof of If and Only if. Slides cover Assignments1, What Is a Mathematical Proof?, Theorem 3.2.1 — The Infinity of Primes, Euclid’s Proof, Direct Proof, Proof by Contrapositive, Prove by contrapositive that for every prime number p, if p≠2,, Ration and Irrational Numbers, A Special Case of Proof by Contradiction, and Pigeonholes."
