  3052,Lecture 22 — Trees - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2024-08/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-22.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics graph-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 22 — Trees - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-08). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 47 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2024-08): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: dm 4.2 Trees. Subsections include Definition of Trees, Properties of Trees, Rooted Trees, Bipartite Graphs, Spanning Trees, and Cut Edges. Slides cover Assignments1, Acyclic Graphs, Trees, Example of trees and forests, Think-Pair-Share, Proposition 4.2.1, Proposition 4.2.3 (dm)/Proposition 5.11 (ac), Proposition 4.2.4, Rooted Trees, and Where to Put the Root?."
  3053,Lecture 24 — Eulerian and Hamiltonian Graphs - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2024-08/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-24.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.SG mathematics graph-theory symplectic-geometry algorithms lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 24 — Eulerian and Hamiltonian Graphs - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-08). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 53 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2024-08): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 5.3 Eulerian and Hamiltonian Graphs. Subsections include Eulerian Graphs, and Hamiltonian Graphs. Slides cover Assignments1, The Seven Bridges Problem, Eulerian Graphs, Theorem 5.13 (ac) — Euler’s Theory, The Algorithm, Termination on A Disconnected Graph, Hamiltonian Graphs, Theorem 5.18 (ac) – Sufficient Condition For Being Hamiltonian, and Theorem 5.18 (ac) – The proof."
  3054,Lecture 25 — Graph Colouring (1) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2024-08/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-25.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.AT mathematics graph-theory chromatic-homotopy-theory extremal-combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 25 — Graph Colouring (1) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-08). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 52 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2024-08): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 5.4 Graph Colouring. Subsections include Motivational Example, Chromatic Number, Chromatic Number of Specific Graphs, Chromatic Number of Cycles, and Chromatic Number of Bipartite Graphs. Slides cover Assignments1, Colours to Help, Can We Do Better?, Chromatic Number, Nature of Colours, Trivial Bounds, Chromatic Number and Subgraphs, A Recipe for Finding the Chromatic Number of a Graph, Chromatic Number of Cycles, and Odd Cycle."
  3055,Lecture 26 — Graph Colouring (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2024-08/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-26.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.AT mathematics graph-theory chromatic-homotopy-theory extremal-combinatorics lecture-notes slides problem-list gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 26 — Graph Colouring (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-08). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 45 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2024-08): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 5.4.2 Cliques and Chromatic Number. Subsections include Cliques and Clique Number, Proof of Proposition 5.25 (ac) by J. Kelly and L. Kelly, and Proof of Proposition 5.25 (ac) by J. Mycielski. Slides cover Required Reading and Exercises, Review — Induced Subgraphs, Clique Number and Chromatic Number, For every t≥3, there exists a graph Gtso that χ(Gt) = tand, Proposition 5.24 (ac) — Generalized Hole Principle, Proof of Proposition 5.25 (ac) by Kelly and Kelly — A Sketch, Construct Gt+1, Verify Gt+1 is -free, and A Lower Bound of the Chromatic Number."
