  3057,Lecture 28 — Planar Graphs - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2024-08/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/lecture-28.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics graph-theory lecture-notes slides problem-list gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 28 — Planar Graphs - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-08). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 53 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2024-08): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 5.5 Planar Graphs. Subsections include Definitions of Planar Graphs, Euler's Formula, Is This Planar? — A Simple Check, Kuratowski's Theorem, and Four Colour Theorem. Slides cover Required Reading and Exercises, Planar graphs, Euler’s Formula, Faces of a planar graph, Theorem 5.32 (ac) — Euler’s Formula, Euler’s Formula — Induction step, Think-Pair-Share, An Inequality, Theorem 5.33 (ac) — Applications, and Proof that K3,3 Is Not Planar."
  3058,Welcome - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2024-08/-/blob/main/pdf/slides/welcome.pdf",gitlab.com,math.FA,math.FA mathematics functional-analysis lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Welcome - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2024-08). Beamer slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 15 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2024-08): Welcome to the repository for the course COMPSCI203 Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science at Duke Kunshan University. Sections: Why Are You Here?; A Few Important Things. Slides cover Why Should You Take This Course?, Why I Think You Should Take This Course?, Distribution of Points, You may also be asked to repeat a proof presented in the, What You Definitely Need to Know, Emoji, and Now let’s play!."
  3059,Lecture 01 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/30-lectures-discrete-mathematics),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/30-lectures-discrete-mathematics/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-01.pdf",gitlab.com,math.LO,math.LO mathematics mathematical-logic lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 01 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/30-lectures-discrete-mathematics). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 54 pages. Part of 30 Lectures in Discrete Mathematics. Sections: dm 0.2 Mathematical Statements. Subsections include Atomic and Molecular Statements, Implications, Converses and Contrapositives, Necessity and Sufficiency, and Predicates and Quantifiers. Slides cover Assignments1, Statements, Molecular Statements, Logic Connectives, Think-Pair-Share, Implications, A Lying Professor, Does Implication Equal Causality?, Converses, and If and only if/Biconditional."
  3060,Lecture 02 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/30-lectures-discrete-mathematics),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/30-lectures-discrete-mathematics/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-02.pdf",gitlab.com,math.LO,math.LO mathematics mathematical-logic lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 02 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/30-lectures-discrete-mathematics). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 59 pages. Part of 30 Lectures in Discrete Mathematics. Sections: dm 0.4 Functions. Subsections include Notations, Relationships Between Sets, Operations On Sets, Describing Functions, Surjections, Injections and Bijections, and Image and Inverse Image. Slides cover Assignments1, Numbers, Set Builder Notation, Think-Pair-Share, Subsets, Difference, Set Theory Notations, Functions, Example — Non-Functions, and Describing Functions (2)."
  3061,Lecture 03 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/30-lectures-discrete-mathematics),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/30-lectures-discrete-mathematics/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-03.pdf",gitlab.com,math.LO,math.LO math.PR mathematics mathematical-logic random-matrix-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 03 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/30-lectures-discrete-mathematics). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 52 pages. Part of 30 Lectures in Discrete Mathematics. Sections: dm 3.1 Propositional Logic. Subsections include Truth Tables, Xor — Exclusive-or, Logical Equivalence, Deductions — How to argue with logic, and Beyond Propositions. Slides cover Assignments1, A Propositional about Monopoly, Truth Tables, The Monopoly Problem, Knights and Knaves Puzzles, Solving the Puzzle with a Truth Table, Exercise, Example — Snow and Rain, Basic Logic Equivalence (1), and Basic Logic Equivalence (2)."
  3062,Lecture 04 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/30-lectures-discrete-mathematics),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/30-lectures-discrete-mathematics/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-04.pdf",gitlab.com,math.NT,math.NT math.CO math.HO physics.hist-ph mathematics physics number-theory combinatorics philosophy-of-mathematics lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 04 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/30-lectures-discrete-mathematics). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 65 pages. Part of 30 Lectures in Discrete Mathematics. Sections: dm 3.2 Proofs. Subsections include What Is a Mathematical Proof?, Direct Proof, Proof by Contrapositive, Proof by Contradiction, Proof by (Counter) Example, Proof by Cases, and Proof of If and Only if. Slides cover Assignments1, What Is a Mathematical Proof?, Theorem 3.2. 1 — The Infinity of Primes, Euclid’s Proof, Direct Proof, Proof by Contrapositive, Prove by contrapositive that for every prime number p, if p≠2 ,, Ration and Irrational Numbers, A Special Case of Proof by Contradiction, and Pigeonholes."
