  3064,Lecture 07 — Alternating Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/30-lectures-discrete-mathematics),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/30-lectures-discrete-mathematics/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-07.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA mathematics real-analysis lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2024,null,"Lecture 07 — Alternating Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/30-lectures-discrete-mathematics). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2024; 59 pages. Part of 30 Lectures in Discrete Mathematics. Sections: ec 9.2 Test of Convergence (Continued); ec 9.3 Alternating Series. Subsections include Integral Test, p-series Test, Comparison Test for Series, Limit Comparison Test, Telescope Series Test, Properties of Convergent Series, Alternative Series Test, and Absolute and Conditional Convergence. Slides cover Assignments1, Proof of Integral Test: Divergent Case, The series ∑∞, Comparison Test for Series, Limit Comparison Test, Telescope Series Test, Properties of Convergent Series, A numeric experiment, Alternating Series Test, and A Paradox?."
