  3094,The Classical Part of Quantum Mechanics,"https://gitlab.com/m-amin/conferences-and-workshops/-/blob/master/TC16-presentation.pdf",gitlab.com,math-ph,math-ph quant-ph math.PR hep-th physics mathematics mathematical-physics quantum-mechanics probability dynamics-and-vibrations slides talk gitlab,Mustafa Amin,2024,null,"The Classical Part of Quantum Mechanics. Beamer slides by Mustafa Amin, 2024; 16 pages. Part of Conferences and Workshops: A repository of my contributions (presentations, posters, etc.) to conferences and workshops. Slides cover Why would we want classical in the quantum, The classical within - Part I: The classical limit, Problems, The classical within - Part II: Coherent states, Too restrictive, A classical state corresponding to a quantum one, Where do classical probabilities come from?, How to calculate the classical probability?, The Van Vleck \"wavefunction\", Example: The harmonic oscillator, Example: With pictures, The quantum-classical difference, The classical/nonclassical decomposition, and C/NC decomposition in phase space (Wigner)."
