  3097,Integrating and querying data with AskOmics,"https://gitlab.com/odameron/eins2024/-/blob/main/askomicsTutorial/presentation/askomics-tutorial.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.DC,cs.DC math.CO computer-science mathematics distributed-systems graph-theory slides gitlab,Anthony Bretaudeau and Olivier Dameron and Olivier Filangi and Xavier Garnier and Fabrice Legeai,2024,null,"Integrating and querying data with AskOmics. Beamer tutorial slides by Anthony Bretaudeau, Olivier Dameron, Olivier Filangi, and Xavier Garnier (IRISA, France), 2024; 19 pages. From a repository described as: Material for the 2024 Interdisciplinary summer school on digital health (École d'été interdisciplinaire en numérique de la santé), Sherbrooke University. Sections: Integrating and querying data; What AskOmics is useful for. Subsections include Why it is difficult, Why RDF and SPARQL are relevant, Integrating data, and Querying data. Slides cover Data everywhere! (aka death by spreadsheet), Death by spreadsheet: the worst is yet to come!, Data are distributed, Data description involves hierarchies, Requirements, Linked Open Data (in 2009), Linked Open Data (in 2023), Linked Open Data, RDF principles, and RDF as a directed graph."
  3098,"Integrating, querying and reasoning on data and knowledge with Semantic Web technologies","https://gitlab.com/odameron/eins2024/-/blob/main/dameron2024eins.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.DS,cs.DS cs.LO math.CO math.HO computer-science mathematics algorithms formalization graph-theory slides gitlab,Olivier Dameron,2024,null,"Integrating, querying and reasoning on data and knowledge with Semantic Web technologies. Beamer slides by Olivier Dameron (Universit de Rennes), 2024; 67 pages. From a repository described as: Material for the 2024 Interdisciplinary summer school on digital health (École d'été interdisciplinaire en numérique de la santé), Sherbrooke University. Sections: Data, Knowledge and Reasoning in Life Science; Semantic Web: RDF for annotating data; Semantic Web: SPARQL for querying RDF; Semantic Web: RDFS and OWL for representing knowledge; Synthesis. Subsections include Life science data, Complexity, Metadata, Ontologies, Reasoning, Requirements, Linked (Open) Data, RDF principles, Exercice 1: understand an RDF graph, and RDF representation formats. Slides cover Before we begin, Life science from a data science perspective, Complexity of life science data and reasoning, Annotations (aka metadata) describe entities, Ontologies specify/formalize the meaning of annotations, Ontologies support reasoning about annotations, Requirements for coping with life science data complexity, There has to be a better way, Semantic Web and Linked (Open) Data, and RDF is not the problem, it is the solution."
  3099,"Calculus Review: 01204215 Differential Equations and Linear Algebra (parinya-ao/01204215-diffeq-linalg-slides)","https://gitlab.com/parinya-ao/01204215-diffeq-linalg-slides/-/blob/main/slides/01-calculus-review.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA math.DS math.RA math.NA mathematics real-analysis linear-algebra ode-and-dynamical-systems lecture-notes slides gitlab,Jittat Fakcharoenphol,2024,null,"Calculus Review: 01204215 Differential Equations and Linear Algebra (parinya-ao/01204215-diffeq-linalg-slides). Beamer slides by Jittat Fakcharoenphol (Kasetsart University), 2024; 42 pages. From the course-materials archive parinya-ao/01204215-diffeq-linalg-slides. Sections: Derivatives of key functions; Rules for derivatives; The Fundamental Theorem of Calculus; Taylor expansion. Slides cover Quick notes, First principle, Practice, Polynomials: $x^n$, Exponential function: $e^x$, Natural logarithm: $\\ln x$, Product rule: $(f\\cdot g)'=f\\cdot g' + g\\cdot f'$, Quotient rule and Chain rule, Antiderivatives, and Definite integrals."
