  3162,"Model Predictive Control: Part 1: Introduction","https://github.com/Rory-WeiCheng/ESE-619-Model-Predictive-Control/blob/main/Slides/01_introduction.pdf",github.com,eess.SY,eess.SY math.OC cs.AI cs.MA electrical-engineering mathematics computer-science control-theory ai-agents optimization cognitive-science slides github,Prof. Manfred Morari,2023,null,"Model Predictive Control: Part 1: Introduction. Beamer slides by Prof. Manfred Morari, 2023; 68 pages. From a repository described as: Copyright of the slides belongs to Professor Manfred Morari and his collaborators. Sections: Optimization based Control; Concept of MPC; Applications; History of MPC; Literature & Acknowledgements. Subsections include Ball on Plate, Path Following, Autonomous Quadrocopter Flight, Autonomous dNaNo Race Cars, Energy Efficient Building Control, Kite Power, Automotive Systems, Catalytic Cracker, and Predictive Control in NeuroScience. Slides cover Optimization in the loop, Optimization-Based Control: Motivation, Constraints in Control, MPC: Applications, Ball on Plate, Autonomous Quadrocopter Flight, Energy Efficient Building Control, Example: One-Zone Building, Kite Power, and Ford Autonomous Driving on Ice."
  3163,"Model Predictive Control: Part 2: system Theory Basics","https://github.com/Rory-WeiCheng/ESE-619-Model-Predictive-Control/blob/main/Slides/02_systemTheoryBasics.pdf",github.com,eess.SY,eess.SY cs.LG math.OC stat.ML electrical-engineering computer-science mathematics statistics control-theory machine-learning numerical-analysis slides github,Prof. Manfred Morari,2023,null,"Model Predictive Control: Part 2: system Theory Basics. Beamer slides by Prof. Manfred Morari, 2023; 60 pages. From a repository described as: Copyright of the slides belongs to Professor Manfred Morari and his collaborators. Sections: Models of Dynamic Systems; Analysis of LTI Discrete-Time Systems; Analysis of Nonlinear Discrete-Time Systems. Subsections include Nonlinear Time-Invariant Continuous-Time State Space Models, LTI Continuous-Time State Space Models, Time-Invariant, Discrete-Time, State Space Models, Stability, Observability & Controllability, Lyapunov Stability of LTI Discrete-Time Systems, and Example. Slides cover Goal: Introduce mathematical models to be used in Model Predictive, Nonlinear Time-Invariant Continuous-Time State, LTI Continuous-Time State Space Models (2/7), LTI Continuous-Time State Space Models (6/7), Time-Invariant, Discrete-Time, State Space, Exact Discretization of Linear Time-Invariant, Discrete Time Systems: Recap, Coordinate Transformations (2/2), Stability of Linear Systems (3/3), and Controllability (3/3)."
  3164,"Model Predictive Control: Part 3: model Uncertainty","https://github.com/Rory-WeiCheng/ESE-619-Model-Predictive-Control/blob/main/Slides/03_modelUncertainty.pdf",github.com,eess.SY,eess.SY math.ST math.OC stat.ME electrical-engineering mathematics statistics control-theory probability slides github,Prof. Manfred Morari,2023,null,"Model Predictive Control: Part 3: model Uncertainty. Beamer slides by Prof. Manfred Morari, 2023; 47 pages. From a repository described as: Copyright of the slides belongs to Professor Manfred Morari and his collaborators. Sections: Uncertainty Modeling; State Estimation. Subsections include Objective Statement, Stochastic Processes, Modeling using State Space Descriptions, Obtaining Models from First Principles, Obtaining Models from System Identification, Linear State Estimation, State Observer, and Kalman Filter. Slides cover Stochastic processes (2/2), Stationary Case (1/2), Nonstationary Case (2/2), Stationary Case, General Estimation Problem (2/2), Linear Estimator Structure, Estimation Error (3/3), State Observer (2/2), Kalman Filter Derivation (2/9), and Kalman Filter Derivation (5/9)."
  3165,"Model Predictive Control: Part 4: Optimization","https://github.com/Rory-WeiCheng/ESE-619-Model-Predictive-Control/blob/main/Slides/04_optimization.pdf",github.com,math.OC,math.OC cs.LG eess.SY mathematics computer-science electrical-engineering optimization convex-analysis control-theory real-analysis survey slides github,Prof. Manfred Morari,2023,null,"Model Predictive Control: Part 4: Optimization. Beamer slides by Prof. Manfred Morari, 2023; 135 pages. From a repository described as: Copyright of the slides belongs to Professor Manfred Morari and his collaborators. Sections: Convex Sets; Convex Functions; Convex Optimization Problems; Duality; Generalized Inequalities. Subsections include Motivation and Overview, Common Types of Optimization Problems, Definition and Examples, Set Operations, Definitions, Examples, Properties, Standard Convex Optimization Problem, Linear Programs, and Quadratic Programs. Slides cover Properties of Optimization Problems, “Easier” problems, Definitions: Hyperplanes and halfspaces, UnionX∪Y, Restriction to a Line, Convexity-preserving Operations (3/6), Optimality Criterion for Differentiablef (1/3), General Linear Program (LP), General Quadratic Program, and Example : Dual of a Linear Program (LP)."
  3166,"Model Predictive Control: Part 5: unconstrained Control","https://github.com/Rory-WeiCheng/ESE-619-Model-Predictive-Control/blob/main/Slides/05_unconstrainedControl.pdf",github.com,eess.SY,eess.SY math.OC electrical-engineering mathematics control-theory slides github,Prof. Manfred Morari,2023,null,"Model Predictive Control: Part 5: unconstrained Control. Beamer slides by Prof. Manfred Morari, 2023; 59 pages. From a repository described as: Copyright of the slides belongs to Professor Manfred Morari and his collaborators. Sections: Finite Horizon; Receding Horizon; Infinite Horizon. Subsections include Batch Approach, and Recursive Approach. Slides cover Optimal Control Introduction (1/2), Objectives, Solution via Recursive Approach (4/6), Linear Quadratic Optimal Control, Solution approach 1: Batch Approach (1/4), Solution approach 2: Recursive Approach (3/8), Solution approach 2: Recursive Approach (7/8), Example: Short horizonN = 5, and Example: Long horizonN = 20."
  3167,"Model Predictive Control: Part 6: CFTOC","https://github.com/Rory-WeiCheng/ESE-619-Model-Predictive-Control/blob/main/Slides/06_CFTOC.pdf",github.com,eess.SY,eess.SY math.OC electrical-engineering mathematics control-theory slides github,Prof. Manfred Morari,2023,null,"Model Predictive Control: Part 6: CFTOC. Beamer slides by Prof. Manfred Morari, 2023; 54 pages. From a repository described as: Copyright of the slides belongs to Professor Manfred Morari and his collaborators. Sections: Constrained Optimal Control; Basic Ideas of Predictive Control; Constrained Linear Optimal Control; Constrained Optimal Control: 2-Norm; Constrained Optimal Control: 1-Norm and Infinity-Norm; Receding Horizon Control Notation. Slides cover 1. Constrained Optimal Control, Objectives of Constrained Optimal Control, Limitations of Linear Controllers, Constrained Infinite Time Optimal Control, On-line Receding Horizon Control, 3. Constrained Linear Optimal Control, Feasible Sets, 4. Constrained Optimal Control: 2-Norm, Construction of QP constraints with substitution, and Construction of the QP without substitution."
  3168,"Model Predictive Control: Part 7: feasibility Stability","https://github.com/Rory-WeiCheng/ESE-619-Model-Predictive-Control/blob/main/Slides/07_feasibilityStability.pdf",github.com,eess.SY,eess.SY math.OC electrical-engineering mathematics control-theory slides github,Prof. Manfred Morari,2023,null,"Model Predictive Control: Part 7: feasibility Stability. Beamer slides by Prof. Manfred Morari, 2023; 67 pages. From a repository described as: Copyright of the slides belongs to Professor Manfred Morari and his collaborators. Sections: Receding Horizon Control and Model Predictive Control; Challenges: Feasibility and Stability; Guaranteeing Feasibility and Stability; Extension to Nonlinear MPC. Subsections include Proof for Xf= 0, General Terminal Sets, and Example. Slides cover Infinite Time Constrained Optimal Control, Example: LQR with saturation, Example: Inclusion of state constraints, Example: Loss of feasibility - Double Integrator, Example: Feasibility and stability are function of, Feasibility and stability in MPC - Solution, Stability of MPC - Zero terminal state constraint, Example: Impact of Horizon with Zero Terminal, Invariant sets, and Under those 3 assumptions."
  3169,"Model Predictive Control: Part 8: Invariance","https://github.com/Rory-WeiCheng/ESE-619-Model-Predictive-Control/blob/main/Slides/08_invariance.pdf",github.com,eess.SY,eess.SY math.OC math.CO electrical-engineering mathematics control-theory discrete-geometry slides github,Prof. Manfred Morari,2023,null,"Model Predictive Control: Part 8: Invariance. Beamer slides by Prof. Manfred Morari, 2023; 86 pages. From a repository described as: Copyright of the slides belongs to Professor Manfred Morari and his collaborators. Sections: Objectives of Constrained Control; Invariance; Controlled Invariance; Polytopes and Polytopic Computation; Ellipsoids and Invariance. Slides cover Constrained Control, Invariance: Which states are “good”?, Controlled Invariance: Does a good input exist?, Pre-Sets, Computing Invariant Sets, Conceptual Calculation of Control Invariant Sets, Computing Control Invariant Sets, Polyhedra, Most Common Polytopic Constraints, and Subset Test."
  3170,"Model Predictive Control: Part 9: Reachability","https://github.com/Rory-WeiCheng/ESE-619-Model-Predictive-Control/blob/main/Slides/09_reachability.pdf",github.com,eess.SY,eess.SY math.CO math.OC math.MG electrical-engineering mathematics control-theory discrete-geometry ai-agents slides github,Prof. Manfred Morari,2023,null,"Model Predictive Control: Part 9: Reachability. Beamer slides by Prof. Manfred Morari, 2023; 64 pages. From a repository described as: Copyright of the slides belongs to Professor Manfred Morari and his collaborators. Sections: Polyhedra and Polytopes; Reachable Sets; Invariant Sets; Reachability and Controllability – Robust Case. Subsections include General Set Definitions and Operations, Basic Operations on Polytopes, Pre and Reach Sets Definition, Pre and Reach Sets Computation, Controllable Sets, N-Step Reachable Sets, and Control Invariant Sets. Slides cover Polyhedra Representations, Special Polytopal Complexes, Basic Operations on Polytopes, Affine Mappings and Polyhedra, Set Definition, Pre Set Computation - Autonomous Systems, Control Invariant Sets, and Set Evolution ofKN(Xf )."
  3171,"Model Predictive Control: Part 10: practicalMPC","https://github.com/Rory-WeiCheng/ESE-619-Model-Predictive-Control/blob/main/Slides/10_practicalMPC.pdf",github.com,eess.SY,eess.SY math.OC electrical-engineering mathematics control-theory slides github,Prof. Manfred Morari,2023,null,"Model Predictive Control: Part 10: practicalMPC. Beamer slides by Prof. Manfred Morari, 2023; 26 pages. From a repository described as: Copyright of the slides belongs to Professor Manfred Morari and his collaborators. Sections: Reference Tracking; Soft Constraints; Generalizing the Problem. Subsections include The Steady-State Target Problem, RHC Reference Tracking without Offset, and Mathematical Formulation. Slides cover 1. Reference Tracking, Tracking problem, Steady-state Target Problem, RHC Reference Tracking, RHC Reference Tracking without Offset (1/6), RHC Reference Tracking without Offset (2/6), RHC Reference Tracking without Offset (3/6), RHC Reference Tracking without Offset (4/6), RHC Reference Tracking without Offset (5/6), and RHC Reference Tracking without Offset (6/6)."
  3172,"Model Predictive Control: Part 11: explicitMPC","https://github.com/Rory-WeiCheng/ESE-619-Model-Predictive-Control/blob/main/Slides/11_explicitMPC.pdf",github.com,eess.SY,eess.SY math.OC electrical-engineering mathematics control-theory slides github,Prof. Manfred Morari,2023,null,"Model Predictive Control: Part 11: explicitMPC. Beamer slides by Prof. Manfred Morari, 2023; 63 pages. From a repository described as: Copyright of the slides belongs to Professor Manfred Morari and his collaborators. Slides cover Problem Formulation - Quadratic Cost, 2-Norm State Feedback Solution, Problem Formulation - Piecewise Linear Cost, Explicit MPC, Logarithmic search (1/6), Logarithmic search (5/6), Ball and Plate, and Multi-Parametric Toolbox 3.0 Formulation."
  3173,"Model Predictive Control: Part 12: hybridMPC","https://github.com/Rory-WeiCheng/ESE-619-Model-Predictive-Control/blob/main/Slides/12_hybridMPC.pdf",github.com,eess.SY,eess.SY math.OC electrical-engineering mathematics control-theory algorithms optimization slides github,Prof. Manfred Morari,2023,null,"Model Predictive Control: Part 12: hybridMPC. Beamer slides by Prof. Manfred Morari, 2023; 42 pages. From a repository described as: Copyright of the slides belongs to Professor Manfred Morari and his collaborators. Sections: Modeling of Hybrid Systems; Optimal Control of Hybrid Systems; Model Predictive Control of Hybrid Systems; Explicit MPC of Hybrid Systems. Subsections include Examples of Hybrid Systems, Piecewise Affine (PWA) Systems, and Mixed Logical Dynamical (MLD) Hybrid Model. Slides cover 2. Optimal Control of Hybrid Systems, Binary States, Inputs, and Outputs, Analytic Approach, Switched Affine Dynamics, Hybrid Modelling - An Example, HYbrid System DEscription Language, Mixed Integer Linear Programming, Explicit MPC for Hybrid Systems. Quadratic Case, and MPC for Hybrid Systems - Complexity."
  3174,"Model Predictive Control: Part 13: robustMPC","https://github.com/Rory-WeiCheng/ESE-619-Model-Predictive-Control/blob/main/Slides/13_robustMPC.pdf",github.com,eess.SY,eess.SY math.OC electrical-engineering mathematics control-theory slides github,Prof. Manfred Morari,2023,null,"Model Predictive Control: Part 13: robustMPC. Beamer slides by Prof. Manfred Morari, 2023; 117 pages. From a repository described as: Copyright of the slides belongs to Professor Manfred Morari and his collaborators. Sections: Uncertainty Models; Impact of Bounded Additive Noise; Robust Open-Loop MPC; Closed-Loop Predictions; Tube-MPC; Nominal MPC with noise. Slides cover Lecture Take Homes, Examples of Common Uncertainty Models, Defining a Cost to Minimize, Reminder: Invariance, Computing Robust Invariant Sets, Uncertain State Evolution, Goals of Robust Constrained Control, System Decomposition, Constraint Tightening, and Putting it all together: Tube MPC."
  3175,"Model Predictive Control: Part 14: Numerical","https://github.com/Rory-WeiCheng/ESE-619-Model-Predictive-Control/blob/main/Slides/14_numerical.pdf",github.com,math.OC,math.OC eess.SY math.NA cs.LG mathematics electrical-engineering computer-science optimization control-theory numerical-analysis convex-analysis slides github,Prof. Manfred Morari,2023,null,"Model Predictive Control: Part 14: Numerical. Beamer slides by Prof. Manfred Morari, 2023; 80 pages. From a repository described as: Copyright of the slides belongs to Professor Manfred Morari and his collaborators. Sections: Unconstrained Optimization; Constrained Optimization; Software. Subsections include Gradient Methods, Newton's Method, Alternating Minimization Methods, Interior Point Methods, Modeling, Solvers for Desktop PCs, and Solvers for Embedded Platforms. Slides cover Recap: Convex Optimization Problems, Unconstrained Optimization Using Gradient, Gradient Method - Summary, Example: Quadratic lower bound on quadratic, Newton’s Method, Initial values: x (1), Constrained Minimization Using Gradient Methods, Sets that Allow Inexpensive Projections, Example: ADMM applied to QPs, and Barrier Method."
