  3189,Cryptography Principles,"https://github.com/YuZhang/cryptography/blob/master/pdf/0intro.pdf",github.com,cs.CR,cs.CR computer-science security-and-privacy mathematical-logic book slides github,Yu Zhang,2023,null,"Cryptography Principles. Beamer slides by Yu Zhang, 2023; 8 pages. From a repository described as: Yu Zhang, Harbin Insitute of Technology, 2011, 2012, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024. Slides cover What cryptography is and is not, Purposes, We will learn from Turing Award recipients, Syllabus [in Chinese], Textbooks, Slides, & Contact, and Grades."
  3190,"Introduction: Part 1","https://github.com/YuZhang/cryptography/blob/master/pdf/1introduction.pdf",github.com,cs.CR,cs.CR computer-science security-and-privacy algorithms history-of-mathematics slides github,Yu Zhang,2023,null,"Introduction: Part 1. Beamer slides by Yu Zhang, 2023; 32 pages. From a repository described as: Yu Zhang, Harbin Insitute of Technology, 2011, 2012, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024. Sections: Cryptography and Modern Cryptography; The Setting of Private-Key Encryption; Historical Ciphers and Their Cryptanalysis; The Basic Principles of Modern Cryptography. Slides cover What is Cryptography?, Changing the names would be easier, but if you’re not comfortable, Securing Key vs Obscuring Algorithm, Attack Scenarios, Caesar’s Cipher, Index of Coincidence (IC) Method (to findk), Attack with Statistical Patterns, Example of Frequency Analysis (Analysis), Vigenère (poly-alphabetic shift) Cipher, and Index of Coincidence (IC) Method (to findt)."
  3191,Perfectly Secret Encryption,"https://github.com/YuZhang/cryptography/blob/master/pdf/2perfectlysecret.pdf",github.com,cs.CR,cs.CR cs.IT math.IT computer-science mathematics security-and-privacy information-theory slides github,Yu Zhang,2023,null,"Perfectly Secret Encryption. Beamer slides by Yu Zhang, 2023; 20 pages. From a repository described as: Yu Zhang, Harbin Insitute of Technology, 2011, 2012, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024. Sections: Definitions and Basic Properties; The One-Time Pad (Vernam's Cipher); Limitations of Perfect Secrecy; Shannon's Theorem; Eavesdropping Indistinguishability. Slides cover Recall The Syntax of Encryption, Definition of ‘Perfect Secrecy’, Perfect Secrecy On One Bit, An Equivalent Formulation, Perfect Indistinguishability, One-Time Pad (Vernam’s Cipher), Limitations of OTP and Perfect Secrecy, Two Time Pad: Real World Cases, Shannon’s Theorem, and Application of Shannon’s Theorem."
  3192,Private-Key Encryption and Pseudorandomness (Part I),"https://github.com/YuZhang/cryptography/blob/master/pdf/3.1privatekey.pdf",github.com,cs.CR,cs.CR cs.CC math.AG computer-science mathematics security-and-privacy complexity-theory algebraic-geometry schemes slides github,Yu Zhang,2023,null,"Private-Key Encryption and Pseudorandomness (Part I). Beamer slides by Yu Zhang, 2023; 36 pages. From a repository described as: Yu Zhang, Harbin Insitute of Technology, 2011, 2012, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024. Sections: A Computational Approach to Cryptography; Defining Computationally-Secure Encryption; Pseudorandomness; Proof By Reduction; Constructing Secure Encryption Schemes. Slides cover Idea of Computational Security, Concrete Approach and Asymptotics, Efficient Computation, Asymptotic Approach, Defining Private-key Encryption Scheme, Defining Private-key Encryption Security, Semantic Security, Conceptual Points of Pseudorandomness, Intuition for Defining Pseudorandom, and Real World Cases."
  3193,Private-Key Encryption and Pseudorandomness (Part II),"https://github.com/YuZhang/cryptography/blob/master/pdf/3.2privatekey.pdf",github.com,cs.CR,cs.CR cs.CC computer-science security-and-privacy complexity-theory slides github,Yu Zhang,2023,null,"Private-Key Encryption and Pseudorandomness (Part II). Beamer slides by Yu Zhang, 2023; 42 pages. From a repository described as: Yu Zhang, Harbin Insitute of Technology, 2011, 2012, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024. Sections: Stream Ciphers And Chosen-Plaintext Attacks; CPA-Security From Pseudorandom Functions; Modes of Operation; Security Against Chosen-Ciphertext Attacks (CCA). Slides cover Stream Ciphers, Related Keys: Real World Cases, Attack On Deterministic Multiple Encryptions, Definition of CPA Security, Definition of Pseudorandom Function, Proof of CPA-Security from PRF, PRF, PRP, PRG, and Modes of Operation, Cipher Block Chaining (CBC) Mode, CTR Mode Is CPA-secure, and Non-deterministic Encryption."
  3194,Practical Constructions of Pseudorandom Permutations (Block Ciphers),"https://github.com/YuZhang/cryptography/blob/master/pdf/4blockcipher.pdf",github.com,math.RT,math.RT cs.CC cs.CR math.RA mathematics computer-science quiver-representations complexity-theory security-and-privacy slides github,Yu Zhang,2023,null,"Practical Constructions of Pseudorandom Permutations (Block Ciphers). Beamer slides by Yu Zhang, 2023; 42 pages. From a repository described as: Yu Zhang, Harbin Insitute of Technology, 2011, 2012, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024. Sections: Substitution-Permutation Networks; Feistel Networks; DES – The Data Encryption Standard; Increasing the Key Length of a Block Cipher; AES – The Advanced Encryption Standard; Differential and Linear Cryptanalysis – A Brief Look. Slides cover Block Ciphers, A Substitution-Permutation Network, A Framework for KPA against Block Ciphers, The Design of DES, An S-box in DES, Chronology of DES, The Meet-In-the-Middle Attack, ShangMi 4 (SM4): a block cipher “Information security, An Example of Linear Analysis ofS-box, and Differential Cryptanalysis."
  3195,Message Authentication Codes and Collision-Resistant Hash Functions,"https://github.com/YuZhang/cryptography/blob/master/pdf/6mac-crhf.pdf",github.com,cs.CR,cs.CR computer-science security-and-privacy slides github,Yu Zhang,2023,null,"Message Authentication Codes and Collision-Resistant Hash Functions. Beamer slides by Yu Zhang, 2023; 45 pages. From a repository described as: Yu Zhang, Harbin Insitute of Technology, 2011, 2012, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024. Sections: Message Authentication Codes (MAC) – Definitions; Constructing Secure MAC; CBC-MAC; Collision-Resistant Hash Functions; Hash-based MAC; Information-Theoretic MACs. Slides cover Integrity and Authentication, MAC Applications2, Proof of Secure MAC from PRF, Secure Variable-Length MAC, Defining Hash Function, Applications of Hash Functions, The Merkle-Damgård Transform, Cryptographic Hash Functions: SHA-1 and MD5, Nested MAC (NMAC), and Remarks on HMAC."
  3196,CCA-Secure and Authentication Encryption,"https://github.com/YuZhang/cryptography/blob/master/pdf/7cca-ae.pdf",github.com,cs.CR,cs.CR math.AG computer-science mathematics security-and-privacy algebraic-geometry schemes slides github,Yu Zhang,2023,null,"CCA-Secure and Authentication Encryption. Beamer slides by Yu Zhang, 2023; 27 pages. From a repository described as: Yu Zhang, Harbin Insitute of Technology, 2011, 2012, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024. Sections: Authenticated Encryptions; Deterministic Encryptions; Key Derivation Function. Slides cover Recall Security Against CCA, Message Transmission Scheme, Defining Secure Message Transmission, Combining Encryption and Authentication, Analyzing Security of Combinations, Constructing Authenticated Encryption Schemes, Proof of AE(/CCA-Secure) Encryption Schemes, Proof of “Pr[VQ] is negligible”, Proof of “Pr[PrivKcca, and Authenticated Encryption Theory and Practice."
  3197,Сравнение эффективности и скорости методов интерполяции при изменении размеров картинки,"https://github.com/amkatrutsa/nla2023_masters/blob/main/projects/project1/interpolation_pictures.pdf",github.com,math.NA,math.NA math.RA cs.NA mathematics computer-science linear-algebra numerical-analysis lecture-notes slides github,null,2023,null,"Сравнение эффективности и скорости методов интерполяции при изменении размеров картинки. Beamer slides, 2023; 24 pages, in Russian. Part of Numerical linear algebra course, AI Masters, Fall 2023. Slides cover Постановка задачи, Как измеряем качество, Интер по чему?, Методы интерполяции (неадаптивные), Тестовые картинки, Дальше экспериментируем с grayscale, Сравнение сложностей, Примеры [Nearest x3], Примеры [Nearest x10], Примеры [Bilinear x3], Примеры [Bilinear x10], Примеры [Bicubic x3], and Примеры [Bicubic x10]."
