  3215,"Backpropagation and the Chain Rule: Part 12: B Backpropagation","https://github.com/davidrosenberg/mlcourse/blob/gh-pages/Lectures/12b.backpropagation.pdf",github.com,math.CO,math.CO math.ST stat.ME mathematics statistics graph-theory lecture-notes slides github,null,2023,null,"Backpropagation and the Chain Rule: Part 12: B Backpropagation. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 24 pages. From the course-materials archive davidrosenberg/mlcourse. Sections: Partial Derivatives and the Chain Rule; Example: Least Squares Regression; Example: Ridge Regression; General Backpropagation. Slides cover Learning with Back-Propagation, Partial Derivatives, Partial Derivatives of an Affine Function, Chain Rule (in terms of partial derivatives), Review: Linear least squares, Computation Graph and Intermediate Variables, Partial Derivatives on Computation Graph, and Ridge Regression: Computation Graph and Intermediate Variables."
  3216,"EM Algorithm for Latent Variable Models: Part 13: c EM - algorithm","https://github.com/davidrosenberg/mlcourse/blob/gh-pages/Lectures/13c.EM-algorithm.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS computer-science algorithms lecture-notes slides github,null,2023,null,"EM Algorithm for Latent Variable Models: Part 13: c EM - algorithm. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 52 pages. From the course-materials archive davidrosenberg/mlcourse. Sections: Latent Variable Models; EM Algorithm (and Variational Methods) – The Big Picture; Math Prerequisites; The ELBO: Family of Lower Bounds on logp(x); Does EM Work?; Variations on EM; Summer Homework: Gaussian Mixture Model (Hints). Slides cover General Latent Variable Model, Log-Likelihood and Terminology, The Marginal Log-Likelihood Function, Supremum over Lower Bounds is a Lower Bound, The Expected Complete Data Log-Likelihood, Kullback-Leibler Divergence, The ELBO: Family of Lower Bounds on logp(x | θ), MLE, EM, and the ELBO, EM: Coordinate Ascent on Lower Bound, and General EM Algorithm."
  3217,Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lecture 1 — NLP tasks and evaluation,"https://github.com/dl4nlp-tuda/deep-learning-for-nlp-lectures/blob/main/pdf/dl4nlp2023-lecture01.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning ml-systems lecture-notes survey book slides github,Dr. Ivan Habernal,2023,null,"Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lecture 1 — NLP tasks and evaluation. Beamer lecture slides by Dr. Ivan Habernal, 2023; 58 pages. Part of Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lectures 2023: This repository contains slides for the course \"20-00-0947: Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing\" (Technical University of Darmstadt, Summer term 2023). Sections: Course logistics; Overview of typical NLP tasks; Evaluation; Recap. Subsections include Text classification tasks, Text generation tasks, Classification as generation, Evaluation of text classification, Evaluation of text generation, and Caveats of NLP benchmarking. Slides cover Text classification tasks, Why study deep learning for NLP?, Preliminary course roadmap, Textbooks and resources, Trustworthy Human Language Technologies, Side step 1: Gold standard data, NER: BIO encoding, BoolQ, Machine translation, and Classification as generation."
  3218,Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lecture 2 — Mathematical foundations of deep learning,"https://github.com/dl4nlp-tuda/deep-learning-for-nlp-lectures/blob/main/pdf/dl4nlp2023-lecture02.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning optimization lecture-notes slides github,Dr. Ivan Habernal,2023,null,"Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lecture 2 — Mathematical foundations of deep learning. Beamer lecture slides by Dr. Ivan Habernal, 2023; 65 pages. Part of Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lectures 2023: This repository contains slides for the course \"20-00-0947: Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing\" (Technical University of Darmstadt, Summer term 2023). Sections: Problem 1: Minimize functions; Problem 2: Minimize multivariate functions; Problem 3: When functions become heavily nested; Recap. Subsections include Efficient computation of gradient. Slides cover Efficient computation of gradient, Quick poll, How deep will we go?, Lines in two dimensions, Derivative-computing function, Chain rule example, Gradient-based optimization: Find minimum of a function, Multivariate functions, Gradient properties, and Problem 3: When functions."
  3219,"Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lecture 3 — Text classification 1: Log-linear models","https://github.com/dl4nlp-tuda/deep-learning-for-nlp-lectures/blob/main/pdf/dl4nlp2023-lecture03.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML math.NA math.RT computer-science statistics mathematics machine-learning numerical-analysis representation-theory large-language-models lecture-notes slides github,Dr. Ivan Habernal,2023,null,"Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lecture 3 — Text classification 1: Log-linear models. Beamer lecture slides by Dr. Ivan Habernal, 2023; 53 pages. Part of Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lectures 2023: This repository contains slides for the course \"20-00-0947: Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing\" (Technical University of Darmstadt, Summer term 2023). Sections: Feedback; The challenges of NLP; Towards supervised machine learning on text data; Numerical representation of natural language text; Binary text classification; Recap. Slides cover Thank you for your feedback!, Ambiguity and variability of human language, Language is symbolic and discrete, Data sparseness, Notation, Towards supervised classification setup, Numerical representation of, Tokens, Averaged bag-of-words example: x ∈R3,000, and Byte-pair encoding example on a toy corpus (part 1)."
  3220,"Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lecture 4 — Text classification 2: Deep neural networks","https://github.com/dl4nlp-tuda/deep-learning-for-nlp-lectures/blob/main/pdf/dl4nlp2023-lecture04.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning probability lecture-notes slides github,Dr. Ivan Habernal,2023,null,"Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lecture 4 — Text classification 2: Deep neural networks. Beamer lecture slides by Dr. Ivan Habernal, 2023; 38 pages. Part of Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lectures 2023: This repository contains slides for the course \"20-00-0947: Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing\" (Technical University of Darmstadt, Summer term 2023). Sections: Where we finished last time; Finding the best model's parameters; Log-linear multi-class classification; Loss function for softmax; Stacking transformations and non-linearity; Recap. Slides cover Finding the best model’s parameters, Our binary text classification function, Decision rule of log-linear model, The loss function, Binary cross-entropy loss (logistic loss), (Online) Stochastic Gradient Descent, Properties of Minibatch Stochastic Gradient Descent, From binary to multi-class labels, Projecting input vector to output vector f (x) : Rdin →Rdout, and Log-linear multi-class."
  3221,"Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lecture 5 — Text generation 1: Language models and word embeddings","https://github.com/dl4nlp-tuda/deep-learning-for-nlp-lectures/blob/main/pdf/dl4nlp2023-lecture05.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG cs.CL stat.ML cs.AI computer-science statistics machine-learning large-language-models probability category-theory lecture-notes slides github,Dr. Ivan Habernal,2023,null,"Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lecture 5 — Text generation 1: Language models and word embeddings. Beamer lecture slides by Dr. Ivan Habernal, 2023; 43 pages. Part of Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lectures 2023: This repository contains slides for the course \"20-00-0947: Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing\" (Technical University of Darmstadt, Summer term 2023). Sections: The story so far; Today: Language models and word embeddings; Language models; Word embeddings; Recap. Subsections include Recap 1: MLP and non-linearity, Recap 2: Embedding categorical features, Probability refresher, `Classical' language models, and Neural language models. Slides cover Recap 1: MLP and non-linearity, Recap: Log-linear model for binary classification, Recap: Stacking linear layers is still a linear model, Figure 4: XOR solvable with, e.g., ReLU, Recap: Matrix W as learned representation — rows, Probability refresher, Probability refresher 3, Language models formally, Evaluating language models: Perplexity, and Neural LMs."
  3222,"Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lecture 5 — Text classification 3: Learning word embeddings","https://github.com/dl4nlp-tuda/deep-learning-for-nlp-lectures/blob/main/pdf/dl4nlp2023-lecture06.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning large-language-models lecture-notes slides talk github,Dr. Ivan Habernal,2023,null,"Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lecture 5 — Text classification 3: Learning word embeddings. Beamer lecture slides by Dr. Ivan Habernal, 2023; 46 pages. Part of Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing - Lectures 2023: This repository contains slides for the course \"20-00-0947: Deep Learning for Natural Language Processing\" (Technical University of Darmstadt, Summer term 2023). Sections: Recap: Neural LMs learn word embeddings; We need to talk about the dot product; Distributional hypothesis; From neural LMs to training word embeddings; word2vec; FastText embeddings: Sub-word embeddings; Advantages and limitations of words embeddings; Recap. Slides cover Recap: Neural LMs learn word, Neural language model, context = 3 preceding words, We need to talk about the dot, Recall: One-hot encoding of words, Count-based methods, From neural language models to training word embeddings, Negative sampling, Final CBOW word2vec — similarity score is the dot product, Skip-Gram — even more relaxed context notion, and FastText embeddings."
