  3302,Lecture 18— Trees (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-01/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-18.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics graph-theory combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 18— Trees (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 41 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-01): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: DM 4.2 Trees; ac 5.6 Counting Labelled Trees — Cayley's formula; Generating functions and labelled trees. Subsections include Rooted Trees, Spanning Trees, and A Proof Using Prüfer code. Slides cover Rooted Trees, A rooted trees, Speed dating, More bipartite graphs, Every is a bipartite graph!, Spanning trees, Think-Pair-Share, The number of of small sizes, Theorem 5.39 (ac) — Cayley’s formula, and Bijection proof."
  3303,Lecture 19 — Eulerian and Hamiltonian Graphs - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-01/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-19.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.SG mathematics graph-theory symplectic-geometry algorithms lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 19 — Eulerian and Hamiltonian Graphs - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 32 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-01): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 5.3 Eulerian and Hamiltonian Graphs. Subsections include Eulerian Graphs, and Hamiltonian Graphs. Slides cover A walk with Euler, The 一笔画problem, Eulerian graphs, Is this eulerian?, Theorem 5.13 (ac) — Euler’s theory, Finding an eulerian circuit, A graph with odd degrees?, The algorithm to find an eulerian circuit (1), Think-Pair-Share, and Let’s deliver some packages."
