  3305,Lecture 21 — Graph Colouring (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-01/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-21.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.AT mathematics graph-theory chromatic-homotopy-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 21 — Graph Colouring (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 39 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-01): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 5.4.2 Cliques and Chromatic Number. Subsections include Proof of Proposition 5.25 (ac) by J. Mycielski, and Proof of Proposition 5.25 (ac) by J. Kelly and L. Kelly. Slides cover Warming up, Cliques, Chromatic number ≥clique number, What is ω(C5) and χ(C5)? What about C2n+1?, A bit more, Proposition 5.25 (ac), Base case, Proof by contradiction —, Construct Gt+1, and Think-Pair-Share."
