  3307,Lecture 24 — Ramsey's Theory - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-01/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-24.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics extremal-combinatorics graph-theory combinatorics large-language-models lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 24 — Ramsey's Theory - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 42 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-01): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 11 Applying Probability to Combinatorics. Subsections include 11.1 A First Taste of Ramsey Theory, 11.2 Small Ramsey Numbers, 11.3 Estimate Ramsey Number, 11.5 Ramsey’s Theorem, and Extremal Graph Theory. Slides cover Six students come to the class, More examples, Theorem 11.2 (ac) — Ramsey’s theory for graphs, Proof of Theorem 11.2, Small Ramsey Numbers, Stirling’s approximation, Theorem 11.6 (ac) — Ramsey’s theory for 3 colours, Theorem 11.6 (ac) — Ramsey’s theory beyond, Pál Turán, and A Poem of Graphs — by ChatGPT."
  3308,Lecture 25 — Sequences and limits - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-01/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-25.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA math.HO physics.hist-ph mathematics physics real-analysis philosophy-of-mathematics lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 25 — Sequences and limits - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 44 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-01): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: Why should we know real analysis?; bai 1.2 The set of real numbers; bai 2.1 Sequences and limits. Subsections include 2.1.1 Monotone sequences. Slides cover Quick-sort, Example of big O, Back to Quick-sort, Infinity is weird, Examples of supreme, Definition 1.1.2 — Lower bound and Infimum, Think-Pair-Share, Examples of sequences, Example of convergence, and Is the sequence ൲."
  3309,"Lecture 26 — Limit superior, limit inferior - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science","https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-01/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-26.pdf",gitlab.com,math.LO,math.LO math.CA mathematics mathematical-logic real-analysis lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 26 — Limit superior, limit inferior - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 32 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-01): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: bai 2.1 Sequences and limits; Story Time — Wittgenstein and Turing; bai 2.3 Limit superior, limit inferior, and Bolzano–Weierstrass. Subsections include 2.1.3 Subsequences, and 2.3.2 Using limit inferior and limit superior. Slides cover 2.1.3 Subsequences, Proposition 2.1.17 — Convergence of subsequence, Story Time — Wittgenstein and, Wittgenstein’s on math, A conversation between Turing and Wittgenstein, Turing’s conclusion, Definition 2.3.1 — Limit superior/inferior, Proposition 2.3.2 — Properties of lim sup and lim inf, Example, and Theorem 2.3.4 — The nice subsequences."
  3310,Lecture 27 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2023-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-01/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-27.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA math-ph mathematics physics asymptotics-and-resummation lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 27 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2023-01). Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 32 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-01): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: bai 2.4 Cauchy sequences; Story Time — Sum of divergent series; bai 2.5 Series. Subsections include 2.5.1 Definition, 2.5.2 Cauchy series, and 2.5.3 Basic properties. Slides cover Augustin-Louis Cauchy, Proposition 2.4.4 — Cauchy sequences are bounded, Theorem 2.4.5 — Cauchy sequences are convergent, Ramanujan summation, Check out this film!, 2.5.1 Definition, Example, Proposition 2.5.5 — How many do we need?, 2.5.2 Cauchy series, and Proposition 2.5.8 — Is this series Cauchy?."
  3311,Lecture 28 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2023-01),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-01/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-28.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA cs.CL cs.AI cs.LG mathematics computer-science real-analysis large-language-models lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 28 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2023-01). Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 24 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-01): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: bai 2.5 Series; Story Time — ChatGPT for math?. Subsections include 2.5.4 Absolute convergence, 2.5.5 Comparison test and the p-series, and 2.5.6 Ratio test. Slides cover 2.5.4 Absolute convergence, Proposition 2.5.13 — When xn≥0, Definition 2.5.14 — Converge Absolutely, Proposition 2.5.15, Converge conditionally, 2.5.5 Comparison test and the p-series, Proposition 2.5.16 — Comparison test, Proposition 2.5.17 — p-test, The series ∑, and 2.5.6 Ratio test."
  3312,Lecture 03 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2023-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-03.pdf",gitlab.com,math.LO,math.LO math.PR mathematics mathematical-logic random-matrix-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 03 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2023-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 41 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-08): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: dm 3.1 Propositional Logic. Subsections include Truth Tables, Xor — Exclusive-or, Logical Equivalence, Deductions — How to argue with logic, and Beyond Propositions. Slides cover Propositions, Example, Truth tables, The Monopoly problem, Xor — Exclusive-or, An application of Xor — Knights and knaves, Think-Pair-Share, Logical equivalence, Basic logic equivalence, and Verifying equivalence."
