  3324,Lecture 18 — Eulerian and Hamiltonian Graphs - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-18.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.SG mathematics graph-theory symplectic-geometry algorithms lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 18 — Eulerian and Hamiltonian Graphs - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 48 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-08): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 5.3 Eulerian and Hamiltonian Graphs. Subsections include Eulerian Graphs, and Hamiltonian Graphs. Slides cover The 7️⃣-bridges problem, Eulerian Graphs, Theorem 5.13 (ac) — Euler’s Theory, The algorithm to find an eulerian circuit, The first example, A graph with odd degrees?, Let’s deliver some packages, Hamiltonian Graphs, Hamiltonian property in complete bipartite graphs, and Floor and Ceiling Functions."
  3325,Lecture 19 — Graph Colouring (1) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-19.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.AT mathematics graph-theory chromatic-homotopy-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 19 — Graph Colouring (1) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 30 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-08): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 5.4 Graph Colouring. Subsections include Motivational Example, Chromatic Number, Chromatic Number of Specific Graphs, Chromatic Number of Cycles, and Chromatic Number of Bipartite Graphs. Slides cover Motivational Example, Colours to help, Colouring to help again, Chromatic Number, Nature of colours, Independent Graphs, Star graphs, Cycles, Odd cycle, and A wedding puzzle."
  3326,Lecture 20 — Graph Colouring (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-20.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.AT mathematics graph-theory chromatic-homotopy-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 20 — Graph Colouring (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 36 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-08): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 5.4.2 Cliques and Chromatic Number. Subsections include Cliques and Clique Number, Proof of Proposition 5.25 (ac) by J. Mycielski, and Proof of Proposition 5.25 (ac) by J. Kelly and L. Kelly. Slides cover Cliques, Cliques in graphs, A lower bound of the chromatic number, A bit more, For every t≥3, there exists a graph Gtso that χ(Gt) = tand, Proof of Proposition 5.25 (ac) by J. Mycielski — A sketch, How to construct Gt+1, Example: Construct G4, Verify Gt+1 is -free, and A lower bound of χ(Gt+1)."
  3327,Lecture 21 – Graph Colouring (3) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-21.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO cs.DS math.AT mathematics computer-science graph-theory algorithms chromatic-homotopy-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 21 – Graph Colouring (3) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 43 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-08): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 5.4.3 Can We Determine Chromatic Number?. Subsections include First-Fit Algorithm, Maximum Degrees and Chromatic Numbers, Interval Graphs, Independent number, and Perfect Graphs. Slides cover Example: First-fit algorithm, Theorem 4.4.5 (dm): Brook’s Theorem, Interval graphs, Review: Independent Graphs, Independence number, Think-Pair-Share, Example: Interval graphs, The Strong Perfect Graph Theorem, and Example: Complete graphs."
  3328,Lecture 22 — Planar Graphs - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-22.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics graph-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 22 — Planar Graphs - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 39 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-08): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 5.5 Planar Graphs. Subsections include Definitions of Planar Graphs, Euler's Formula, Is this graph planar? — A Simple Check, Is this graph planar? – Kuratowski's Theorem, and Four colour theorem. Slides cover Definitions of Planar Graphs, Planar graphs, Euler’s Formula, Faces of a planar graph, Faces, edges, and vertices, Induction step, Think-Pair-Share, Edges and faces, Proof that K3,3 is not planar, and Elementary subdivision."
  3329,Lecture 23 — Probability and Graph Theory (1) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-23.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.PR mathematics graph-theory extremal-combinatorics probability lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 23 — Probability and Graph Theory (1) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 33 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-08): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 11.1 A First Taste of Ramsey Theory; ac 11.2 Small Ramsey Numbers; ac 11.5 Ramsey's Theorem. Subsections include A Six-student Lemma, and Ramsey's Theory for Graphs. Slides cover Let’s try it out, Some possible edge colouring of K6, Let Gbe any graph with 6 vertices. Then Gcontains either a K3, Having six vertices is necessary, Theorem 11.2 (ac) — Ramsey’s theory for graphs, Proof of Theorem 11.2, A recursive inequality, Erdős and Ramsey numbers, and Another bet."
  3330,Lecture 24 — Probability and Graph Theory (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-24.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.PR mathematics graph-theory probability extremal-combinatorics probabilistic-combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 24 — Probability and Graph Theory (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 26 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-08): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ac 11.3 Estimate Ramsey Number; ac 11.4 Applying Probability to Ramsey Theory; The Probabilistic Method; Extremal Graph Theory. Slides cover Small numbers versus large numbers, Big Oand small oNotation, Stirling’s approximation, Estimate Ramsey Number, Theorem 11.4: A Lower Bound for the Ramsey Number, Proof Sketch, and Where is the Probability?."
  3331,Lecture 25 — Sequences and Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-25.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA mathematics real-analysis lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 25 — Sequences and Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 31 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-08): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ec 9.1 Infinite Sequence and Series. Subsections include Sequences, Series, and Continued Fractions. Slides cover Elementary Calculus (ec) 9.1 Infinite, An intuitive answer, Review: limit of function, Limit of sequence, Example 9.1, Recall from calculus that, Review: L’Hôpital’s Rule, Example 9.3, Golden Ratio, and Series."
  3332,Lecture 26 — Test of Convergence - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-26.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA mathematics real-analysis lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 26 — Test of Convergence - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 40 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-08): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ec 9.2 Test of Convergence. Slides cover Elementary Calculus (ec) 9.2 Test of, Impact of Finite Changes on Limits, Bounded Sequence, Monotone Sequence, Monotone Bounded Test, Example 7.9, Comparison Test, Ratio Test, Integral Test, and Comparison Test for Convergence."
  3333,Lecture 27 — Alternating Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-27.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA mathematics real-analysis lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 27 — Alternating Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 15 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-08): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ec 9.3 Alternating Series. Slides cover Elementary Calculus (ec) 9.3, The First Example, A numeric experiment, Alternating Series Test, Example 9.14, Conditional Convergence, Absolute Convergence, Absolute Convergence Test, A Paradox?, and Riemann’s Rearrangement Theorem."
  3334,Lecture 28 — Power Series and Taylor Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-28.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA math.CO mathematics real-analysis combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Lecture 28 — Power Series and Taylor Series - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 28 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-08): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: ec 9.4 Power Series; ec 9.5 Taylor Series. Slides cover Elementary Calculus (ec) 9.4 Power, Power Series, Radius of Convergence, Power Series and Generating Functions, Example 9.16, Example 9.18, Differentiation and Integration, Elementary Calculus (ec) 9.5 Taylor, Taylor’s formula, and Why do we both with Taylor series?."
  3335,Welcome - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2023-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2023-08/-/blob/main/pdf/welcome.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.LO mathematics combinatorics graph-theory mathematical-logic lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2023,null,"Welcome - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2023-08). Beamer slides, 2023; 15 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (2023-08): This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University. Sections: Why are you here?; What is Discrete Mathematics?; A few important things. Slides cover Why are you taking this course?, Why I think you should take this course?, Discrete Mathematics: A Buffet of Topics, 1. Logic, 2. Combinatorics, 3. Graph Theory, 4. Sequences and Series, What you need to know, What you definitely need to know, and Emoji."
