  3381,Chapter 1 Introduction (ofec-release/io-slides),"https://gitlab.com/ofec-release/io-slides/-/blob/main/chp%201/chp1.pdf",gitlab.com,math.OC,math.OC cs.LG cs.DS mathematics computer-science optimization algorithms machine-learning book slides gitlab,Changhe Li,2023,null,"Chapter 1 Introduction (ofec-release/io-slides). Beamer lecture slides by Changhe Li, 2023; 25 pages. Part of IO Slides: To make it easy for you to get started with GitLab, here's a list of recommended next steps. Sections: Optimization and Machine Learning; Optimization Problems; Optimization Algorithms. Subsections include What is AI?, What about optimization?, Mathematical Formulation, Continuous Optimization versus Discrete Optimization, and Intelligent Optimization Techniques. Slides cover 1.1.2 What about optimization?, 1.1.2 What about Optimization?, 2.2.1 Mathematical Formulation, 1.2.2 Continuous Optimization versus Discrete Optimization, 1.3.1 Deterministic Algorithms and Probabilistic Algorithms, and 1.3.2 Intelligent Optimization Techniques."
