  3383,Chapter 3 Canonical Optimization Algorithms,"https://gitlab.com/ofec-release/io-slides/-/blob/main/chp%203/chp3.pdf",gitlab.com,math.OC,math.OC cs.DS cs.LG math.CT mathematics computer-science optimization algorithms descent-theory numerical-analysis book slides gitlab,Changhe Li,2023,null,"Chapter 3 Canonical Optimization Algorithms. Beamer lecture slides by Changhe Li, 2023; 34 pages. Part of IO Slides: To make it easy for you to get started with GitLab, here's a list of recommended next steps. Sections: Numerical Optimization Algorithms; State Space Search; Single-solution-based Random Search. Subsections include Line Search, Steepest Descent Method, Newton Method, Conjugate Gradient Method, State Space, Uniformed Search, Informed Search, and Simulated Annealing Algorithm. Slides cover 3.1.1 Line search, 3.1.2 Steepest Descent Method, 3.1.3 Newton Method, 3.1.4 Conjugate Gradient Method, 3.2 State Space Search, 3.2.1.1 The Shortest Path Problem, 3.2.1.2 The Shortest Path Problem, 3.2.1 State Space, 3.2.2.1 Breadth-First Search (BFS), and 3.2.2.2 Depth-First Search (DFS)."
  3384,Chapter 4 Basics of Evolutionary Computation Algorithms,"https://gitlab.com/ofec-release/io-slides/-/blob/main/chp%204/chp4.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.DS,cs.DS q-bio.GN q-bio.QM computer-science quantitative-biology algorithms bioinformatics book slides gitlab,Changhe Li,2023,null,"Chapter 4 Basics of Evolutionary Computation Algorithms. Beamer lecture slides by Changhe Li, 2023; 37 pages. Part of IO Slides: To make it easy for you to get started with GitLab, here's a list of recommended next steps. Sections: Solution Representation; Selection; Reproduction; Applications. Subsections include 4.1.1 Biological Evolution, 4.1.2 Biological Evolution and Evolutionary Algorithms, 4.1.3 Basic Evolutionary Process, 4.1.4 Developments, 4.2.1 Binary Representation, 4.2.2 Integer Representation, 4.2.3 Real-valued Representation, 4.2.4 Tree Representation, 4.2.5 The Effect of Representation, and 4.3.1 Mating and Survivor Selection. Slides cover 4.1 Biological Evolution, 4.1.2 Biological Evolution and Evolutionary Algorithms, 4.1.3 Basic Evolutionary Process, 4.1.4 EC Family Development, 4.2.1 Binary Representation, 4.2.2 Integer Representation, 4.2.3 Real-valued Representation, 4.2.4 Tree Representation, 4.2.5 The Effect of Representation, and 4.3.1 Mating and Survivor Selection."
