  3391,"Welcome and Overview: NBER Heterogeneous-Agent Macro Workshop (prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023)","https://gitlab.com/prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023/-/blob/main/Lectures/Lecture%200%20Welcome%20and%20Overview.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AI,cs.AI cs.MA cs.SE computer-science ai-agents philosophy-of-mathematics lecture-notes survey slides talk gitlab,null,2023,null,"Welcome and Overview: NBER Heterogeneous-Agent Macro Workshop (prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023). Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 8 pages. Part of Spring 2023 NBER Workshop: This repo contains code for the tutorials of the Spring 2023 heterogeneous-agent macro workshop at the NBER taught by Adrien Auclert, Bence Bardóczy, Matt Rognlie, and Ludwig Straub. Slides cover Welcome, Workshop objectives, Applications of the heterogeneous agent modeling framework, Working in the sequence space, Modeling philosophy, and Course material."
  3392,"Information frictions: NBER Heterogeneous-Agent Macro Workshop","https://gitlab.com/prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023/-/blob/main/Lectures/Lecture%2010%20Information%20slides.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AI,cs.AI cs.MA cs.SE computer-science ai-agents slides talk gitlab,null,2023,null,"Information frictions: NBER Heterogeneous-Agent Macro Workshop. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 70 pages. Part of Spring 2023 NBER Workshop: This repo contains code for the tutorials of the Spring 2023 heterogeneous-agent macro workshop at the NBER taught by Adrien Auclert, Bence Bardóczy, Matt Rognlie, and Ludwig Straub. Sections: Introductory example; Information frictions in the sequence space; Examples; Takeaway. Slides cover Today, Problem, Monetary policy revisited, Manipulating the Jacobians, Solving behavioral IKC, Some general assumptions we’ll make, Separable vs non-separable deviations from FIRE, General Jacobian manipulation, Intuition, and Next, we’ll walk through examples from the literature."
  3393,"The canonical HANK model: NBER Heterogeneous-Agent Macro Workshop (prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023)","https://gitlab.com/prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023/-/blob/main/Lectures/Lecture%204%20Canonical%20HANK%20slides.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AI,cs.AI cs.MA cs.SE computer-science ai-agents condensed-mathematics slides talk gitlab,null,2023,null,"The canonical HANK model: NBER Heterogeneous-Agent Macro Workshop (prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023). Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 48 pages. Part of Spring 2023 NBER Workshop: This repo contains code for the tutorials of the Spring 2023 heterogeneous-agent macro workshop at the NBER taught by Adrien Auclert, Bence Bardóczy, Matt Rognlie, and Ludwig Straub. Sections: The canonical HANK model; Three instructive special cases; Solving the model using blocks and DAGs. Slides cover This session, Introducing the canonical HANK model, Unions and sticky wages, Production, Government: Monetary policy, Representative-agent model, Two-agent model, Zero-liquidity model, Solving the model using blocks and, and Defining blocks and models."
  3394,"Fiscal Policy: NBER Heterogeneous-Agent Macro Workshop (prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023)","https://gitlab.com/prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023/-/blob/main/Lectures/Lecture%205%20Fiscal%20Policy%20slides.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AI,cs.AI cs.MA cs.SE math.CA computer-science mathematics ai-agents harmonic-analysis linear-algebra slides talk gitlab,null,2023,null,"Fiscal Policy: NBER Heterogeneous-Agent Macro Workshop (prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023). Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 65 pages. Part of Spring 2023 NBER Workshop: This repo contains code for the tutorials of the Spring 2023 heterogeneous-agent macro workshop at the NBER taught by Adrien Auclert, Bence Bardóczy, Matt Rognlie, and Ludwig Straub. Sections: The intertemporal Keynesian cross; Three special cases; iMPCs in the HA model; Insights about Fiscal Multipliers; Takeaway. Slides cover This session, Roadmap, Intertemporal MPCs, Rewrite equation (1) in vector / matrix notation, Solving the intertemporal Keynesian cross, The balanced budget multiplier, Representative-agent model, Fiscal policy in RA model, Two agent model, and Fiscal policy in TA model."
  3395,"Monetary policy: NBER Heterogeneous-Agent Macro Workshop (prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023)","https://gitlab.com/prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023/-/blob/main/Lectures/Lecture%206%20Monetary%20policy%20slides.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AI,cs.AI math.AG cs.MA cs.SE computer-science mathematics ai-agents derived-algebraic-geometry condensed-mathematics ml-systems survey slides talk gitlab,null,2023,null,"Monetary policy: NBER Heterogeneous-Agent Macro Workshop (prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023). Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 73 pages. Part of Spring 2023 NBER Workshop: This repo contains code for the tutorials of the Spring 2023 heterogeneous-agent macro workshop at the NBER taught by Adrien Auclert, Bence Bardóczy, Matt Rognlie, and Ludwig Straub. Sections: Review of monetary policy in the standard NK model; Monetary policy in the canonical HANK model; Direct and indirect effects of monetary policy; Cyclical income risk; Takeaway. Slides cover Class plan, Roadmap, Monetary propagation in the NK model, Setting up the model, DAG of this model, DAG including the valuation block, Jacobians again, Benchmark result with zero liquidity, Neutrality for monetary policy in the ZL limit, and Direct and indirect effects."
  3396,"Monetary policy topics: NBER Heterogeneous-Agent Macro Workshop","https://gitlab.com/prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023/-/blob/main/Lectures/Lecture%207%20Monetary%20policy%20topics%20slides.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AI,cs.AI cs.MA cs.SE computer-science ai-agents slides talk gitlab,null,2023,null,"Monetary policy topics: NBER Heterogeneous-Agent Macro Workshop. Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 36 pages. Part of Spring 2023 NBER Workshop: This repo contains code for the tutorials of the Spring 2023 heterogeneous-agent macro workshop at the NBER taught by Adrien Auclert, Bence Bardóczy, Matt Rognlie, and Ludwig Straub. Sections: Maturity structure; Nominal assets; Fiscal policy; Investment; Takeaway. Slides cover What’s next, Roadmap, Longer maturities, Steady state and dynamics, Impulse responses with longer maturities, Incorporating unexpected revaluation, Aggregate implication of Fisher channel: AR(1) shock to r, Fiscal-monetary interactions, Setting up a fiscal rule, and No investment so far. Let’s change this!."
  3397,"Estimating HANK: NBER Heterogeneous-Agent Macro Workshop (prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023)","https://gitlab.com/prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023/-/blob/main/Lectures/Lecture%208%20Estimating%20HANK%20slides.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AI,cs.AI cs.MA cs.SE math.CO computer-science mathematics ai-agents probabilistic-combinatorics control-theory graph-theory slides talk gitlab,null,2023,null,"Estimating HANK: NBER Heterogeneous-Agent Macro Workshop (prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023). Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 44 pages. Part of Spring 2023 NBER Workshop: This repo contains code for the tutorials of the Spring 2023 heterogeneous-agent macro workshop at the NBER taught by Adrien Auclert, Bence Bardóczy, Matt Rognlie, and Ludwig Straub. Sections: Quick recap on estimating state-space models; Estimating models in the sequence space; Estimating HANK. Slides cover Today, Roadmap, What do we get from the state space representation?, Estimating het-agent models in the state space, Estimating models in the sequence, Impulse response matching, Second moments, minimum distance estimation, Obtaining second moments, Covariance decomposition, and Likelihood function."
  3398,Discrete choice with extreme-value taste shocks (prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023),"https://gitlab.com/prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023/-/blob/main/Lectures/Lecture%209%20Discrete%20Choice.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AI,cs.AI q-fin.RM cs.MA cs.SE computer-science quantitative-finance ai-agents economics-and-finance slides talk gitlab,null,2023,null,"Discrete choice with extreme-value taste shocks (prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2023). Beamer lecture slides, 2023; 38 pages. Part of Spring 2023 NBER Workshop: This repo contains code for the tutorials of the Spring 2023 heterogeneous-agent macro workshop at the NBER taught by Adrien Auclert, Bence Bardóczy, Matt Rognlie, and Ludwig Straub. Sections: SIM with labor force participation; Solving the SIM model with participation; General framework; Jacobians with discrete choice. Slides cover Today, Why is discrete choice hard?, Roadmap, SIM model with labor force participation, Economics of the model, Stages, Stage 3: continuous choice, EGM + upper envelope, Stage 2: discrete choice, and Stage 1: discrete shock."
