  3522,Introduction to machine learning - Victor Kitov (yandexdataschool/MLatImperial2022),"https://github.com/yandexdataschool/MLatImperial2022/blob/main/Lectures/01-Introduction%20to%20ML.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML math.ST computer-science statistics mathematics machine-learning software-engineering lecture-notes survey slides github,null,2022,null,"Introduction to machine learning - Victor Kitov (yandexdataschool/MLatImperial2022). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 72 pages. Part of Machine Learning & Deep Learning Course at ICL: Alternatively you can open Seminars/00-Welcome.ipynb locally on your computer via Jupyter notebook. Sections: Problem statement; Visual examples; Function class; Function estimation; Notation used in the course. Subsections include Supervised learning, Unsupervised learning, Separate validation set, Cross-validation, and A/B testing. Slides cover Relevance, Formal definitions of machine learning, Types of features, Supervised learning, Unsupervised learning, Linear function class, Loss function L(by, y), Types of learning, Estimation of empirical risk, and Separate validation set."
