  3546,History of Game Console Security,"https://gitlab.com/Jnunez101/jnunez-presentations/-/blob/main/console-security-oresec-talk/slides.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.CR,cs.CR math.HO computer-science mathematics security-and-privacy history-of-mathematics slides talk gitlab,null,2022,null,"History of Game Console Security. Beamer talk slides, 2022; 56 pages. From a repository described as: A repo of all my presentations for LUG, and ORESEC. Sections: lug.mines.edu/attend; What consoles?; early security; A break from security let's see what Nintendo has been doing!; Back to Actual Security. Slides cover Consoles, Why secure consoles?, Why is piracy such a big problem?, The light cube, NES Cont, Graphic Cont, Nintendo 64, Gamecube!!!, Small Disc, and DREAM!!cast."
  3547,"Welcome to LUG: What is Linux?, A kernel!","https://gitlab.com/Jnunez101/jnunez-presentations/-/blob/main/lug-intro-presentations/LUG-INTRO-REDONE/slides.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.OS,cs.OS computer-science operating-systems slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Welcome to LUG: What is Linux?, A kernel!. Beamer slides, 2022; 64 pages. From a repository described as: A repo of all my presentations for LUG, and ORESEC. Sections: What is Linux?; A kernel!; Why Linux?; Lets look at my laptop(Demo). Slides cover Who are we?, What do we do?, A typical meeting, Previous talks!, Kernels, What makes Linux special?, Open Source, Linux Kernel Code!, Distros, and Installing Software."
  3548,Ecaping the PS4,"https://gitlab.com/Jnunez101/jnunez-presentations/-/blob/main/ps2-escape-ps4/slides.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.CR,cs.CR computer-science security-and-privacy slides gitlab,"Jesus Nu\\ nez",2022,null,"Ecaping the PS4. Beamer slides by Jesus Nu\\ nez, 2022; 54 pages. From a repository described as: A repo of all my presentations for LUG, and ORESEC. Sections: lug.mines.edu/attend; What makes an exploit?; PS4 security; Playstation 2 in 4; Starting to escape the Emulator; Part 1; part 2; Now we have writing to memory!; Now where are we in memory; Part 3; ASLR defeated!; Game over now literally. Slides cover Exploits, PS4 Cont, PS4 ASLR, The PS2 entry point, JIT, Processes protections, Step 1: Escape the game, What do we need?, The emu exploit, and OVERFLOW!!!."
  3549,"Application 3D remote sensing scientist: RSC4Earth","https://gitlab.com/SimpleForest/application-slides/-/blob/main/applicationSlidesLeipzig.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.LG,cs.LG math.ST stat.ML cs.DC computer-science mathematics statistics machine-learning bioinformatics distributed-systems slides thesis gitlab,Jan Hackenberg,2022,null,"Application 3D remote sensing scientist: RSC4Earth. Beamer slides by Jan Hackenberg, 2022; 83 pages. Part of Application Slides: To make it easy for you to get started with GitLab, here's a list of recommended next steps. Sections: SimpleForest distributed results; Well Prepared; Prequiste for biodiversity; Ecological interaction. Subsections include General SimpleForest software paper [Applied Informatics], DTM and segmentation [Applied Remote Sensing], Metabolic Scaling Theory [Biology], R package [Applied Statistics, Thesis], Automated Leave filter [Applied Machine Learning, Teja], Ecological TLS data base [Data Bases, External], Cloud to Conifer/BroadLeave [Applied Machine Learning, Thesis], Cloud to Species [Applied Machine Learning, Thesis], Drought effects on the growth rate [Spatial and Temporal statistics], and Detect bark beetle. Slides cover Structure, Resources to extract papers from, Rework of, DTM and segmentation, Not yet done, Traditional forestry vs QSMs, Branch Orders, QSMs - mathematical trees with, SimpleForest backs up the controversially discussed WBE model, and SimpleForest backs up the."
  3550,"Базы Данных. Лекция 1.: Введение, Иерархические базы данных (areksei/shad-db-materials)","https://gitlab.com/areksei/shad-db-materials/-/blob/master/lectures2022/lecture1.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.DB,cs.DB computer-science databases graph-theory slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Базы Данных. Лекция 1.: Введение, Иерархические базы данных (areksei/shad-db-materials). Лекция 1.: Введение, Иерархические базы данных. Beamer lecture slides (Школа Анализа Данных), 2022; 85 pages, in Russian. Subject (translated): databases. Sections: Введение; Иерархические базы данных; Реляционные базы данных; Key-Value Store; Wide-column store; Colum-oriented Databases; NewSQL Databases; Timeseries Databases; Document Databases; Graph Databases; Queues; Заключение. Slides cover Простое приложение, работающее с данными, Проблемы такого подхода, IMS, Реляционная модель, IBM System R, Пример выражения на SQL, Коммерческие реляционные СУБД, Открытые реляционные СУБД, Направления разработки реляционных СУБД, and Способы работы с базой."
  3551,A biologically-inspired methodology for mesh optimization in fluid-structure interaction problems,"https://gitlab.com/biocca.nicolas/bimo-presentation/-/blob/main/main.pdf",gitlab.com,q-bio.GN,q-bio.GN math.OC physics.flu-dyn q-bio.QM quantitative-biology mathematics physics bioinformatics optimization fluid-dynamics slides gitlab,Nicolás Biocca Santiago Urquiza,2022,null,"A biologically-inspired methodology for mesh optimization in fluid-structure interaction problems. Beamer slides by Nicolás Biocca Santiago Urquiza (National University of Mar del Plata Faculty of Engineering), 2022; 53 pages. Part of Biologically-Inspired Mesh Optimizer (BIMO) - Presentation: BIMO presentation (formerly PhD defense) written in LaTeX by means of Beamer class, editable through TeXstudio edito and ready to be presented via pdfpc presentation viewer. Sections: Mesh Moving Methods; Optmización de mallas (MWEs); Movimiento de Mallas - Ejemplos prácticos; Movimientos cíclicos; Moving Meshes - Application Problems; Conclusiones y trabajo futuro. Slides cover Interface-tracking, Arterial tissue composition, Historial review, Biologically-Inspired Mesh Optimizer (BIMO), BIMO - Virtual configuration, Fiber recruitment, Pseudo-material remodeling, Mesh Optimization, Regular hexagon - no recruitment, and Rectangular parallelogram - oscillatory phenomenon."
