  3564,"CPSC 1430 Introduction: Special Fall Term Edition: Basic","https://gitlab.com/braxtoncuneo/lecture_slides/-/blob/main/F2022/basic/basic.pdf",gitlab.com,math.AG,math.AG mathematics stacks lecture-notes survey slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"CPSC 1430 Introduction: Special Fall Term Edition: Basic. Beamer slides, 2022; 62 pages. From the course-materials archive braxtoncuneo/lecture_slides. Sections: Survey Results; Course Plan; Getting Oriented with C++; Common C++/Java/Python Features; Checking our C++ Literacy. Subsections include Some Stats, Concerns about Learning C++, Concerns about Repeating the Course, Desired Course Material, Basics, Memory, Classes + ADT Fundamentals, Stacks + Queues, Debugging, and Linked Lists. Slides cover Some Stats, Concerns about Learning C++, Concerns about Repeating the Course, Desired Course Material, Course Plan - Assignments (as of 09/23/2022), Basics, Memory, Classes, Stacks + Queues, and Debugging."
  3565,H1Server Crash Course,"https://gitlab.com/braxtoncuneo/lecture_slides/-/blob/main/F2022/server_crash/ServerCrashCourse.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.OS,cs.OS math.HO computer-science mathematics operating-systems history-of-mathematics lecture-notes survey slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"H1Server Crash Course. Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 19 pages. From the course-materials archive braxtoncuneo/lecture_slides. Sections: A Crash Course on Servers and Terminals. Subsections include A Brief History Lesson on Terminals, The File System, The Teletype Machine (aka Teleprinter), and The Command Line Interface. Slides cover H2Overview, H2The First Time-share Computers, H2Who cares about UNIX?, H2The File System, H2Identifying Places in a Filesystem - Part 1, H2Identifying Places in a Filesystem - Part 2, H2Identifying Places in a Filesystem - Part 3, H2Identifying Places in a Filesystem - Part 4, H2Identifying Places in a Filesystem - Part 5, and H2Your Home Directory."
  3566,Lecture 03 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-03),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-03/-/blob/main/pdf/lecture-03.pdf",gitlab.com,math.LO,math.LO mathematics mathematical-logic lecture-notes slides gitlab,Xing Shi Cai,2022,null,"Lecture 03 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-03). Beamer lecture slides by Xing Shi Cai, 2022; 31 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) taught at Duke Kunshan University by Xing Shi Cai starting from March 2022. Sections: 3.1 Propositional Logic. Subsections include Truth Tables, Logical Equivalence, Deductions, and Beyond Propositions. Slides cover Who gets a ?, Sound and unsound arguments, Propositional logic, The truth table of ¬P∨Qis, The Monopoly problem, Think-Pair-Share — Three monkeys, Logical equivalence, Boolean algebra, Verifying equivalence, and Deductions."
