  3593,Lecture 09 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-09.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 09 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 25 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: AC 7 Inclusion-Exclusion. Subsections include 7.1 Introduction, 7.2 The Inclusion-Exclusion Formula, and 7.3 Enumerating Surjections. Slides cover 7.1 Introduction, The number of CS students, A Venn Diagram, Amanda’s again, 7.2 The Inclusion-Exclusion Formula, Some notations, The CS student example, Amanda’s example, Three properties, and Four properties."
  3594,Lecture 11 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-11.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 11 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 26 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: AC 8 Generating functions. Subsections include 8.1 Basic Notion and Terminology, and 8.2 Another look at distributing apples or folders. Slides cover 8.1 Basic Notion and Terminology, What is a generating function (gf), Examples of GF, Multiply polynomials, Multiply GFs, Multiplicative inverse, Add GFs, More operations on GF, Shorthand for GFs, and The transfer principle."
  3595,Lecture 12 — Generating Functions (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-12.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 12 — Generating Functions (2) - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 19 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: AC 8 Generating functions; 8.4 Newton's Binomial Theorem. Subsections include 8.2 Another look at distributing apples or folders, and 8.4 An Application of the Binomial Theorem. Slides cover 8.2 Another look at distributing apples or, Example 8.5, The gf for fruit baskets, 8.4 Newton’s Binomial Theorem, Definition 8.8, Definition 8.9 – Binomial coefficients, Binomial Theorem, Newton’s Binomial Theorem, and Applying Newton’s Binomial Theorem."
  3596,Lecture 13 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-13.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 13 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 24 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: AC 8 Generating functions. Subsections include AC 8.5 Partition of an Integer, and AC 8.6 Exponential Generating Function. Slides cover AC 8.5 Partition of an Integer, Paying lunch with cash, Paying with $1 bills, Paying with $2 bills, Paying with $m bills, Paying lunch with more cash, The integer partition problem, Paying with of distinct values, Proving an identity by gf, and Think-Pair-Share."
  3597,Lecture 15 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-15.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.LO,cs.LO math.CO math.HO computer-science mathematics formalization combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 15 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 21 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: AC 9 Recurrence Equations. Subsections include 9.4.2 Solving Advancement Operator Equations – Nonhomogeneous Case, 9.5 Formalizing our approach to recurrence equations, and 9.6 Using Generating Functions to Solve Recurrences. Slides cover 9.4.2 Solving Advancement Operator, Nonhomogeneous equations, Finding a particular solution, When we have one solution, A recipe for nonhomogeneous equations, Example 9.15, Example 9.16, Example — Towers of Hanoi puzzle, Think-Pair-Share, and 9.5 Formalizing our approach to."
  3598,Lecture 16 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-16.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics graph-theory extremal-combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 16 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 30 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: AC 5 Graph Theory. Subsections include 5.1 Basic Notation and Terminology for Graphs, and 5.2 Multigraphs: Loops and Multiple Edges. Slides cover 5.1 Basic Notation and Terminology for, Model networks with graphs, Graphs, Neighbours, Induced subgraph, Independent graph, Paths, Graphs isomorphism, Connected graphs, and Odd degrees."
  3599,Lecture 17 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-17.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics graph-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 17 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 23 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: DM 4.2 Trees. Subsections include Properties of Trees, Rooted Trees, and Spanning Trees. Slides cover Properties of Trees, Trees, Proposition 4.2.1, Corollary 4.2.2, Proposition 4.2.3, Proposition 4.2.4, Think-Pair-Share, Rooted Trees, and Bipartite graph."
  3600,Lecture 18 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science,"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-18.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 18 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science. Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 19 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: AC 5.6 Counting Labelled Trees — Cayley's formula. Subsections include A Proof Using Prüfer code, and A Proof Using Generating Functions. Slides cover AC 5.6 Counting Labelled Trees —, Trees of size 2, 3 and 4, Cayley’s formula, Prüfer code, A key observation, From code to tree, Proof by induction, How to generate all trees?, Think-Pair-Share — Trees with fixed degrees, and Lagrange–Bürmann formula."
  3601,Lecture 19 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-19.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.SG mathematics graph-theory symplectic-geometry lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 19 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 23 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: AC 5.3 Eulerian and Hamiltonian Graphs. Subsections include Eulerian Graphs, and Hamiltonian Graphs. Slides cover AC 5.3 Eulerian and Hamiltonian, Leonhard Euler, The seven-bridges problem, Eulerian graphs, A special weird case, An eulerian graph, Euler’s theory, Finding an eulerian circuit, A disconnected graph?, and A graph with odd degrees?."
  3602,Lecture 20 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-20.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.AT mathematics graph-theory chromatic-homotopy-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 20 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 18 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: AC 5.4 Graph Colouring. Subsections include The Chromatic Number, and Bipartite Graphs. Slides cover The Chromatic Number, Friendships, Model networks with graphs, So many radio stations, Turn this into a graph, Can you do better?, Some simple cases, Bipartite Graphs, Colouring cycles, and How to arrange a wedding?."
  3603,Lecture 21 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-21.pdf",gitlab.com,math.AT,math.AT mathematics chromatic-homotopy-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 21 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 28 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: AC 5.4.2 Cliques and Chromatic Number. Subsections include Proof by J. Mycielski, and Proof by J. Kelly and L. Kelly. Slides cover AC 5.4.2 Cliques and Chromatic, Warming up, What is the clique numbers, Construct G4, Three different ways to draw G4, How to colour G4 with 4 colours?, Things get complicated soon!, Think-Pair-Share, Cakes!, and Generalized Hole Principle."
  3604,Lecture 22 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-22.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO math.AT mathematics graph-theory chromatic-homotopy-theory algorithms lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 22 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 30 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: AC 5.4.3 Can We Determine Chromatic Number?. Subsections include First-Fit Algorithm, Maximum Degrees and Chromatic Numbers, Interval Graphs, and Perfect Graphs. Slides cover AC 5.4.3 Can We Determine, Let’s colour a graph, Colouring a graph greedily, The maximum degree, A simpler bound, Interval graphs, The clique number of an interval graph, Think-Pair-Share, The Strong Perfect Graph Theorem, and The complete graph is perfect (again)!."
  3605,Lecture 23 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-23.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics graph-theory lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 23 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 28 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: AC 5.5 Planar Graphs. Subsections include Definitions, Euler's Formula, Is this graph planar? – A Simple Check, Is this graph planar? – Kuratowski's Theorem, and Four colour theorem. Slides cover Definitions, Planar graphs, Euler’s Formula, Faces, edges, and vertices, Edges and faces, A corollary, Is this graph planar? – Kuratowski’s, Homeomorphism, Think-Pair-Share, and Four colour theorem."
  3606,Lecture 24 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-24.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics extremal-combinatorics graph-theory probability combinatorics lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 24 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 30 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: AC 11 Applying Probability to Combinatorics. Subsections include 11.1 A First Taste of Ramsey Theory, 11.2 Small Ramsey Numbers, 11.3 Estimate Ramsey Number, and 11.5 Ramsey’s Theorem. Slides cover AC 11 Applying Probability to, Some more examples, A six student lemma, Ramsey’s theory for graphs, Think-Pair-Share, Proof of Theorem 11.2, Erdős and Ramsey numbers, Stirling’s approximation, How to Estimate Ramsey Number?, and Another bet."
  3607,Lecture 25 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-25.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA mathematics real-analysis lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 25 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 35 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: bai 1.2 The set of real numbers; bai 2.1 Sequences and limits. Subsections include 2.1.1 Monotone sequences. Slides cover A few words before we start, The maximum, Upper bound, Examples of supreme, Infimum, What are real numbers?, Examples of sequences, Convergence, Example of convergence, and Uniqueness of limits."
  3608,Lecture 26 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-26.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA mathematics real-analysis lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 26 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 31 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: bai 2.1 Sequences and limits; bai 2.4 Cauchy sequences; bai 2.5 Series. Subsections include 2.1.1 Monotone sequences, 2.1.3 Subsequences, and 2.5.1 Definition. Slides cover 2.1.1 Monotone sequences, Keeling Curve, Examples, When is a monotone sequence convergent, Limits of monotone sequences — Proposition 2.1.10, Is the sequence ൲1 +, 2.1.3 Subsequences, Convergence of subsequence, Think-Pair-Share, and Cauchy."
  3609,Lecture 27 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-27.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA mathematics real-analysis lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 27 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 31 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: bai 2.5 Series. Subsections include 2.5.1 Definition, 2.5.2 Cauchy series, 2.5.3 Basic properties, 2.5.4 Absolute convergence, 2.5.5 Comparison test and the p-series, and 2.5.6 Ratio test. Slides cover 2.5.1 Definition, What is a series?, How many do we need?, 2.5.2 Cauchy series, Cauchy series, When a series converges, Harmonic numbers/series, Linearity of series, 2.5.4 Absolute convergence, and Converge Absolutely."
  3610,Lecture 28 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08),"https://gitlab.com/compsci-203/2022-08/-/blob/main/pdf/lectures/lecture-28.pdf",gitlab.com,math.CA,math.CA cs.DS mathematics computer-science real-analysis algorithms lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Lecture 28 - COMPSCI 203 — Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science (compsci-203/2022-08). Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 30 pages. Part of COMPSCI203 -- Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science: This repository contains materials which I (Xing Shi Cai) prepared for the course COMPSCI203 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science) of Duke Kunshan University, taught from 2022-08 till 2022-10. Sections: bai 2.5 Series; 2.6 More on series; Real Analysis in Algorithm Analysis. Subsections include 2.5.5 Comparison test and the p-series, 2.5.6 Ratio test, 2.6.2 Alternating series test, and 2.6.5 Power series. Slides cover 2.5.5 Comparison test and the p-series, Comparison test, 2.5.6 Ratio test, Try ratio test, Alternating series, What is 2π?, Some functions defined by power series, Radius of convergence, Quick-sort, and Big Onotation."
  3611,FHPC - presentation and SSH 101,"https://gitlab.com/cozzini/Foundations_of_HPC_2022/-/blob/main/Basic/0_ssh101.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.DC,cs.DC cs.PF computer-science high-performance-computing slides gitlab,Ruggero Lot,2022,null,"FHPC - presentation and SSH 101. Beamer slides by Ruggero Lot, 2022; 21 pages. From a repository described as: Stefano Cozzini, Area Science Park, Trieste. Sections: The infrastructure; SSH. Slides cover Who am I?, The HPC cluster, The support infrastructure, How to access all this bonanza?, What is this login node?, How do we connect to this node?, How to obtain it?, What is key authentication?, and Generate the key."
  3612,"PHIDIAS HPC Final Impact Webinar: The path towards new services to increase HPC and Data capacities","https://gitlab.com/ctroupin/PresentationsLatex/-/blob/master/20220712_Phidias_Webinar/DIVA_PhidiasWebinar202207_ULiege.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.DC,cs.DC cs.PF computer-science high-performance-computing slides gitlab,C. Troupin,2022,null,"PHIDIAS HPC Final Impact Webinar: The path towards new services to increase HPC and Data capacities. Beamer slides by C. Troupin, 2022; 20 pages. From a repository described as: This project aims to store the source files (LaTeX) used to generate the conference presentations and posters. The pdf will be stored and images won't be stored in GitHub due to memory issues. Slides cover Getting oceanographic data is harder than you think, Collect once, use many times, Gridding oceanographic data is harder than you think, Our solution: the Data-Interpolating Variational Analysis, Providing data & code: is it enough?, Code citation through DOI, Speeding up the installation, The SeaDataCloud Virtual Research Environment, The BlueCloud Virtual Research Environment, and Final word's: let's speed up research!."
  3613,Софтуерно дефинирани периферини шини с PRU,"https://gitlab.com/dinuxbg/presentations/-/blob/master/2022.10-bg-lightning-talk-pru/pru-lightning-talk.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.AR,cs.AR computer-science computer-architecture slides talk gitlab,null,2022,null,"Софтуерно дефинирани периферини шини с PRU. Beamer talk slides, 2022; 9 pages, in Russian. From a repository described as: A collection of public talks I have presented. Subject (translated): assembly language. Slides cover Защо да пиша периферна шина?, Какво е PRU?, За какво мога да го ползвам?, Софтуерна поддръжка, Отворени проекти с PRU, and Недостатъци."
  3614,"Nonlinear manifold ROM with Convolutional Autoencoders and Reduced Over-Collocation method: Eccomas Oslo2022","https://gitlab.com/giovastabile/pdf_presentations/-/blob/main/eccomas_oslo2022.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning real-analysis slides gitlab,Giovanni Stabile* and Gianluigi Rozza,2022,null,"Nonlinear manifold ROM with Convolutional Autoencoders and Reduced Over-Collocation method: Eccomas Oslo2022. Beamer slides by Giovanni Stabile*, and Gianluigi Rozza, 2022; 31 pages. From a repository described as: To make it easy for you to get started with GitLab, here's a list of recommended next steps. Slides cover Overcoming a Slow decaying Kolmogorov n-width with nonlinear ROMs, Solution manifold learning with Convolutional Autoencoders (CAE), Manifold learning: physical, geometrical, analytical inductive biases, Hyper-reduction: reduced over-collocation method (NM-LSPG-ROC)2, Time-dependent parametric nonlinear 2d test case: Nonlinear conservation law4, Latent nonlinear dynamics NCL, Comparison with LSTM neural networks NCL, Time-dependent parametric nonlinear 2d test case: Shallow Water equations, Solution manifold learning SWE: POD vs CAE reconstruction error, Solutions FOM SWE for train parameters 1, 10, Conclusions: references and software, Computational cost NCL: offline and online stages, ROC convergence SWE hU, and Compressed decoder SWE."
  3615,"Nonlinear manifold ROM with Convolutional Autoencoders and Reduced Over-Collocation method: Oslo 2022","https://gitlab.com/giovastabile/pdf_presentations/-/blob/main/oslo_2022.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning real-analysis slides gitlab,Giovanni Stabile* and Gianluigi Rozza,2022,null,"Nonlinear manifold ROM with Convolutional Autoencoders and Reduced Over-Collocation method: Oslo 2022. Beamer slides by Giovanni Stabile*, and Gianluigi Rozza, 2022; 21 pages. From a repository described as: To make it easy for you to get started with GitLab, here's a list of recommended next steps. Slides cover Overcoming a Slow decaying Kolmogorov n-width with nonlinear ROMs, Solution manifold learning with Convolutional Autoencoders (CAE), Manifold learning: physical, geometrical, analytical inductive biases, Nonlinear Manifold Least-squares Petrov-Galerkin (NM-LSPG)1, Hyper-reduction: reduced over-collocation method (NM-LSPG-ROC)2, NM-LSPG-ROC with teacher student training (NM-LSPG-ROC-TS)3, Time-dependent parametric nonlinear 2d test case: Nonlinear conservation law4, Solution manifold learning NCL: POD vs CAE reconstruction error, Latent nonlinear dynamics NCL, Hyper-reduction convergence NCL, Comparison with LSTM neural networks NCL, Solutions NM-LSPG-GNAT-TS NCL for test parameters 1, 3, 14, 16, Time-dependent parametric nonlinear 2d test case: Shallow Water equations, and Qualitative view of the solution manifold SWE."
