  3633,Exact resolution of the sparse spectral unmixing problem - Application of branch-and-bound algorithm,"https://gitlab.com/mlatif/slides-mimosa-unmix/-/blob/master/main.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.DS,cs.DS math.DS math.CA computer-science mathematics algorithms ode-and-dynamical-systems optimization slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Exact resolution of the sparse spectral unmixing problem - Application of branch-and-bound algorithm. Beamer slides, 2022; 62 pages. Part of l0-UNMIX Support de présentation: Titre : Algorithme branch-and-bound pour le démélange spectral parcimonieux. Sections: Assumption, model and definitions; Branch-and-bound algorithm for non-OR community; Mathematical development and dedicated branch-and-bound; Some experiments and results. Slides cover Sparse spectral unmixing problem, The short λ’s resume, Sparsity constraint, Exact optimisation of the l0-SU - Our approach, Branch-and-bound algorithm by the example, Branching procedure - K = Card(C), and The dedicated branch-and-bound: Example with K = 3, Q = 20."
  3634,Coriolis – Analog Capabilities - SAL Bootcamp,"https://gitlab.com/mosaic_group/mosaic_bootcamp/bootcamp_presentations/-/blob/main/LIP6-Coriolis.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.NI,cs.NI computer-science networking slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Coriolis – Analog Capabilities - SAL Bootcamp. Beamer slides, 2022; 25 pages. From a repository described as: To make it easy for you to get started with GitLab, here's a list of recommended next steps. Sections: Digital Place & Route; Analog Place & Route; State of The Toolchain; And Now, Let's Have a Demo. Slides cover Who Are We, Overall Analog Design Flow, Devices & Form Factor Functions, Devices Assembly, From Slicing Tree to GCells, and Specific Routing Constraints."
  3635,"Améliorer la localisabilité des systèmes multi-robots: \"Déploiement et localisation coopérative simultanée de réseaux de robots mobiles\"","https://gitlab.com/nitraced/isae-bucket/-/blob/master/pres/presjdd2022.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.RO,cs.RO computer-science robotics aerospace-engineering ai-agents slides gitlab,Jérôme Le Ny,2022,null,"Améliorer la localisabilité des systèmes multi-robots: \"Déploiement et localisation coopérative simultanée de réseaux de robots mobiles\". Beamer slides by Jérôme Le Ny (Institut Supérieur de l'Aéronautique et de l'Espace, Toulouse, France.), 2022; 18 pages, in French. Subject (translated): aerospace engineering and aerodynamics. Sections: Contexte; Localisabilité; Placement de robots; État des lieux et perspectives. Subsections include Sémantique, Multilatération, Géométrie, Connectivité d'un système multi-agent, Rigidité, and Information. Slides cover Plan général de la présentation, Contextualisation par l'analyse sémantique, Localisation par mesures relatives RF : multilatération, Géométrie / petite expérience, Étape 1 : connectivité du graphe de mesures, Étape 2 : Rigidité de la charpente associée au graphe, Étape 3 : Matrice d'information, and Exemple de déploiement."
  3636,Vectorization - the easy way,"https://gitlab.com/nla4hpc/fall-2021/lecture-slides/-/blob/main/lecture_slides_14.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.DC,cs.DC cs.AR cs.PF math.NA computer-science mathematics high-performance-computing computer-architecture numerical-analysis slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Vectorization - the easy way. Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 62 pages. Sections: Batched Routines SIMD Vectorization; Batched Iterative Solver Setting; Batched Iterative Solver Setting (2); Batched Iterative Solver Setting (3); Direct methods vs. iterative methods; Direct methods vs. iterative methods (2); Direct methods vs. iterative methods (3); Performance aspects of batched kernels; Performance aspects of batched kernels (2); Performance aspects of batched kernels (3). Slides cover Batched Routines: Motivation, Batched Routines, Batched Routines in MAGMA, Applications of Batched Routines: Block-Jacobi, Direct methods, 1. Batched functionality is generally, First experiences with Ginkgo’s batched iterative solvers in PeleLM, First experiences with Ginkgo’s batched iterative solvers in XGC, SIMD Vectorization, and Scalar vs SIMD Instruction."
  3637,Octopus Development Roadmap,"https://gitlab.com/octopus-code/octopus-presentations/-/blob/master/Roadmap/octopus_roadmap.pdf",gitlab.com,math.SG,math.SG mathematics symplectic-geometry lecture-notes slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Octopus Development Roadmap. Beamer slides (AKA Micael's wishlist), 2022; 18 pages. From the course-materials archive octopus-code/octopus-presentations. Slides cover Disclaimer, Goals, Strategy, General stuff, Build system, Buildbot, Testsuite, Performance Testsuite, Webpage, Grids, Batches and mesh functions, Hamiltonian and operators, Pseudopotentials, and Multisystem Implementation: Ions."
  3638,"Chapter 10: Constrained Optimization: Chp10","https://gitlab.com/ofec-release/io-slides/-/blob/main/chp%2010/chp10.pdf",gitlab.com,math.OC,math.OC cs.LG mathematics computer-science optimization category-theory book slides gitlab,Changhe Li,2022,null,"Chapter 10: Constrained Optimization: Chp10. Beamer lecture slides by Changhe Li, 2022; 29 pages. Part of IO Slides: To make it easy for you to get started with GitLab, here's a list of recommended next steps. Sections: 10.1 Introduction; 10.2 Constraint-handling Techniques; 10.3 Challenges and Future Directions. Subsections include Concept, Example, Why EA?, Penalty Function, Separation of Objectives and Constraints, and Ensemble Methods. Slides cover Concept of Constrained Optimization Problems (COPs), Example, Why EA?, 10.2.1 Penalty Function, Categories, 10.2.1.1 Static Penalty Function, 10.2.1.2 Dynamic Penalty Function, 10.2.1.3 Adaptive Penalty Function, 10.2.2 Separation of Objectives and Constraints, and 10.2.2.1 Feasibility Rule."
  3639,Chapter 11 Dynamic Optimization,"https://gitlab.com/ofec-release/io-slides/-/blob/main/chp%2011/chp11.pdf",gitlab.com,math.OC,math.OC cs.LG cs.DC mathematics computer-science optimization ml-systems book slides gitlab,Changhe Li,2022,null,"Chapter 11 Dynamic Optimization. Beamer lecture slides by Changhe Li, 2022; 44 pages. Part of IO Slides: To make it easy for you to get started with GitLab, here's a list of recommended next steps. Sections: 11.1 A Brief Introduction; 11.2 Dynamism Handling Methods; 11.3 Benchmark Problems and Metrics for Dynamic Single-objective Optimization; 11.4 Benchmark Problems and Metrics for Dynamic Multi-objective Optimization; 11.5 Dynamic Constrained Optimization; 11.6 Challenges. Slides cover 11.1 Introduction, 11.1.1 Basics of Changes, 11.1.2 Characteristics of Changes, 11.2.1 Difficulties, 11.2.2 Dynamism Handling Strategies, 11.3.1 Classical Problem Generators, 11.3.2 Performance Measures, 11.4.1 Classical Benchmark Problems, and 11.4.2 Performance Measures."
  3640,Chapter 12 Robust Optimization,"https://gitlab.com/ofec-release/io-slides/-/blob/main/chp%2012/chp12.pdf",gitlab.com,math.OC,math.OC cs.LG mathematics computer-science optimization algorithms book slides gitlab,Changhe Li,2022,null,"Chapter 12 Robust Optimization. Beamer lecture slides by Changhe Li, 2022; 20 pages. Part of IO Slides: To make it easy for you to get started with GitLab, here's a list of recommended next steps. Sections: Robust Optimization Algorithms; Discussions. Subsections include Uncertainties in Objective Function, Uncertainties in Environments, and Uncertainties Over Time. Slides cover 12.1 Introduction, 12.2.1 Uncertainties in Decision Variables, 12.2.1 Uncertainties in Decision Variables-Sampling Methods, 12.2.2 Uncertainties in Objective Function, 12.2.3 Uncertainties in Environments, 12.2.4 Uncertainties Over Time, 12.2.5 A general framework for robust optimization over time, and 12.3 Discussions."
  3641,Chapter 13 Large-scale Global Optimization,"https://gitlab.com/ofec-release/io-slides/-/blob/main/chp%2013/chp13.pdf",gitlab.com,math.OC,math.OC cs.DS cs.LG mathematics computer-science optimization algorithms book slides gitlab,Changhe Li,2022,null,"Chapter 13 Large-scale Global Optimization. Beamer lecture slides by Changhe Li, 2022; 49 pages. Part of IO Slides: To make it easy for you to get started with GitLab, here's a list of recommended next steps. Sections: 13.1 Large-scale Global Optimization Problems; 13.2 Co-evolution Methods; 13.3 Non-decomposition-based Methods; 13.4 Learning-based Methods; 13.5 Discussions. Subsections include 13.1.1 Definition, 13.1.2 Difficulties, 13.2.1 Co-operative Co-evolution, 13.2.2 Static Grouping, 13.2.3 Dynamic Grouping, 13.3.1 PSO-based Algorithms, 13.3.2 EDA-based Algorithms, and 13.3.3 DE-based Algorithms. Slides cover 13 Large-scale Global Optimization, Large-scale Global Optimization Problems-Definition, 13.1.2 Difficulties, 13.2.1 Co-operative Co-evolution, 13.2.2 Static Grouping, 13.2.3 Dynamic Grouping, Co-evolution Methods-Dynamic Grouping, Non-decomposition-based Methods, 13.3.1 PSO-based Algorithms, and 13.3.2 EDA-based Algorithms."
