  3657,Price-Setting with Menu Costs,"https://gitlab.com/prollynotmaxime/nber-workshop-2022/-/blob/main/Lectures/Lecture%2010%20Menu%20Costs.pdf",gitlab.com,q-fin.RM,q-fin.RM math.NA cs.AI econ.GN quantitative-finance mathematics computer-science economics economics-and-finance ai-agents functional-analysis linear-algebra slides talk gitlab,null,2022,null,"Price-Setting with Menu Costs. Beamer lecture slides, 2022; 58 pages. Part of Spring 2022 NBER Workshop: This repo contains code for the tutorials of the Spring 2022 heterogeneous-agent macro workshop at the NBER taught by Adrien Auclert, Bence Bardóczy, Michael Cai, Matt Rognlie, and Ludwig Straub. Sections: Pricing models and GPC; Exact equivalence: Menu cost model = 2 TD; Numerical equivalence: Menu cost model Calvo; Measuring the GPC directly; Extra slides. Slides cover Time dependent vs. state dependent pricing, The Phillips curve for menu cost models: 3 main results, Implications, Ss bands and steady state price gap distribution, Pass-through matrix for TD model, Equivalence result, Why does the intensive margin behave like a TD model?, Visualizing GPC for Calvo model, Quality of fit and minimizer across the parameter space, and Fitted hazard function Λ(x) and (GPC)."
