  3839,"CS7301: Advanced Topics in Optimization for Machine Learning - Lecture 1.1: Introduction and Course Overview","https://github.com/rishabhk108/AdvancedOptML/blob/main/slides/CS7301_Lecture1_1.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG math.OC math.RA stat.ML computer-science mathematics statistics optimization machine-learning linear-algebra commutative-algebra lecture-notes survey slides github,Rishabh Iyer,2021,null,"CS7301: Advanced Topics in Optimization for Machine Learning - Lecture 1.1: Introduction and Course Overview. Beamer lecture slides by Rishabh Iyer, 2021; 48 pages. From a repository described as: Deadline for finalizing on the papers to cover: February 26th. Slides cover Course Outline, Why take this Course?, Part III of this course, Part III: Optimization in ML, How is this course different from Machine Learning or, Continuous Optimization in Machine Learning, Matrix-Vector Product, Matrix-Matrix Product, Application 1: Supervised Learning, Some Concrete Supervised Learning Instances, Application 4: Matrix Completion, Application 6: Contextual Bandits and Learning from, Application 2: Feature Selection, and Big Picture: Types of Optimization Problems."
  3840,"CS7301: Advanced Topics in Optimization for Machine Learning - Lecture 1.2: Convex Sets and Convex Functions","https://github.com/rishabhk108/AdvancedOptML/blob/main/slides/CS7301_Lecture1_2.pdf",github.com,math.OC,math.OC cs.LG math.MG mathematics computer-science convex-analysis machine-learning optimization lecture-notes slides github,Rishabh Iyer,2021,null,"CS7301: Advanced Topics in Optimization for Machine Learning - Lecture 1.2: Convex Sets and Convex Functions. Beamer lecture slides by Rishabh Iyer, 2021; 51 pages. From a repository described as: Deadline for finalizing on the papers to cover: February 26th. Slides cover Convex Sets, Properties of Convex Sets, Euclidean balls and ellipsoids, Convex and Strictly Convex Functions, Equivalent Definitions of Convex Functions, Are the following functions convex?, Strongly Convex Functions II, Convex Functions, Properties of Convex Functions, Composition with Scalar Functions, Pointwise Maximums and Supremums, Which of the Following Loss Functions are Convex?, Directional derivative and the gradient vector, and Sublevel Sets of Convex Functions."
  3841,"CS7301: Advanced Topics in Optimization for Machine Learning - Lecture 2.1: Convex Functions Continued","https://github.com/rishabhk108/AdvancedOptML/blob/main/slides/CS7301_Lecture2_1.pdf",github.com,math.OC,math.OC cs.LG math.MG mathematics computer-science convex-analysis machine-learning optimization lecture-notes slides github,Rishabh Iyer,2021,null,"CS7301: Advanced Topics in Optimization for Machine Learning - Lecture 2.1: Convex Functions Continued. Beamer lecture slides by Rishabh Iyer, 2021; 61 pages. From a repository described as: Deadline for finalizing on the papers to cover: February 26th. Slides cover Properties of Convex Functions, Composition with Vector Functions, Pointwise Maximums and Supremums, Directional derivative and the gradient vector, Convex Function ⇒Convex Sub-level sets, Proof that the function is Quasi-Convex, Convex Functions and Their Epigraphs (contd), Second Order Conditions of Convexity, (Sub)Gradients and Convexity (contd), Subgradient of max{w Tx, 0}, Local Minima, and Convexity: Local and Global Minimum."
  3842,"CS7301: Advanced Topics in Optimization for Machine Learning - Lecture 2.2: Gradient Descent and Family","https://github.com/rishabhk108/AdvancedOptML/blob/main/slides/CS7301_Lecture2_2.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG math.OC stat.ML math.CA computer-science mathematics statistics machine-learning optimization real-analysis convex-analysis lecture-notes slides github,Rishabh Iyer,2021,null,"CS7301: Advanced Topics in Optimization for Machine Learning - Lecture 2.2: Gradient Descent and Family. Beamer lecture slides by Rishabh Iyer, 2021; 173 pages. From a repository described as: Deadline for finalizing on the papers to cover: February 26th. Slides cover Recap, Lipschitz Continuity, Smooth Functions Examples, More on Strong Convexity, Lipschitz Continuity and, Properties of ML Loss Functions, Lipschitz Continuous Functions, Recap: Smoothness vs Continuity, Gradient Descent for Smooth Functions: III, Fastest Convergence with Smooth + Strongly Convex II, Lipschitz + Strongly Convex II, and Nesterov’s Accelerated Gradient Descent."
  3843,"CS7301: Advanced Topics in Optimization for Machine Learning - Lecture 3.1: Gradient Descent Continued","https://github.com/rishabhk108/AdvancedOptML/blob/main/slides/CS7301_Lecture_3_1.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML math.OC computer-science statistics mathematics machine-learning optimization ml-systems real-analysis lecture-notes slides github,Rishabh Iyer,2021,null,"CS7301: Advanced Topics in Optimization for Machine Learning - Lecture 3.1: Gradient Descent Continued. Beamer lecture slides by Rishabh Iyer, 2021; 43 pages. From a repository described as: Deadline for finalizing on the papers to cover: February 26th. Slides cover Recap, Gradient Descent: Recap, Recap: Convergence rate for Smooth Functions, Lipschitz Continuous + Strongly Convex, Lower Bounds (No Proof), Why can GD be slow?, Nesterov’s Accelerated Gradient Descent, Does this Matter in Practice?, Gradient Descent in Practice: Basic Version, and Armijo Backtracking Line-Search V2."
  3844,"CS7301: Advanced Topics in Optimization for Machine Learning - Lecture 3.2: Projected and Proximal Gradient Descent","https://github.com/rishabhk108/AdvancedOptML/blob/main/slides/CS7301_Lecture_3_2.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML math.OC computer-science statistics mathematics machine-learning optimization algorithms probabilistic-combinatorics lecture-notes slides github,Rishabh Iyer,2021,null,"CS7301: Advanced Topics in Optimization for Machine Learning - Lecture 3.2: Projected and Proximal Gradient Descent. Beamer lecture slides by Rishabh Iyer, 2021; 29 pages. From a repository described as: Deadline for finalizing on the papers to cover: February 26th. Slides cover Proximal Gradient Descent, How easy is it to compute the Prox operator?, Main ideas for computing Prox, Computing Prox for L1 Norm, Iterative Soft Thresholding Algorithm (Proximal, Tables for the Proximal Operator, Summary of Proximal Gradient Descent, Projected Gradient Descent and Proximal Gradient Descent, Computing the Projection Operator, and Easy to Project Sets C (with closed form solutions)."
  3845,"CS7301: Advanced Topics in Optimization for Machine Learning - Lecture 4.1: Projected Gradient Descent and Conditional Gradient Descent","https://github.com/rishabhk108/AdvancedOptML/blob/main/slides/CS7301_Lecture_4_1.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML math.OC computer-science statistics mathematics machine-learning optimization algorithms real-analysis lecture-notes slides github,Rishabh Iyer,2021,null,"CS7301: Advanced Topics in Optimization for Machine Learning - Lecture 4.1: Projected Gradient Descent and Conditional Gradient Descent. Beamer lecture slides by Rishabh Iyer, 2021; 49 pages. From a repository described as: Deadline for finalizing on the papers to cover: February 26th. Slides cover Recap: Proximal Gradient Descent, Recap on Lagrangian and Duality, Algorithm: Projected Gradient Descent (We use xk, Computing the Projection Operator, Convergence Results for Projected Gradient Descent, Pros and Cons of Projected Gradient Descent, Conditional Gradient Descent, Example: L1 Norm Constraints, Duality Gap, and Step Size Variants."
