  4002,"Chapter 1: Introduction to data","https://github.com/OpenIntroStat/openintro-statistics-slides/blob/master/Chp%201/chp1.pdf",github.com,math.PR,math.PR math.ST physics.class-ph cond-mat.mtrl-sci mathematics physics random-matrix-theory solid-mechanics statistics survey book slides github,OpenIntro Statistics,2020,null,"Chapter 1: Introduction to data. Beamer lecture slides by OpenIntro Statistics ($\\:$ Slides developed by Mine Cetinkaya-Rundel of OpenIntro. The slides may be copied, edi), 2020; 85 pages. From a repository described as: These slides are available at http://www.openintro.org under a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported license (CC BY-NC-SA):. Sections: Case study; Data basics; Sampling principles and strategies; Experiments. Subsections include Observations and variables, Types of variables, Relationships among variables, Explanatory and response variables, Introducing observational studies and experiments, Populations and samples, Anecdotal evidence, Sampling from a population, Observational studies, and Four sampling methods. Slides cover Treating Chronic Fatigue Syndrome, Study design, Generalizing the results, Types of variables (cont.), Relationships among variables, Association vs. causation, Populations and samples, Census, Exploratory analysis to inference, and Sampling bias example: Landon vs. FDR."
  4003,"Chapter 2: Summarizing data","https://github.com/OpenIntroStat/openintro-statistics-slides/blob/master/Chp%202/chp2.pdf",github.com,math.ST,math.ST math.CO math.FA stat.ME mathematics statistics algebraic-combinatorics functional-analysis category-theory book slides github,OpenIntro Statistics,2020,null,"Chapter 2: Summarizing data. Beamer lecture slides by OpenIntro Statistics ($\\:$ Slides developed by Mine Cetinkaya-Rundel of OpenIntro. The slides may be copied, edi), 2020; 96 pages. From a repository described as: These slides are available at http://www.openintro.org under a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported license (CC BY-NC-SA):. Sections: Examining numerical data; Considering categorical data; Case study: Gender discrimination. Subsections include Scatterplots for paired data, Dot plots and the mean, Histograms and shape, Variance and standard deviation, Box plots, quartiles, and the median, Robust statistics, Transforming data, Mapping data, Contingency tables and bar plots, and Row and column proportions. Slides cover Scatterplot, Histograms - Extracurricular hours, Extracurricular activities, Commonly observed shapes of distributions, Application activity: Shapes of distributions, Variance (cont.), Outliers (cont.), Robust statistics, Pros and cons of transformations, and Contingency tables."
  4004,"Chapter 3: Probability","https://github.com/OpenIntroStat/openintro-statistics-slides/blob/master/Chp%203/chp3.pdf",github.com,math.PR,math.PR math.FA mathematics probability functional-analysis statistics book slides github,OpenIntro Statistics,2020,null,"Chapter 3: Probability. Beamer lecture slides by OpenIntro Statistics ($\\:$ Slides developed by Mine Cetinkaya-Rundel of OpenIntro. The slides may be copied, edi), 2020; 175 pages. From a repository described as: These slides are available at http://www.openintro.org under a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported license (CC BY-NC-SA):. Sections: Defining probability; Conditional probability; Sampling from a small population; Random variables; Continuous distributions. Subsections include Probability, Disjoint or mutually exclusive outcomes, Probabilities when events are not disjoint, Probability distributions, Complement of an event, Independence, Recap, Exploring probabilities with a contingency table, Marginal and joint probabilities, and Defining conditional probability. Slides cover Random processes, Probability, Union of non-disjoint events, Sample space and complements, Determining dependence based on sample data, Joint probability, Conditional probability (cont.), Independence and conditional probabilities (cont.), Practice, and Sampling with replacement."
  4005,"Chapter 4: Distributions of random variables","https://github.com/OpenIntroStat/openintro-statistics-slides/blob/master/Chp%204/chp4.pdf",github.com,math.FA,math.FA math.PR mathematics functional-analysis probability arithmetic-geometry statistics book slides github,OpenIntro Statistics,2020,null,"Chapter 4: Distributions of random variables. Beamer lecture slides by OpenIntro Statistics ($\\:$ Slides developed by Mine Cetinkaya-Rundel of OpenIntro. The slides may be copied, edi), 2020; 161 pages. From a repository described as: These slides are available at http://www.openintro.org under a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported license (CC BY-NC-SA):. Sections: Normal distribution; Geometric distribution; Binomial distribution; Negative binomial distribution; Poisson distribution. Subsections include Normal distribution model, Standardizing with Z scores, Finding tail areas, Normal probability examples, Bernoulli distribution, The binomial distribution, Normal approximation to the binomial, and The normal approximation breaks down on small intervals. Slides cover Unimodal and symmetric, bell shaped curve, Heights of males, Six sigma, Practice, Geometric distribution (cont.), The question from the prior slide asked for the probability of given, The birthday problem (cont.), Expected value and its variability, and Below are four pairs of Binomial distribution parameters. Which."
  4006,"Chapter 5: Foundations for inference","https://github.com/OpenIntroStat/openintro-statistics-slides/blob/master/Chp%205/chp5.pdf",github.com,math.ST,math.ST math.PR cs.SE stat.ME mathematics computer-science statistics probability software-engineering mathematical-logic book slides github,OpenIntro Statistics,2020,null,"Chapter 5: Foundations for inference. Beamer lecture slides by OpenIntro Statistics ($\\:$ Slides developed by Mine Cetinkaya-Rundel of OpenIntro. The slides may be copied, edi), 2020; 101 pages. From a repository described as: These slides are available at http://www.openintro.org under a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported license (CC BY-NC-SA):. Sections: Point estimates and sampling variability; Confidence intervals for a proportion; Hypothesis testing for a proportion. Subsections include Point estimates and error, Understanding the variability of a point estimate, Application exercise, Central Limit Theorem, Applying the Central Limit Theorem to a real-world setting, More details regarding the Central Limit Theorem, Extending the framework for other statistics, Capturing the population parameter, Constructing a 95% confidence interval, and Changing the confidence level. Slides cover Point estimates and sampling, Point estimates and error, Suppose we randomly sample 1,000 adults from each state in the, # 1. Create a set of 250 million entries, where 88\\% of, CLT - conditions, Confidence intervals for a, Facebook’s categorization of user interests, Width of an interval, Recap: hypothesis testing framework, and Decision errors."
