  4106,Declarative Concurrent Programming with Join Calculus in Scala,"https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/join_calculus/chymyst_2020_lambda-conf.pdf",github.com,math.CA,math.CA cs.DC cs.LO mathematics computer-science real-analysis concurrency formalization survey slides talk github,Sergei Winitzki,2020,null,"Declarative Concurrent Programming with Join Calculus in Scala. Beamer slides by Sergei Winitzki (Lambda-Conf 2020 Global Edition), 2020; 32 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover Chemical Machine: a new hope, The chemical metaphor I. \"Abstract\" chemistry, The chemical metaphor II. Chemical Machine in a nutshell, Programming the Chemical Machine using Chymyst, Example: throttling, Example: throttling test, Example: async cancellation, Example: async cancellation test, Example: async racing, Example: async racing test, Additional feature: blocking molecules, Example: synchronous rendez-vous, Example: racing with blocking molecules, and Example: parallel map/reduce."
