  4276,Where has all my sand gone? Hydro-morphodynamics 2D modelling using a discontinuous Galerkin discretisation,"https://github.com/firedrakeproject/firedrake/blob/main/docs/source/_static/firedrake19-slides/clare.pdf",github.com,math.NA,math.NA cs.NA math.AP physics.class-ph mathematics computer-science physics numerical-analysis pde solid-mechanics algebraic-geometry slides github,Dr. James Percival* and Dr. Athanasios Angeloudis**,2019,null,"Where has all my sand gone? Hydro-morphodynamics 2D modelling using a discontinuous Galerkin discretisation. Beamer slides by Dr. James Percival*, and Dr. Athanasios Angeloudis**, 2019; 36 pages. From a repository described as: Firedrake is an automated system for the portable solution of partial differential equations using the finite element method (FEM). Firedrake enables users to employ a wide range of discretisations to an infinite variety of PDEs and obtain high performance code on CPUs. Sections: Building a hydro-morphodynamics 2D model in Thetis; Migrating Trench; Meander. Slides cover February 2014 in Dawlish, Devon, Sediment Transport, Basic Model Equations, Adding Physical Effects, Comparing with Industry Standard Model, Migrating Trench: Initial Set-up, Migrating Trench: Varying Diffusivity, Migrating Trench: Simulation, Meander: Initial Set-up, and Meander: Physical Effects."
