  4314,"Chapter 2: The Functional Approach to Collections","https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/ftt-fp/02-functional-collections.pdf",github.com,math.CA,math.CA cs.LO cs.DC math.CO mathematics computer-science real-analysis concurrency formalization graph-theory survey book slides talk problem-list github,Sergei Winitzki,2019,null,"Chapter 2: The Functional Approach to Collections. Beamer lecture slides by Sergei Winitzki, 2019; 16 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover Tuples, Pattern-matching syntax for tuples, Combining tuple types with other types, Worked examples, Exercises I, Exercises II, Mathematical induction I, Mathematical induction II, Tail recursion, Mathematical induction III, Mathematical induction IV, Mathematical induction V, and Exercises III."
  4315,"Chapter 7: Computations lifted to a functor context II. Monads - Part 2: Laws and structure of monads and semimonads","https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/ftt-fp/07-monads-part2.pdf",github.com,math.CT,math.CT mathematics category-theory real-analysis concurrency formalization survey book slides talk problem-list github,Sergei Winitzki,2019,null,"Chapter 7: Computations lifted to a functor context II. Monads - Part 2: Laws and structure of monads and semimonads. Beamer lecture slides by Sergei Winitzki, 2019; 17 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover Semimonad laws I: The intuitions, Semimonad laws II: The laws for flatMap, Semimonad laws III: The laws for flatten, Equivalence of a natural transformation and a “lifting”, Semimonad laws IV: Deriving the laws for flatten, Checking the associativity law for standard monads, Motivation for monads, The monad laws formulated in terms of pure and flatten, Formulating laws via Kleisli functions, Motivation for categories and functors, From Kleisli back to flatMap, Structure of semigroups and monoids, Structure of (semi)monads, and Exercises II."
  4316,"Chapter 10: Free type constructions","https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/ftt-fp/10-free-constructions.pdf",github.com,math.CA,math.CA math.CT cs.LO cs.DC mathematics computer-science real-analysis category-theory concurrency formalization survey book slides talk github,Sergei Winitzki,2019,null,"Chapter 10: Free type constructions. Beamer lecture slides by Sergei Winitzki, 2019; 36 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover The interpreter pattern I. Expression trees, The interpreter pattern II. Variable binding, The interpreter pattern III. Type safety, The interpreter pattern V. Define Monad-like methods, The interpreter pattern VII. Handling errors, Monad laws for DSL programs, Free constructions in mathematics: Example II, Worked example II: Free monoid, Church encoding I: Motivation, Church encoding III: How it works, Encoding with an existential type: How it works, Church encoding IV: Recursive types and type constructors, Properties of free type constructions, and Properties of inductive typeclasses."
  4317,"Chapter 11: Computations in a functor context III - Monad transformers","https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/ftt-fp/11-monad-transformers.pdf",github.com,math.CT,math.CT cs.CL cs.AI cs.LG mathematics computer-science category-theory large-language-models real-analysis concurrency survey book slides talk github,Sergei Winitzki,2019,null,"Chapter 11: Computations in a functor context III - Monad transformers. Beamer lecture slides by Sergei Winitzki, 2019; 22 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover Computations within a functor context: Combining monads, Combining monadic effects I. Trial and error, Combining monadic effects II. Lifting into a larger monad, Laws for monad liftings I. Identity laws, Laws for monad liftings II. Simplifying the laws, Laws for monad liftings III. The naturality law, Monad transformers I: Motivation, Monad transformers II: The requirements, Monad transformers III: First examples, Monad transformers IV: The zoology of ad hoc methods, Composed-inside transformers I, Composed-inside transformers II. Proofs of lifting laws, Composed-inside transformers III. Proofs of runner laws, and Rigid monads I: Definitions."
  4318,C Programming in Linux,"https://github.com/wx672/lecture-notes/blob/master/c/slides/c-b.pdf",github.com,cs.OS,cs.OS computer-science operating-systems numerical-analysis lecture-notes slides github,null,2019,null,"C Programming in Linux. Beamer slides, 2019; 75 pages. Sections: Basic Building Blocks of C; The make Utility; C Concepts; Pointers and Arrays; Memory Model; x86 Assembly; Hacker's Tools; Linux GUI Programming; APUE. Slides cover Reference Books, Course Web Links, Homework, High level languages, Data, Variable Types, Floating Point vs. Integer Divide, Strings, Loop Control Statements, and Makefile."
  4319,Estimation of particle position and momentum for LHCb electromagnetic calorimeter,"https://github.com/yandexdataschool/mlhep2019/blob/master/slides/day-1/MLHEP_coopetition__regression.pdf",github.com,math.ST,math.ST stat.ME mathematics statistics slides github,Vladislav Belavin,2019,null,"Estimation of particle position and momentum for LHCb electromagnetic calorimeter. Beamer slides by Vladislav Belavin, 2019; 12 pages. Slides cover LHCb experiment, Electromagnetic calorimeter, Electromagnetic samples, Dataset, Problem statement, Metric, Competition organization information, Some additional information, and Let’s go to the practice!."
  4320,"Intro into Machine Learning: Fifth Machine Learning in High Energy Physics Summer School, MLHEP 2019, August 1–10","https://github.com/yandexdataschool/mlhep2019/blob/master/slides/day-1/linear-1/lecture-03-linear-models-tasks.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML math-ph math.ST computer-science statistics physics mathematics machine-learning mathematical-physics numerical-analysis optimization survey slides github,"Alexey Artemov$^{",2019,null,"Intro into Machine Learning: Fifth Machine Learning in High Energy Physics Summer School, MLHEP 2019, August 1–10. Beamer lecture slides by Alexey Artemov$^{ (tabularc c $^1$ Skoltech & $^2$ Higher School of Economics tabular), 2019; 157 pages. Sections: Linear models for regression; Numerical and stochastic optimization at a glance; Linear models for classification; Figures of merits; Overfitting: how to fool the linear regression; Regularization; A Bayesian perspective on regularization. Slides cover Lecture overview, \"Physics-based\" vs. machine-learned models, Machine learning as function approximation, Function approximation: energy usage, Univariate linear regression, Some other evaluation metrics for regression, Multivariate linear regression, Multivariate linear regression: the solution, A quick intro into the Numerical Optimization, and The gradient descent algorithm."
  4321,"Decision Trees and Ensembling algorithms - Fifth Machine Learning in High Energy Physics Summer School, MLHEP 2019, July 1–10","https://github.com/yandexdataschool/mlhep2019/blob/master/slides/day-2/decision-trees-ensembles.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG cs.DS math-ph math.ST computer-science physics mathematics machine-learning algorithms mathematical-physics statistics survey slides github,Alexey Artemov and Andrey Ustyuzhanin,2019,null,"Decision Trees and Ensembling algorithms - Fifth Machine Learning in High Energy Physics Summer School, MLHEP 2019, July 1–10. Beamer slides by Alexey Artemov, and Andrey Ustyuzhanin, 2019; 80 pages. Sections: Decision trees; Bagging and Random Forests; Learning Theory (continued); Naive boosting for regression; Reweighting and AdaBoost; Gradient boosting; XGBoost algorithm; Stacked generalization; Bonus track. Slides cover Lecture overview, Decision making at a bank, With decision trees, overfitting is extra-easy!, Stopping rules for decision tree learning, Bias-variance decomposition, An application: statistical analysis of Bagging, Boosting for regression, Boosting: an example regression problem, Adaptive boosting for classification, and GBM: an example regression problem."
  4322,"Generative Models, part I - Machine Learning in High Energy Physics","https://github.com/yandexdataschool/mlhep2019/blob/master/slides/day-5/generative-1/generative.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML math-ph computer-science statistics physics machine-learning mathematical-physics probability software-engineering slides github,Maxim Borisyak,2019,null,"Generative Models, part I - Machine Learning in High Energy Physics. Beamer slides by Maxim Borisyak, 2019; 64 pages. Sections: Generative models; Kernel Density Estimation; Gaussian Mixtures; Variational AutoEncoder; Generative Adversarial Networks; GAN training tricks. Slides cover Given samples of a random variable X, find X′, such that, Applications, Main idea: place a small gaussian-like function around each sample, Advantages, Types of GMM, VAE non-deterministically transforms latent variables Z into samples X, Variational bound, Reconstruction error, Testing time, and Approximating JS distance."
  4323,Learning to pivot - Machine Learning in High Energy Physics,"https://github.com/yandexdataschool/mlhep2019/blob/master/slides/day-5/pivoting/learning-to-pivot.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG math-ph stat.ML hep-th computer-science physics statistics machine-learning mathematical-physics slides github,Maxim Borisyak,2019,null,"Learning to pivot - Machine Learning in High Energy Physics. Beamer slides by Maxim Borisyak, 2019; 9 pages. Slides cover Learning to pivot, Measuring dependencies, Adversarial training, Learning to pivot with adversarial networks, and Conditional pivoting."
  4324,"Sequence Modelling - Fifth Machine Learning in High Energy Physics Summer School, MLHEP 2019","https://github.com/yandexdataschool/mlhep2019/blob/master/slides/day-5/sequence_modellig/SequenceModellig.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG math-ph stat.ML cs.CL computer-science physics statistics machine-learning mathematical-physics large-language-models slides github,Ekaterina Artemova,2019,null,"Sequence Modelling - Fifth Machine Learning in High Energy Physics Summer School, MLHEP 2019. Beamer slides by Ekaterina Artemova, 2019; 51 pages. Sections: Sequence modelling; Recurrent neural network; Gated architectures; RNN generators; The Transformer; Implementation in PyTorch; Take-home message; Bonus: Recursive NN. Slides cover Definition, Sequential data, Sequence modelling III, Sequence modelling with RNN, RNN unrolled, Multilayer RNN, Sequence labelling, Long short term memory, Sequence generation, and Multi-head Attention."
  4325,Introduction to Causal Inference,"https://github.com/yandexdataschool/mlhep2019/blob/master/slides/day-6/ICI.pdf",github.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics graph-theory survey slides github,Evgeniy Riabenko Facebook and Core Data Science,2019,null,"Introduction to Causal Inference. Beamer slides by Evgeniy Riabenko Facebook, and Core Data Science, 2019; 41 pages. Sections: Causality; Conditioning techniques. Subsections include Simpsons' paradox, Causal graphs, Interventions, and Backdoor criterion. Slides cover Why bother?, What is causality?, The Three Layer Causal Hierarchy, Randomized experiment, Cholesterol and exercise, Simpson’s paradox, Elements of causal graph, Intervention, Graph surgery, and Adjustment formula."
