  4330,"Compressed Sensing: Theory, Algorithms and Applications","https://github.com/zhanglabtools/DSMO.course/blob/master/course_files/lecture_slides/CompressedSensing.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS math.RA math.NA math.OC computer-science mathematics algorithms linear-algebra optimization commutative-algebra slides github,Shihua Zhang,2019,null,"Compressed Sensing: Theory, Algorithms and Applications. Beamer lecture slides by Shihua Zhang, 2019; 117 pages. Part of Data Science and Matrix Optimization: The ten topics and the corresponding material are as follows: 1. Robust PCA material slides 2. Sections: Technological Applications; Reconstruction Algorithms; Measurement Matrix and Recovery Theory; Theoretical Extensions; Extended Methods. Subsections include Single-Pixel Camera, Magnetic Resonance Imaging, Optimization Methods, Greedy Methods, Thresholding-based Methods, Coherence, Restricted Isometry Property, Error Correction, Low-Rank Matrix Recovery, and Matrix Completion. Slides cover Single-Pixel Camera, Magnetic Resonance Imaging, How to Implement CS?, Computational Cost, Which Algorithm Should One Choose?, Restricted Isometry Property, Phase Transition, Robust PCA [Cand`es et al., 2011], and How to Impose Sparse on Signal x."
  4331,"Data Science and Matrix Optimization, Manifold Alignment","https://github.com/zhanglabtools/DSMO.course/blob/master/course_files/lecture_slides/ManifoldAlignment.pdf",github.com,math.OC,math.OC math.RA cs.LG math.NA mathematics computer-science linear-algebra optimization algorithms category-theory slides github,Shihua Zhang,2019,null,"Data Science and Matrix Optimization, Manifold Alignment. Beamer lecture slides by Shihua Zhang, 2019; 118 pages. From a repository described as: The ten topics and the corresponding material are as follows: 1. Robust PCA material slides 2. Sections: Key Ideas of MA; Feature-level Alignment (Linear); Semi/unsupervised MA; Manifold Alignment and Deep Learning. Subsections include Background, Problem Definition, Two Ideas of MA, General Solution of MA, Linear MA, Canonical Correlation Analysis (CCA), Generalized Unsupervised MA (GUMA), MA Preserving Global Geometry, Semi-supervised Manifold Alignment (SSMA), and Kernel Manifold Alignment (KEMA). Slides cover Background, Learning Correspondences, Categories of MA, Objective 1: Preserve Similarities, Linear Restriction, GUMA Algorithm, Global MA - Problem, Global MA - Experiments, SSMA - Problem, and KEMA - Problem."
  4332,"Data Science and Matrix Optimization, Matrix Completion","https://github.com/zhanglabtools/DSMO.course/blob/master/course_files/lecture_slides/MatrixCompletion.pdf",github.com,math.RA,math.RA math.AC math.NA math.OC mathematics linear-algebra commutative-algebra optimization graph-theory slides github,Shihua Zhang,2019,null,"Data Science and Matrix Optimization, Matrix Completion. Beamer lecture slides by Shihua Zhang, 2019; 108 pages. From a repository described as: The ten topics and the corresponding material are as follows: 1. Robust PCA material slides 2. Sections: What is Matrix Completion?; Exact Matrix Completion; Approximate Matrix Completion; Follow-up Research. Subsections include Nuclear Norm Minimization, Low-Rank Matrix Factorization, Distributed Matrix Completion, Graph-regularized Matrix Completion, Link Prediction on Graphs with Deep Learning, and Matrix Completion under Missing Mechanisms. Slides cover Movie Recommendation, Application 1: Sensor Localization, What Can Go Wrong?, Exact Unique Recovery Theorem, Convergence Analysis, The Lagrange Form, Hard-Impute Algorithm, What is SVD?, Alternating Least Square (ALS), and Probabilistic Models on Matrix Factorization."
  4333,"Nonnegative Matrix Factorization (NMF): Models, Algorithms and Applications","https://github.com/zhanglabtools/DSMO.course/blob/master/course_files/lecture_slides/NMF.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS math.RA math.NA math.OC computer-science mathematics algorithms linear-algebra optimization slides github,Shihua Zhang,2019,null,"Nonnegative Matrix Factorization (NMF): Models, Algorithms and Applications. Beamer lecture slides by Shihua Zhang, 2019; 144 pages. Part of Data Science and Matrix Optimization: The ten topics and the corresponding material are as follows: 1. Robust PCA material slides 2. Sections: What is NMF?; Algorithms of NMF; Complexity of NMF; Variants of NMF; NMF towards Big Data. Subsections include Constrained NMF, Structured NMF, and Generalized NMF. Slides cover Many Data Are Nonnegative!, NMF vs PCA, Local Optimization Algorithms, Summary of PG, Constrained NMF, Incorporate Discriminant Information to NMF, Structured NMF, Semi-NMF, How to address those challenges (even partially)?, and Orthogonal Transformation."
  4334,"Data Science and Matrix Optimization, Nonlinear Manifold Learning","https://github.com/zhanglabtools/DSMO.course/blob/master/course_files/lecture_slides/NonlinearManifoldLearning.pdf",github.com,math.OC,math.OC math.RA cs.LG math.NA mathematics computer-science linear-algebra optimization slides github,Shihua Zhang,2019,null,"Data Science and Matrix Optimization, Nonlinear Manifold Learning. Beamer lecture slides by Shihua Zhang, 2019; 123 pages. From a repository described as: The ten topics and the corresponding material are as follows: 1. Robust PCA material slides 2. Sections: Background; Manifold Learning; Linear Manifold Learning; Nonlinear Manifold Learning. Subsections include PCA, MDS, IsoMap, LLE, Follow-up Methods, SNE, t-SNE, and UMAP."
  4335,Precision Matrix Estimation,"https://github.com/zhanglabtools/DSMO.course/blob/master/course_files/lecture_slides/PrecisionEstimation.pdf",github.com,math.ST,math.ST math.RA stat.ME math.NA mathematics statistics linear-algebra optimization slides github,Shihua Zhang,2019,null,"Precision Matrix Estimation. Beamer lecture slides by Shihua Zhang, 2019; 127 pages. Part of Data Science and Matrix Optimization: The ten topics and the corresponding material are as follows: 1. Robust PCA material slides 2. Sections: Gaussian Graphical Models; Main Approaches; Variants. Subsections include Sparsity, Penalized Likelihood Methods, Column-by-column Estimation Methods, CLIME, Graphical Model with Hubs, Joint Graphical Lasso, and Differential Network Estimation. Slides cover Network of Variables, Independence vs Conditional Independence, Sparsity, Optimization of Graphical Lasso, ADMM, Time Cost, QUIC, Block Screen (Important), D-trace Loss Estimator, and If we perform multiple linear regression of Y on Z."
  4336,Robust Principal Component Analysis,"https://github.com/zhanglabtools/DSMO.course/blob/master/course_files/lecture_slides/RobustPCA.pdf",github.com,cs.CC,cs.CC cs.DS math.HO math.OC computer-science mathematics algorithms complexity-theory history-of-mathematics linear-algebra slides github,Shihua Zhang,2019,null,"Robust Principal Component Analysis. Beamer lecture slides by Shihua Zhang, 2019; 124 pages. Part of Data Science and Matrix Optimization: The ten topics and the corresponding material are as follows: 1. Robust PCA material slides 2. Sections: History; Principal Component Analysis (PCA); Robust PCA (RPCA); Applications of RPCA. Subsections include Convex relaxation of RPCA without noise, Convex relaxation of RPCA with noise, and Nonconvex relaxation of RPCA. Slides cover Principal component analysis (PCA) was first proposed in 1901, PCA is a statistical procedure concerning with elucidating the, Minimum projection distance of the samples, Application 1: Dimensionality reduction, Motivation of Robust PCA, Connection between PCA and RPCA, Difficulties of designing algorithms, Convex relaxation of RPCA, SDP for RPCP, and Subproblems (S-subproblem)."
  4337,Sparse Coding and Dictionary Learning,"https://github.com/zhanglabtools/DSMO.course/blob/master/course_files/lecture_slides/SparseCoding.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS cs.LG math.OC cs.CC computer-science mathematics algorithms optimization cognitive-science complexity-theory survey slides github,Shihua Zhang,2019,null,"Sparse Coding and Dictionary Learning. Beamer lecture slides by Shihua Zhang, 2019; 123 pages. Part of Data Science and Matrix Optimization: The ten topics and the corresponding material are as follows: 1. Robust PCA material slides 2. Sections: What's Sparse Coding?; Algorithms of Sparse Coding; Algorithms of Dictionary Learning; Sparse Coding Meets Neural Networks. Slides cover A Brief Review of Signal Transform, How do Brains Code the Image Signal?, Difficulties of Sparse Coding Model, This is an NP-hard problem! [Natarajan, 1995], Greedy Algorithms, Proximal Gradient Method [Rockafellar, 1970], Iterative Shrinkage/Thresholding Algorithm, Coordinate-Wise Minimization, Sparse Coding Based Classification Method, and K-SVD."
  4338,"Data Science and Matrix Optimization, Subspace Clustering","https://github.com/zhanglabtools/DSMO.course/blob/master/course_files/lecture_slides/SubspaceClustering.pdf",github.com,math.OC,math.OC math.RA cs.LG math.NA mathematics computer-science linear-algebra optimization slides github,Shihua Zhang,2019,null,"Data Science and Matrix Optimization, Subspace Clustering. Beamer lecture slides by Shihua Zhang, 2019; 125 pages. From a repository described as: The ten topics and the corresponding material are as follows: 1. Robust PCA material slides 2. Sections: Background; Sparse Subspace Clustering; Other Self-Expressive Models; Subspace Clustering by Block Diagonal Representation; More than Linear Model."
  4339,"Tensor Factorization Models, Algorithms and Applications","https://github.com/zhanglabtools/DSMO.course/blob/master/course_files/lecture_slides/TensorFactorization.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS cs.LG math.AC computer-science mathematics algorithms commutative-algebra machine-learning combinatorics slides github,Shihua Zhang,2019,null,"Tensor Factorization Models, Algorithms and Applications. Beamer lecture slides by Shihua Zhang, 2019; 111 pages. Part of Data Science and Matrix Optimization: The ten topics and the corresponding material are as follows: 1. Robust PCA material slides 2. Sections: Low-rank Models; Algorithms; Applications in machine Learning. Subsections include Canonical Polyadic Decomposition (CPD), Tucker Decomposition, Multilinear SVD (MLSVD), Alternating Least Squares (ALS), Gradient Descent Methods, Imposing Constraints, Knowledge Base Completion, Recommender Systems, Multilinear Classification, and Topic Mining. Slides cover Tensors?, Useful Product 2, Slab Representations-Towards CPD, Essential Uniqueness, Tucker Decomposition, Multilinear SVD (MLSVD), MLSVD, Tensor Completion, Imposing Constraints, and Constrained least squares using ADMM."
  4340,Probabilistic Complexity,"https://gitlab.com/733amir/dorehami/-/blob/master/13-Probabilistic-Complexity-Soroush-Zargar/document.pdf",gitlab.com,math.PR,math.PR mathematics probability lecture-notes slides gitlab,S. Soroush H. Zargarbashi,2019,null,"Probabilistic Complexity. Beamer slides by S. Soroush H. Zargarbashi, 2019; 52 pages. From the course-materials archive 733amir/dorehami. Sections: Preliminaries and Motivation; Polynomial Probability; Bounded Error Probabilistic Polynomial; Probabilistic Polynomials Inclusions."
