  4619,"Chapter 3: The Logic of Types, Part III - The Curry-Howard correspondence","https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/ftt-fp/03-logic-of-types-3.pdf",github.com,math.LO,math.LO cs.LO math.CA mathematics computer-science mathematical-logic type-theory real-analysis concurrency survey book slides talk problem-list github,Sergei Winitzki,2018,null,"Chapter 3: The Logic of Types, Part III - The Curry-Howard correspondence. Beamer lecture slides by Sergei Winitzki, 2018; 14 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover Types and propositional logic, Working with the CH correspondence I, Working with the CH correspondence II, Working with the CH correspondence III, Type isomorphisms I, Type isomorphisms II, Type isomorphisms III, Using school-level algebra to reason about types, Worked examples, Exercises III, Working with the CH correspondence IV, Working with the CH correspondence V, and Addendum."
