  4790,"Part 1: Introduction","https://github.com/15172658790/Blog/blob/branch_1/%E8%AE%A1%E7%AE%97%E6%9C%BA%E4%B8%8E%E4%BF%A1%E6%81%AF%E7%B1%BB/%E6%93%8D%E4%BD%9C%E7%B3%BB%E7%BB%9F%E5%8E%9F%E7%90%86%E4%B8%8E%E8%AE%BE%E8%AE%A1/slides-%E9%99%88%E9%A6%99%E5%85%B0/1_introduction.pdf",github.com,cs.OS,cs.OS cs.DC math.HO computer-science mathematics operating-systems distributed-systems history-of-mathematics lecture-notes slides github blog,null,2017,null,"Part 1: Introduction. Beamer slides, 2017; 127 pages, in Chinese. From the course-materials archive 15172658790/Blog. Subject (translated): operating systems. Sections: What is OS?; History of Operating Systems; 其他操作系统; 作业、实验和小结. Subsections include 操作系统的定义和目标, Roles of operating system, 操作系统的层次模型, 操作系统的发展动力, 1980~present,PC时代,百花齐放, 1990~present,移动计算时代, Personal-Computer Systems, Parallel Systems, Distributed Systems, and Embedded System."
  4791,"Part 2: OS structure","https://github.com/15172658790/Blog/blob/branch_1/%E8%AE%A1%E7%AE%97%E6%9C%BA%E4%B8%8E%E4%BF%A1%E6%81%AF%E7%B1%BB/%E6%93%8D%E4%BD%9C%E7%B3%BB%E7%BB%9F%E5%8E%9F%E7%90%86%E4%B8%8E%E8%AE%BE%E8%AE%A1/slides-%E9%99%88%E9%A6%99%E5%85%B0/2_OS%20structure.pdf",github.com,cs.OS,cs.OS cs.AR computer-science operating-systems computer-architecture lecture-notes slides github blog,null,2017,null,"Part 2: OS structure. Beamer slides, 2017; 88 pages, in Chinese. From the course-materials archive 15172658790/Blog. Subject (translated): operating systems; computer architecture. Sections: 操作系统的组成、服务、特征; 操作系统的抽象模型和体系结构; 小结和作业. Subsections include System components, OS Services, System Calls & Types, system programs, 操作系统的特征, 进程模型, 线程模型, OS structure, Virtual Machine, and 系统设计与实现."
  4792,"Part 3: Processes","https://github.com/15172658790/Blog/blob/branch_1/%E8%AE%A1%E7%AE%97%E6%9C%BA%E4%B8%8E%E4%BF%A1%E6%81%AF%E7%B1%BB/%E6%93%8D%E4%BD%9C%E7%B3%BB%E7%BB%9F%E5%8E%9F%E7%90%86%E4%B8%8E%E8%AE%BE%E8%AE%A1/slides-%E9%99%88%E9%A6%99%E5%85%B0/3_Processes.pdf",github.com,cs.DC,cs.DC cs.OS computer-science distributed-systems operating-systems lecture-notes slides github blog,null,2017,null,"Part 3: Processes. Beamer slides, 2017; 121 pages. From the course-materials archive 15172658790/Blog. Sections: 多道程序技术和程序并发执行的条件; Process Concept; Process Scheduling; Operation on processes; Interprocess Communication (进程间通信, IPC); Example of IPC Systems; Communication in C/S Systems; 小结和作业."
  4793,"Part 4: CPU Scheduling","https://github.com/15172658790/Blog/blob/branch_1/%E8%AE%A1%E7%AE%97%E6%9C%BA%E4%B8%8E%E4%BF%A1%E6%81%AF%E7%B1%BB/%E6%93%8D%E4%BD%9C%E7%B3%BB%E7%BB%9F%E5%8E%9F%E7%90%86%E4%B8%8E%E8%AE%BE%E8%AE%A1/slides-%E9%99%88%E9%A6%99%E5%85%B0/4_CPU_Scheduling.pdf",github.com,cs.DC,cs.DC cs.AR cs.OS cs.DS computer-science distributed-systems computer-architecture operating-systems algorithms lecture-notes slides github blog,null,2017,null,"Part 4: CPU Scheduling. Beamer slides, 2017; 92 pages. From the course-materials archive 15172658790/Blog. Sections: Basic Concepts; Scheduling Criteria; Scheduling Algorithms; Multiple-Processor Scheduling; Real-Time Scheduling; OS examples; Algorithm Evaluation; 小结和作业."
  4794,"Part 5: Threads","https://github.com/15172658790/Blog/blob/branch_1/%E8%AE%A1%E7%AE%97%E6%9C%BA%E4%B8%8E%E4%BF%A1%E6%81%AF%E7%B1%BB/%E6%93%8D%E4%BD%9C%E7%B3%BB%E7%BB%9F%E5%8E%9F%E7%90%86%E4%B8%8E%E8%AE%BE%E8%AE%A1/slides-%E9%99%88%E9%A6%99%E5%85%B0/5_Threads.pdf",github.com,cs.DC,cs.DC cs.OS computer-science distributed-systems operating-systems lecture-notes slides github blog,null,2017,null,"Part 5: Threads. Beamer slides, 2017; 51 pages. From the course-materials archive 15172658790/Blog. Sections: Multithreading Models; Thread Libraries; Threading Issues; OS Examples for Thread; Thread Scheduling; 小结和作业."
  4795,"Part 6: Process synchronization","https://github.com/15172658790/Blog/blob/branch_1/%E8%AE%A1%E7%AE%97%E6%9C%BA%E4%B8%8E%E4%BF%A1%E6%81%AF%E7%B1%BB/%E6%93%8D%E4%BD%9C%E7%B3%BB%E7%BB%9F%E5%8E%9F%E7%90%86%E4%B8%8E%E8%AE%BE%E8%AE%A1/slides-%E9%99%88%E9%A6%99%E5%85%B0/6_Process_synchronization.pdf",github.com,cs.OS,cs.OS computer-science operating-systems lecture-notes slides github blog,null,2017,null,"Part 6: Process synchronization. Beamer slides, 2017; 73 pages. From the course-materials archive 15172658790/Blog. Sections: Background; The Critical-Section Problem (临界区问题); Peterson's Solution; Synchronization Hardware; Semaphores; Classical Problems of Synchronization; Monitors; Synchronization Examples; 小结和作业."
  4796,"Part 7: Deadlock","https://github.com/15172658790/Blog/blob/branch_1/%E8%AE%A1%E7%AE%97%E6%9C%BA%E4%B8%8E%E4%BF%A1%E6%81%AF%E7%B1%BB/%E6%93%8D%E4%BD%9C%E7%B3%BB%E7%BB%9F%E5%8E%9F%E7%90%86%E4%B8%8E%E8%AE%BE%E8%AE%A1/slides-%E9%99%88%E9%A6%99%E5%85%B0/7_deadlock.pdf",github.com,cs.OS,cs.OS computer-science operating-systems lecture-notes slides github blog,null,2017,null,"Part 7: Deadlock. Beamer slides, 2017; 59 pages. From the course-materials archive 15172658790/Blog. Sections: Background and System Model; Deadlock Characterization; Deadlock Prevention (死锁预防); Deadlock Avoidance (死锁避免); Deadlock Detection (死锁检测) and Recovery; 小结和作业."
  4797,"Part 8: Memory","https://github.com/15172658790/Blog/blob/branch_1/%E8%AE%A1%E7%AE%97%E6%9C%BA%E4%B8%8E%E4%BF%A1%E6%81%AF%E7%B1%BB/%E6%93%8D%E4%BD%9C%E7%B3%BB%E7%BB%9F%E5%8E%9F%E7%90%86%E4%B8%8E%E8%AE%BE%E8%AE%A1/slides-%E9%99%88%E9%A6%99%E5%85%B0/8_memory.pdf",github.com,cs.OS,cs.OS computer-science operating-systems lecture-notes slides github blog,null,2017,null,"Part 8: Memory. Beamer slides, 2017; 145 pages. From the course-materials archive 15172658790/Blog. Sections: background; Contiguous Memory Allocation (连续内存分配); Swapping; Paging (分页); Structure of the Page Table; Segmentation (分段); Segmentation with paging (段页式); 小结和作业."
  4798,"Part 9: Virtual Memory","https://github.com/15172658790/Blog/blob/branch_1/%E8%AE%A1%E7%AE%97%E6%9C%BA%E4%B8%8E%E4%BF%A1%E6%81%AF%E7%B1%BB/%E6%93%8D%E4%BD%9C%E7%B3%BB%E7%BB%9F%E5%8E%9F%E7%90%86%E4%B8%8E%E8%AE%BE%E8%AE%A1/slides-%E9%99%88%E9%A6%99%E5%85%B0/9_VirtualMemory.pdf",github.com,cs.OS,cs.OS computer-science operating-systems lecture-notes slides github blog,null,2017,null,"Part 9: Virtual Memory. Beamer slides, 2017; 114 pages. From the course-materials archive 15172658790/Blog. Sections: Background; Demand Paging (按需调页); Copy-on-Write (写时复制); Page Replacement (页面置换); Allocation of Frames; Thrashing (抖动); Memory-Mapped Files; Allocating Kernel Memory; Other Issues; Operating System Examples; 小结和作业."
  4799,"Developing Data Products, Plotly","https://github.com/DataScienceSpecialization/Developing_Data_Products/blob/master/plotly/plotly.pdf",github.com,math.CO,math.CO mathematics graph-theory lecture-notes slides github,null,2017,null,"Developing Data Products, Plotly. Beamer slides, 2017; 29 pages. From a repository described as: Developing Data Products Course from the Johns Hopkins Data Science Lab. Slides cover What is Plotly?, Installing Plotly, Basic Scatterplot, Scatterplot Color, Continuous Color, Scatterplot Sizing, 3D Scatterplot, Line Graph, Multi Line Graph, Histogram, Boxplot, Heatmap, 3D Surface, and Choropleth Maps: Setup."
  4800,Operations that Preserve Convexity,"https://github.com/Hsins/NTU-Courses/blob/main/2016%20Fall/CommE5050%20-%20Convex%20Optimization/handout/05_Convex-Functions-%28III%29.pdf",github.com,math.OC,math.OC math.MG mathematics convex-analysis algebraic-combinatorics optimization slides github,null,2017,null,"Operations that Preserve Convexity. Beamer slides, 2017; 61 pages. Part of NTU Courses: Materials (slide, handout, homework, cheatsheet.) of the courses I took or audited at National Taiwan University. Sections: Operations that Preserve Convexity; Conjugate functions and Other Related Topics; Optimization Problems. Subsections include Basic Operations that Preserve Convexity, Pointwise maximum and supremum, Composition, Minimization, Conjugate functions, Quasiconvex functions, Log-convex and log-concave functions, Basic Terminologies, Standard Forms, and Equivalent Problems. Slides cover Conjugate functions, and Basic Terminologies."
  4801,Conjugate functions and Other Related Topics,"https://github.com/Hsins/NTU-Courses/blob/main/2016%20Fall/CommE5050%20-%20Convex%20Optimization/handout/06_Convex-Optimization-%28I%29.pdf",github.com,math.OC,math.OC cs.LG math.MG mathematics computer-science convex-analysis optimization algebraic-combinatorics real-analysis slides github,null,2017,null,"Conjugate functions and Other Related Topics. Beamer slides, 2017; 67 pages. Part of NTU Courses: Materials (slide, handout, homework, cheatsheet.) of the courses I took or audited at National Taiwan University. Sections: Conjugate functions and Other Related Topics; Optimization Problems; Convex Optimization. Subsections include Conjugate functions, Quasiconvex functions, Log-convex and log-concave functions, Basic Terminologies, Standard Forms, Equivalent Problems, Standard Form, Optimality criterion for differentiable objectives, and Quasiconvex optimization. Slides cover Standard Form."
  4802,Equivalent Reformulations of Optimization Problems,"https://github.com/Hsins/NTU-Courses/blob/main/2016%20Fall/CommE5050%20-%20Convex%20Optimization/handout/10_Duality-%28III%29.pdf",github.com,math.OC,math.OC cs.LG mathematics computer-science optimization survey slides github,null,2017,null,"Equivalent Reformulations of Optimization Problems. Beamer slides, 2017; 47 pages. Part of NTU Courses: Materials (slide, handout, homework, cheatsheet.) of the courses I took or audited at National Taiwan University. Sections: Equivalent Reformulations of Optimization Problems; Theorems of Alternatives. Subsections include Introducing new variables and equality constraints, Transforming the objective, Implicit Constraints, Weak Alternatives, Weak Alternatives for Strict Inequalities, Strong alternatives, and Examples. Slides cover Introducing new variables and equality constraints (1/2), Example – Unconstrained Geometric Program (2/2), Introduction to Dual Norms (2/3), Example – Norm approximation problem (2/2), Dual Norms and Conjugate functions of Norms (1/3), Example – minimum norm problem (1/2), Example – Linear program with box constraints (1/4), and Example – Linear program with box constraints (4/4)."
  4803,Unconstrained Minimization Problems,"https://github.com/Hsins/NTU-Courses/blob/main/2016%20Fall/CommE5050%20-%20Convex%20Optimization/handout/11_Unconstrained-Minimization.pdf",github.com,math.CT,math.CT math.AG cs.LG mathematics computer-science descent-theory machine-learning convex-analysis slides github,null,2017,null,"Unconstrained Minimization Problems. Beamer slides, 2017; 83 pages. Part of NTU Courses: Materials (slide, handout, homework, cheatsheet.) of the courses I took or audited at National Taiwan University. Sections: Unconstrained Minimization Problems; Descent methods; Gradient Descent and Steepest Descent Methods; Newton's method. Subsections include Unconstrained minimization, Examples, Strong convexity, Condition number of sublevel sets, General descent method, Exact Line search, Backtracking Line search, Gradient descent method, Steepest descent method, and The Newton step. Slides cover General descent method."
  4804,Feasibility and phase I methods,"https://github.com/Hsins/NTU-Courses/blob/main/2016%20Fall/CommE5050%20-%20Convex%20Optimization/handout/14_Interior-point-methods-%28II%29.pdf",github.com,math.OC,math.OC cs.LG mathematics computer-science optimization slides github,null,2017,null,"Feasibility and phase I methods. Beamer slides, 2017; 35 pages. Part of NTU Courses: Materials (slide, handout, homework, cheatsheet.) of the courses I took or audited at National Taiwan University. Sections: Feasibility and phase I methods; Primal-dual interior-point methods. Subsections include Basic phase I method, Sum of infeasibilities, Termination near the phase II central path, Primal-dual search direction, The surrogate duality gap, Primal-dual interior-point method, and Examples. Slides cover Basic phase I method (1/4), Basic phase I method (3/4), Sum of infeasibilities (1/3), Sum of infeasibilities (3/3), Comparison of phase I methods (2/2), and Termination near the phase II central path (2/2)."
  4805,"线性代数与解析几何: Linearalgebrageometry","https://github.com/NJUPTFreeExams/NJUPT-General-Free-Exams/blob/master/public/%E7%BA%BF%E6%80%A7%E4%BB%A3%E6%95%B0%E4%B8%8E%E8%A7%A3%E6%9E%90%E5%87%A0%E4%BD%95/linearalgebrageometry.pdf",github.com,math.RA,math.RA math.NA mathematics linear-algebra lecture-notes slides github,null,2017,null,"线性代数与解析几何: Linearalgebrageometry. Beamer slides, 2017; 2315 pages, in Chinese. From the course-materials archive NJUPTFreeExams/NJUPT-General-Free-Exams. Subject (translated): linear algebra. Sections: 第一章 行列式; 第二章 矩阵; 第三章 空间解析几何与向量运算; 第四章 n维向量; 第五章 线性方程组; 第六章 矩阵相似对角化; 第七章 二次型; 附录 习题. Slides cover 第一章行列式, 课程目标及课程结构与框架, 课程教材, 第二章矩阵, 向量及其线性运算, 向量的乘积, 两平面间的位置关系: 点到平面的距离, 空间直线, 曲面和空间曲线, and 第四章n 维向量."
  4806,"CMake入门笔记: CMake入门笔记 - 王逸凡 48801133","https://github.com/PKUanonym/REKCARC-TSC-UHT/blob/master/%E5%A4%A7%E4%B8%80%E4%B8%8B/%E9%9D%A2%E5%90%91%E5%AF%B9%E8%B1%A1%E7%A8%8B%E5%BA%8F%E8%AE%BE%E8%AE%A1%E5%9F%BA%E7%A1%80-%E5%A7%9A%E6%B5%B7%E9%BE%99%E8%80%81%E5%B8%88/hw/inClassTalk/CMake%E5%85%A5%E9%97%A8%E7%AC%94%E8%AE%B0-%E7%8E%8B%E9%80%B8%E5%87%A1_48801133.pdf",github.com,cs.PL,cs.PL computer-science programming-languages lecture-notes slides talk github,null,2017,null,"CMake入门笔记: CMake入门笔记 - 王逸凡 48801133. Beamer talk slides, 2017; 47 pages, in Chinese. From the course-materials archive PKUanonym/REKCARC-TSC-UHT. Subject (translated): programming languages and compilers. Sections: 一些背景介绍; 如何使用CMake; 参考资料. Slides cover 什么是J F2, 什么是*J F2, 为什么要使用*J F2, 安装与配置, 比如我们有一个文件K BMX+TT,放在一个名叫?QK2的目, 在?QK2这个目录下,我们新建一个文件*J F2GBbibXiti,, 一种最直接的办法是点开*J F2。, 当然,我们可以直接把文件生成在?QK2文件夹中。不过这, 除了上面的做法以外,我们还可以直接在终端下执行, and 多个文件下*K F2的使用."
