  4938,"Chapter 1: Values, types, expressions, functions","https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/ftt-fp/01-values-types-expressions.pdf",github.com,math.CA,math.CA cs.LO cs.DC cs.PL mathematics computer-science real-analysis concurrency formalization programming-languages survey book slides talk problem-list github,Sergei Winitzki,2017,null,"Chapter 1: Values, types, expressions, functions. Beamer lecture slides by Sergei Winitzki, 2017; 12 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover What is “Functional Programming”?, Examples of functional programs, What exactly is “math-like” about that code?, Adapting math to programming I, Adapting math to programming II, Some collection types available in Scala, Adapting math to programming III, Adapting math to programming IV, Examples, and Exercises."
  4939,"Chapter 3: The Logic of Types, Part I - Higher-order functions","https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/ftt-fp/03-logic-of-types-1.pdf",github.com,math.LO,math.LO math.CA cs.LO cs.DC mathematics computer-science mathematical-logic real-analysis concurrency formalization survey book slides talk problem-list github,Sergei Winitzki,2017,null,"Chapter 3: The Logic of Types, Part I - Higher-order functions. Beamer lecture slides by Sergei Winitzki, 2017; 5 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover Types and syntax of functions that return functions, Functions with fully parametric types, Worked examples, and Exercises I."
  4940,"Chapter 3: The Logic of Types, Part II - Disjunction types","https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/ftt-fp/03-logic-of-types-2.pdf",github.com,math.LO,math.LO math.CA cs.LO cs.DC mathematics computer-science mathematical-logic real-analysis concurrency formalization survey book slides talk problem-list github,Sergei Winitzki,2017,null,"Chapter 3: The Logic of Types, Part II - Disjunction types. Beamer lecture slides by Sergei Winitzki, 2017; 11 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover Tuples with names: “case classes”, Tuples with one element and with zero elements, Pattern-matching syntax for case classes, Disjunction types, Disjunction types: mathematical point of view, Disjunction type: Either[A, B], More general disjunction types: trait + case classes, The most often used disjunction type: Option[T], Worked examples, and Exercises II."
  4941,"Concurrent Join Calculus in Scala: Join Calculus 2016 Revised","https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/join_calculus/join_calculus_2016_revised.pdf",github.com,math.CA,math.CA cs.DC cs.LO mathematics computer-science real-analysis concurrency formalization operating-systems survey slides talk github,Sergei Winitzki,2017,null,"Concurrent Join Calculus in Scala: Join Calculus 2016 Revised. Beamer slides by Sergei Winitzki, 2017; 28 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover What is “Join Calculus”?, Parallelism vs. Asynchrony vs. Concurrency, Concurrency vs. Parallelism vs. Asynchrony, Dining philosophers, How I learned to forget deadlocks and to love concurrency, Join Calculus: The genesis, Example: concurrent counter, Using JoinRun: more features, JoinRun: Examples I, JoinRun: Examples III, Roadmap for JoinRun, JoinRun: Examples IV, Other approaches to concurrency, and Conclusions and outlook."
  4942,Declarative Concurrent Programming with Chymyst,"https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/join_calculus/join_calculus_2017_SBTB.pdf",github.com,cs.DC,cs.DC cs.LO math.CA computer-science mathematics concurrency real-analysis formalization high-performance-computing survey slides talk github,Sergei Winitzki,2017,null,"Declarative Concurrent Programming with Chymyst. Beamer slides by Sergei Winitzki (Scale by the Bay 2017), 2017; 26 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover What is \"Chymyst\"?, Concurrent & parallel programming is hard, \"Dining philosophers\", Talk overview, Join Calculus: A New Hope, Concurrent data and concurrent functions, Join Calculus: The Genesis, Join Calculus in a Nutshell, Programs = chemical laws + initial molecules, Chymyst: basic features, Chymyst: basic usage, Chymyst: more features, Chymyst: examples I, and Definitions in local scopes."
