  4944,Scala Threads and Futures,"https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/scala-threads-futures/scala_threads_futures_talk.pdf",github.com,math.CA,math.CA cs.DC cs.LO mathematics computer-science real-analysis concurrency formalization survey slides talk github,Sergei Winitzki,2017,null,"Scala Threads and Futures. Beamer talk slides by Sergei Winitzki (Workday, Inc.), 2017; 16 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover JVM threads, ThreadPoolExecutor = thread pool + task queue, Usages of thread pools, First look at scala.concurrent.Future, How does a Future run?, How does map work on a Future?, How to work with APIs returning a Future?, How to convert callback APIs into a Future?, Example: Converting Apache's HttpAsyncClient, \"Mistakes were made\", What is \"thread-safe\", What is \"non-blocking\", Can we avoid \"blocking\"?, and How and when to convert \"blocking\" to \"non-blocking\"."
