  5128,"Inference and Representation (DS-GA-1005, CSCI-GA.2569), MCMC: Lab10","https://github.com/joanbruna/infrep17/blob/master/labs/lab10/Lab10.pdf",github.com,math.PR,math.PR cs.DS cs.LG mathematics computer-science markov-chains machine-learning statistical-mechanics symplectic-geometry slides github,Rahul G. Krishnan,2016,null,"Inference and Representation (DS-GA-1005, CSCI-GA.2569), MCMC: Lab10. Beamer slides by Rahul G. Krishnan, 2016; 17 pages. From a repository described as: We will study latent graphical models (Latent Dirichlet Allocation, Gaussian Processes), state-space models for (Kalman Filter, HMMs), Gibbs Models, Deep generative models (Variational autoencoders, GANs) covering both the methods (inference, sampling algorithms, learning, exponential families) and…. Sections: MCMC; Hamiltonian Monte Carlo. Slides cover You have seen atleast two few different ways to estimate, Importance Sampling, Three conditions you need to construct a valid MCMC kernel, Stationary Distribution, For the MH kernel we construct,, Gibbs Sampling, Proof, Hamiltonian, Leapfrog Integrator, and Inference."
