  5149,How Triton can help to reverse virtual machine based software protections - How to don't kill yourself when you reverse obfuscated codes.,"https://gitlab.com/The-Real-TechLord/Triton/-/blob/master/src/publications/CSAW2016-SOS-Virtual-Machine-Deobfuscation-RThomas_JSalwan.pdf",gitlab.com,math.HO,math.HO cs.LO math.RT mathematics computer-science mathematical-writing-and-practice formal-methods representation-theory slides talk gitlab,Jonathan Salwan and Romain Thomas,2016,null,"How Triton can help to reverse virtual machine based software protections - How to don't kill yourself when you reverse obfuscated codes. Beamer slides by Jonathan Salwan, and Romain Thomas, 2016; 64 pages. From a repository described as: Triton is a dynamic binary analysis (DBA) framework. It provides internal components like a Dynamic Symbolic Execution (DSE) engine, a Taint Engine, AST representations of the x86 and the x86-64 instructions set semantics, SMT simplification passes, an SMT Solver Interface and, the last but not…. Sections: The Triton framework SSTIC2015-Saudel-Salwan; Virtual Machine Based Software Protections; Demo: Tigress VM; Demo: Unknown VM. Slides cover About us, Roadmap of this talk, The Triton framework [6], The API’s input - Semantics with a context, The API’s input - AST representations, Example - How to get implicit and explicit read registers, Ok, but what can I do with all of this?, VM Based Software Protections, VM abstract architecture, and A jump table based dispatcher."
  5150,Dynamic Binary Analysis and Obfuscated Codes - How to don't kill yourself when you reverse obfuscated codes.,"https://gitlab.com/The-Real-TechLord/Triton/-/blob/master/src/publications/StHack2016_Dynamic_Binary_Analysis_and_Obfuscated_Codes_RThomas_JSalwan.pdf",gitlab.com,math.HO,math.HO cs.DS cs.LO math.RT mathematics computer-science mathematical-writing-and-practice algorithms formal-methods representation-theory slides talk gitlab,Jonathan Salwan and Romain Thomas,2016,null,"Dynamic Binary Analysis and Obfuscated Codes - How to don't kill yourself when you reverse obfuscated codes. Beamer slides by Jonathan Salwan, and Romain Thomas, 2016; 75 pages. From a repository described as: Triton is a dynamic binary analysis (DBA) framework. It provides internal components like a Dynamic Symbolic Execution (DSE) engine, a Taint Engine, AST representations of the x86 and the x86-64 instructions set semantics, SMT simplification passes, an SMT Solver Interface and, the last but not…. Sections: Obfuscation Introduction; Dynamic Binary Analysis Introduction; The Triton SSTIC2015-Saudel-Salwan framework; Simplify expressions; Analyse opaque predicates; Reconstruct a CFG from trace differential; Recover the algorithm of a VM; Future Works. Slides cover About us, Roadmap of this talk, Example: CFG flattened, Dynamic Binary Analysis Introduc-, SBA vs DBA, Offline analysis and symbolic emulation, In what scenarios should I use Triton?, Simplification passes may be applied at different levels, Simplify expressions via z3, and Analyse opaque predicates (3)."
