  5167,"Optimal bound on qFI based on expectation values of input state, Palma Conf2016","https://gitlab.com/iagobaapellaniz/Optimal-Estimation-qFI-Talk-2016/-/blob/master/out/PalmaConf2016.pdf",gitlab.com,math.OC,math.OC cs.LG mathematics computer-science optimization slides gitlab,null,2016,null,"Optimal bound on qFI based on expectation values of input state, Palma Conf2016. Beamer slides, 2016; 41 pages. From a repository described as: Presentation of the recent advances on the tight bounding of the quantum Fisher Information. Sections: Introduction and Motivation; QFI based on expectation values: Are they optimal?; Case study; Conclusion and outlook. Subsections include Optimisation problem, Fidelities, Spin-squeezed states, and Unpolarised Dicke states. Slides cover Basics on quantum metrology, The quantum Fisher information, For large systems, we only have a couple of expectation values, and Optimisation problem."
  5168,Introduction to Transfer Learning,"https://gitlab.com/iamfaith/MachineLearning/-/blob/master/TransferLearning.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML math.CT math.HO computer-science statistics mathematics machine-learning category-theory cognitive-science history-of-mathematics survey slides gitlab,Jindong Wang,2016,null,"Introduction to Transfer Learning. Beamer slides by Jindong Wang, 2016; 23 pages. From a repository described as: 1.1 Machine Learning的一些理解 机器学习的概念自不用多说。这里我仅提到一点,机器学习在学科分类上是属于实现人工智能的一种重要方法,注定它和AI是不可分的。其实,传统的AI一直都侧重解决三个步骤的问题:知识的表示、知识的获取和知识的学习。其中,机器学习涵盖了知识的获取和学习两大部分,是AI的核心部分。其实说白了,ML解决的就是怎么从已知推断未知,它走的是归纳(induction)这个自上而下的过程,AI中还有一个相对立的知识体系叫做演绎(deduction),这个主要是自动推理的范畴,和机器学习基本关系不大,是较独立的一支。. Sections: Taxonomy; Application; Future Work. Subsections include Why Transfer Learning?, Category, Transfer Learning with Deep Learning, Negative Transfer, Activity Recognition, Other Applications, and Resources. Slides cover Examples, Why Transfer Learning?, Brief History, When can we Use TL?, Formulation, Different Views, Categoried by Domain and Task, Categoried by Approaches, Transfer Learning with Deep Learning, and Negative Transfer."
  5169,Introduction to git,"https://gitlab.com/iamfalln1/mygit/-/blob/master/lect1.pdf",gitlab.com,math.AG,math.AG math.SG mathematics geometric-invariant-theory history-of-mathematics survey slides talk gitlab,Sunil T T,2016,null,"Introduction to git. Beamer slides by Sunil T T, 2016; 27 pages. From a repository described as: git tutorial slides for KTU students. These slides are from a hands on workshop for faculty. Slides cover Why you need version control, Installing git, Initialize git repository, Inside the git repo, Git work flow, Examine git status, Add the file to staging area, Commit changes, Add more files, Still more files, Commit more files, Let us see the history, Checkout, and Checkout from previous commits."
  5170,Librería en C++ para procesos Gaussianos - Procesos Gaussianos para Regresión,"https://gitlab.com/in-silico/slides/-/blob/gh-pages/slides/gplib_thesis.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.CC,cs.CC computer-science complexity-theory slides gitlab,Carlos GonzálezAlejandro SuárezManuel Pineda,2016,null,"Librería en C++ para procesos Gaussianos - Procesos Gaussianos para Regresión. Beamer slides by Carlos GonzálezAlejandro SuárezManuel Pineda, 2016; 38 pages, in Spanish. Part of Slides In-silico. Subject (translated): theoretical computer science and complexity theory. Sections: Introducción; Implementación de la Librería; Regresión Completa; Aproximación FITC; Funcionalidad y Desempeño; Conclusiones."
