  5172,Random Phase Approximation,"https://gitlab.com/mussard/talks_and_notes/-/blob/master/doc/talk_201604.pdf",gitlab.com,math.GT,math.GT math.DG mathematics differential-topology slides talk gitlab,B. Mussard,2016,null,"Random Phase Approximation. Beamer talk slides by B. Mussard, 2016; 23 pages. From a repository described as: You will find all talks, notes and posters I produced during my successive academic jobs. Sections: title; Occurences; Piecewise linear; Constancy condition; Implementation SCF; FracCharge : Example; FracCharge : SCF H2+; FracSpin : SCF H2; Basic variable for RPA; With scaled orbitals; RPA equations; Two extensions. Slides cover Context and Motivation, Fractional Charge and Fractional Spin : Motivation, Fractional Charge and Fractional Spin : Occurences, Exact conditions, Fractional Charge, Fractional Spin, Behavior of methods, Implementation for Self-Consistent Field methods, Fractional Charge : Example of H+, and Fractional Spin : Example of H2."
  5173,Fractional-charge and Fractional-spin errors,"https://gitlab.com/mussard/talks_and_notes/-/blob/master/doc/talk_201605.pdf",gitlab.com,math.GT,math.GT math.DG mathematics differential-topology slides talk gitlab,B. Mussard,2016,null,"Fractional-charge and Fractional-spin errors. Beamer talk slides by B. Mussard, 2016; 25 pages. From a repository described as: You will find all talks, notes and posters I produced during my successive academic jobs. Sections: title; Occurences; Piecewise linear; Constancy condition; Implementation SCF; FracCharge : Example; Methods tested; FracCharge : SCF H2+; FracCharge : A more detailed analysis; FracSpin : SCF H2; FracSpin : A more detailed analysis; RPA equations. Slides cover Fractional Charge and Fractional Spin : Motivation, Fractional Charge and Fractional Spin : Occurences, Exact conditions, Fractional Charge, Fractional Spin, Behavior of methods, Implementation for Self-Consistent Field methods, Calculations, Presentation of the results (Example of H+, Fractional Charge : Example of H+, and Example of H+."
