  5233,"Machine Learning I Lecture II: Tutorial on probability theory","https://github.com/mackelab/machine-learning-I/blob/master/slides/lecture2_probability/lecture2.pdf",github.com,math.PR,math.PR cs.LG math.FA stat.ML mathematics computer-science statistics probability functional-analysis machine-learning lecture-notes slides github,null,2015,null,"Machine Learning I Lecture II: Tutorial on probability theory. Beamer lecture slides, 2015; 14 pages. From a repository described as: Slides and lecture notes for the course 'machine learning I' taught at the Graduate School Neural Information Processing in Tuebingen in the first half of the Winter-Semester 2012. The course is a one-semester, once weekly course for students studying for a Master's degree in Neural Information…. Sections: Discrete probability distributions; Multivariate distributions: Joints, conditionals and marginals; Continuous probability distributions. Slides cover Plan for today, The importance of conditional probabilities: Interpreting medical tests, Expectation and covariance of multivariate distributions, Independence of random variables, Continous random variables, and Bivariate continuous distributions: Marginalization, Conditioning and Independence."
  5234,"Machine Learning I Lecture III: Gaussian models","https://github.com/mackelab/machine-learning-I/blob/master/slides/lecture3_gaussians/lecture3.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML math.ST computer-science statistics mathematics machine-learning functional-analysis probability lecture-notes slides github,null,2015,null,"Machine Learning I Lecture III: Gaussian models. Beamer lecture slides, 2015; 9 pages. From a repository described as: Slides and lecture notes for the course 'machine learning I' taught at the Graduate School Neural Information Processing in Tuebingen in the first half of the Winter-Semester 2012. The course is a one-semester, once weekly course for students studying for a Master's degree in Neural Information…. Sections: Wrap up: Continuous random variables; Gaussians; Bayesian inference for Gaussians. Slides cover Plan for today, Bivariate continuous distributions: Marginalization, Conditioning and Independence, The univariate Gaussian, A (very important) aside: Products of Gaussian pdfs are (unnormalized) Gaussians pdfs, Bayesian Inference for the Gaussian, What if the variance is not given?, and What if both the mean and the variance are unknown?."
  5235,"Machine Learning I Lecture IV: Bayesics of Inference","https://github.com/mackelab/machine-learning-I/blob/master/slides/lecture4_bayesianinference/lecture4.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML math.ST computer-science statistics mathematics machine-learning lecture-notes slides github,null,2015,null,"Machine Learning I Lecture IV: Bayesics of Inference. Beamer lecture slides, 2015; 17 pages. From a repository described as: Slides and lecture notes for the course 'machine learning I' taught at the Graduate School Neural Information Processing in Tuebingen in the first half of the Winter-Semester 2012. The course is a one-semester, once weekly course for students studying for a Master's degree in Neural Information…. Sections: Bayesian Inference; Example: Bayesian coin toss; Conjugate priors and the exponential family. Slides cover Plan for today, Why was inference so easy here?, and How can we put our coin-example into this framework?."
  5236,"Machine Learning I Lecture V: Linear Regression Revisited","https://github.com/mackelab/machine-learning-I/blob/master/slides/lecture5_linearregression/lecture5.pdf",github.com,math.ST,math.ST cs.LG stat.ME stat.ML mathematics computer-science statistics machine-learning lecture-notes slides github,null,2015,null,"Machine Learning I Lecture V: Linear Regression Revisited. Beamer lecture slides, 2015; 13 pages. From a repository described as: Slides and lecture notes for the course 'machine learning I' taught at the Graduate School Neural Information Processing in Tuebingen in the first half of the Winter-Semester 2012. The course is a one-semester, once weekly course for students studying for a Master's degree in Neural Information…. Sections: Linear regression revisited; Bayesian linear regression; Fully Bayesian linear regression. Slides cover Plan for today, Calculating the predictive mean and variance for Bayesian regression, But, where do we get $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ from?, What we have not had time to cover, and Do you want a tutorial before the exam?."
  5237,"Machine Learning I Lecture VI: Linear models for Classification","https://github.com/mackelab/machine-learning-I/blob/master/slides/lecture6_linearclassification/lecture6.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning lecture-notes slides github,null,2015,null,"Machine Learning I Lecture VI: Linear models for Classification. Beamer lecture slides, 2015; 14 pages. From a repository described as: Slides and lecture notes for the course 'machine learning I' taught at the Graduate School Neural Information Processing in Tuebingen in the first half of the Winter-Semester 2012. The course is a one-semester, once weekly course for students studying for a Master's degree in Neural Information…. Sections: Binary classification; Least Square Classification; Fisher's linear discriminant; A generative model: Class-conditional Gaussians. Slides cover Plan for today, and Aside: The multivariate Gaussian."
  5238,"Machine Learning I Lecture VII: Logistic Regression","https://github.com/mackelab/machine-learning-I/blob/master/slides/lecture7_logregression/lecture7.pdf",github.com,math.ST,math.ST cs.LG stat.ME stat.ML mathematics computer-science statistics machine-learning functional-analysis lecture-notes slides github,null,2015,null,"Machine Learning I Lecture VII: Logistic Regression. Beamer lecture slides, 2015; 22 pages. From a repository described as: Slides and lecture notes for the course 'machine learning I' taught at the Graduate School Neural Information Processing in Tuebingen in the first half of the Winter-Semester 2012. The course is a one-semester, once weekly course for students studying for a Master's degree in Neural Information…. Sections: Logistic Regression; Maximum likelihood estimation of Logistic Regression; Bayesian Logistic Regression: Approximating the posterior distribution. Slides cover Plan for today, Iterative Least Squares is a more efficient method for minimizing the cost-function, Visualizing the cost-function of logistic regression, Bayesian inference for this model does not have a closed form solution, The Laplace-Approximation is a simple Gaussian approximation to the posterior, and One last bit of business: The exam."
  5239,"Guest Lecture: An Introduction to 1em","https://github.com/murchandamus/BitcoinLecture/blob/master/Bitcoin-Introduction.pdf",github.com,cs.CR,cs.CR math.CT math.HO computer-science mathematics category-theory history-of-mathematics security-and-privacy survey slides github,null,2015,null,"Guest Lecture: An Introduction to 1em. Beamer lecture slides, 2015; 123 pages. From a repository described as: Please do not tipp the address in the slides, the private key has been shared publicly. You may use this address instead:. Sections: What is Money?; What is Bitcoin?; History of Bitcoin. Slides cover Who am I?, Two Categories of Money, What shortfalls does Money have?, Currency is inefficient and slow, Currency is expensive to maintain, Digital currency lacks privacy, Inflation, Loss of Purchasing Power, Lack of Control, and What is the connection to Bitcoin?."
  5240,"MOO: The Milk Output Optimiser - A management tool for New Zealand dairy farmers or How to milk your cash cow","https://github.com/odow/talks/blob/master/2015/EPOC15_MOO.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS computer-science algorithms slides github,Oscar Dowson,2015,null,"MOO: The Milk Output Optimiser - A management tool for New Zealand dairy farmers or How to milk your cash cow. Beamer slides by Oscar Dowson, 2015; 110 pages. Sections: Why do I care?; Why should you care?; ``research'' in Denmark; ``research'' in Switzerland; A mathematical cow.; The basic model; A non-linear approach; A dynamic programming approach; A two-phase approach; But wait, theres more; Results; Is it worth doing?. Slides cover ”just mip it”."
