  5272,"Practical Optimization Algorithms and Applications - Chapter XI: Quadratic Programming","https://github.com/sunbaby01/UCAS_Course_2020/blob/main/%E5%AE%9E%E7%94%A8%E6%9C%80%E4%BC%98%E5%8C%96%E7%AE%97%E6%B3%95%E5%8F%8A%E5%85%B6%E5%BA%94%E7%94%A820-21%E7%A7%8B%E5%AD%A3/ChapterXI.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS math.OC cs.LG computer-science mathematics algorithms optimization lecture-notes book slides github,Lingfeng NIU,2015,null,"Practical Optimization Algorithms and Applications - Chapter XI: Quadratic Programming. Beamer lecture slides by Lingfeng NIU, 2015; 79 pages. From the course-materials archive sunbaby01/UCAS_Course_2020. Sections: Equality-Constrained Quadratic Programs; Inequality-Constrained Quadratic Programs; Perspective and Software. Subsections include Direct Solution of the KKT System, Iterative Solution of the KKT System, Active-Set Methods for Convex QPs, Interior-Point Methods, and The Gradient Projection Method. Slides cover Example - Portfolio Optimization, Direct Solution of the KKT System, Null-Space Method, We discuss several classes of algorithms for solving QPs that contain inequality, Degeneracy, Active-Set Methods for Convex QPs, Finite Termination of Active-Set Algorithm on Strictly, Interior-Point Methods, The Bound-constrained Problem, and Cauchy Point Computation."
  5273,"Practical Optimization Algorithms and Applications - Chapter XII: Penalty and Augmented Lagrangian Methods","https://github.com/sunbaby01/UCAS_Course_2020/blob/main/%E5%AE%9E%E7%94%A8%E6%9C%80%E4%BC%98%E5%8C%96%E7%AE%97%E6%B3%95%E5%8F%8A%E5%85%B6%E5%BA%94%E7%94%A820-21%E7%A7%8B%E5%AD%A3/ChapterXII.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS math.OC cs.LG computer-science mathematics algorithms optimization lecture-notes book slides github,Lingfeng NIU,2015,null,"Practical Optimization Algorithms and Applications - Chapter XII: Penalty and Augmented Lagrangian Methods. Beamer lecture slides by Lingfeng NIU, 2015; 59 pages. From the course-materials archive sunbaby01/UCAS_Course_2020. Sections: The Quadratic Penalty Method; Nonsmooth Penalty Functions; Augmented Lagrangian Method: Equality Constraints; Practical Augmented Lagrangian Methods. Slides cover Update strategy for parameter sequences {μk} and {τk}, How to solve the unconstrained subproblem?, Properties of the Augmented Lagrangian, Bound-Constrained Lagrangian, and Unconstrained Formulation."
  5274,"Practical Optimization Algorithms and Applications - Chapter XIII: Sequential Quadratic Programming","https://github.com/sunbaby01/UCAS_Course_2020/blob/main/%E5%AE%9E%E7%94%A8%E6%9C%80%E4%BC%98%E5%8C%96%E7%AE%97%E6%B3%95%E5%8F%8A%E5%85%B6%E5%BA%94%E7%94%A820-21%E7%A7%8B%E5%AD%A3/ChapterXIII.pdf",github.com,cs.DS,cs.DS math.OC cs.LG math.CA computer-science mathematics algorithms optimization real-analysis mathematical-logic lecture-notes survey book slides github,Lingfeng NIU,2015,null,"Practical Optimization Algorithms and Applications - Chapter XIII: Sequential Quadratic Programming. Beamer lecture slides by Lingfeng NIU, 2015; 64 pages. From the course-materials archive sunbaby01/UCAS_Course_2020. Sections: Local SQP Method; Preview of Practical SQP Method; Algorithmic Development; Trust-Region SQP Methods; Convergence Analysis; Perspective and Software. Slides cover The new iterate (xk+1, λk+1) can therefore be defined, Inequality Constraints - IQP, Enforcing Convergence - Step-Acceptance Mechanisms, Merit Functions, The Inconsistence of Linearized Constraints, The Maratos Effect, Exact Nonsmooth Penalty Functions, Second-Order Correction, Algorithm: Watchdog, and The Trust-Region Subproblem."
  5275,Elm-style Functional Reactive Programming demystified,"https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/elm-talk/elm_talk.pdf",github.com,cs.LO,cs.LO math.CA cs.DC cs.PL computer-science mathematics real-analysis concurrency formal-methods formalization survey slides talk github,Sergei Winitzki,2015,null,"Elm-style Functional Reactive Programming demystified. Beamer talk slides by Sergei Winitzki (SF Types, Theorems, and Programming Languages), 2015; 30 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover Part 1. Functional reactive programming in Elm, Transformational vs. reactive programs, Difficulties in reactive programming, Czaplicki’s original Elm 2012 in a nutshell, Elm operational semantics 1: Current values, Elm operational semantics 3: Updating combinators, Example of using foldp, Asynchrony and concurrency in Elm, Some limitations of Elm-style FRP, The JavaScript backend for Elm (2015), Some conservative extensions of Elm, Boolean arithmetic: notation, Propositional linear-time temporal logic (LTL), and Interpreting values typed by LTL."
  5276,Functional Reactive Programming and Elm,"https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/elm-talk/elm_talk_bayhac2015.pdf",github.com,math.CA,math.CA cs.LO cs.DC mathematics computer-science real-analysis concurrency formalization survey slides talk github,Sergei Winitzki,2015,null,"Functional Reactive Programming and Elm. Beamer talk slides by Sergei Winitzki, 2015; 26 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover Part 1. Functional reactive programming and Elm, Difficulties in reactive programming, FRP basics, Czaplicki's (2012) core Elm in a nutshell, Details: Elm type judgments [Czaplicki 2012], Elm operational semantics 0: Current values, Elm operational semantics 1: Initial values, Elm operational semantics 2: Updating signals, Elm operational semantics 3: Updating combinators, GUI building: \"Hello, world\" in Elm, Example of using scan, Typical GUI boilerplate in Elm, Some limitations of Elm-style FRP, and Elm-style FRP: the good parts."
  5277,Reviving the Traditional Russian Orthography for the 21st Century,"https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/oldru/oldru_talk.pdf",github.com,math.CA,math.CA cs.LO cs.DC mathematics computer-science real-analysis concurrency formalization survey slides talk github,Sergei Winitzki,2015,null,"Reviving the Traditional Russian Orthography for the 21st Century. Beamer talk slides by Sergei Winitzki (Text By The Bay 2015), 2015; 15 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover Old Russian Orthography: what and why, Old Russian orthography: example, .or when guided by a committee of experts, Processing old Russian orthography in 2000, Back to 2015: State of the art, The oldrus-ispell project (1999-2003), The KOI8-C encoding and screen fonts, Working with the oldrus-ispell dictionary, Main linguistic challenge: recover lost information, Disambiguation tasks, Converter for the old Russian orthography, and Outlook: the future of the old Russian orthography."
