  5329,Temporal Logic and Functional Reactive Programming,"https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/frp/frp_talk.pdf",github.com,cs.LO,cs.LO math.LO math.CA cs.SE computer-science mathematics mathematical-logic formal-methods real-analysis category-theory survey slides talk github,Sergei Winitzki,2014,null,"Temporal Logic and Functional Reactive Programming. Beamer talk slides by Sergei Winitzki (Bay Area Categories and Types), 2014; 23 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover What is reactive programming, The uses of logic in computer science, Part 1: Introduction to temporal logic, Boolean algebra: notation, Boolean algebra: example, Synthesis of Boolean programs, Propositional linear-time temporal logic (LTL), Temporal xpoints and the μ-calculus notation, LTL: interpretation of Until, LTL: temporal speci cation, LTL: disjunctive normal form, The failure of LTL program synthesis, Part 2: Temporal logic as type theory, and Interpreting values typed by LTL."
