  5369,KernelGen A prototype of auto-parallelizing Fortran/C compiler for NVIDIA GPUs,"https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/main/polly/www/publications/kernelgen-ncar-2012-slides.pdf",github.com,cs.DC,cs.DC cs.PL cs.LG computer-science ml-systems programming-languages slides github,Dmitry Mikushin and Nikolay Likhogrud and Hou Yunqing and Sergey Kovylov,2013,null,"KernelGen A prototype of auto-parallelizing Fortran/C compiler for NVIDIA GPUs. Beamer slides by Dmitry Mikushin, Nikolay Likhogrud, Hou Yunqing, and Sergey Kovylov, 2013; 28 pages. Part of The LLVM Compiler Infrastructure: This repository contains the source code for LLVM, a toolkit for the construction of highly optimized compilers, optimizers, and run-time environments. Slides cover KernelGen research project, WRF specifics, Project Team, Project state in September 2011 (v0.1), Project state in September 2012 (v0.2 nvptx), OpenACC: no external calls, OpenACC: no pointers tracking, KernelGen: can parallelize while loops, Benchmarking: matmul, KernelGen concepts, LLVM for Fortran & GPU in a nutshell, Please help us to improve the quality and usefulness of KernelGen, and Download link for this presentation."
