  5372,Introduction to Join Calculus,"https://github.com/winitzki/talks/blob/master/join_calculus/join_calculus_talk.pdf",github.com,math.CA,math.CA mathematics real-analysis concurrency formalization survey slides talk github,Sergei Winitzki,2013,null,"Introduction to Join Calculus. Beamer talk slides by Sergei Winitzki (Scala Study Group), 2013; 15 pages. Part of Talk slides for various meetup presentations: Abstract: I give an introduction to Join calculus, a declarative formalism for concurrent programming. Join Calculus is a development of Pi-calculus that is higher-level and easier to use in practice. Slides cover A taste of OCaml, Join Calculus in a nutshell, Join Calculus: Examples, Limitations and restrictions of Join Calculus, Local scope and recursion, Comparison: Join Calculus vs. Actor model, Implementation of Join Calculus, and Conclusions and outlook."
