  5564,"Deep Learning Lecture 05: Recurrent Neural Networks","https://github.com/HITLittleZheng/HITCS/blob/main/%E9%80%89%E4%BF%AE%E8%AF%BE%E7%A8%8B/%E8%AE%A1%E7%AE%97%E6%9C%BA%E8%A7%86%E8%A7%89/RNN%20%E8%A1%A5%E5%85%85%E7%9F%A5%E8%AF%86.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML cs.CL computer-science statistics machine-learning large-language-models probability algorithms lecture-notes slides github,Wanxiang Che,2026,null,"Deep Learning Lecture 05: Recurrent Neural Networks. Lecture slides (PDF) by Wanxiang Che, 2026; 18 pages. From the course-materials archive HITLittleZheng/HITCS. Sections: Recurrent Neural Networks; Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs); Language Models; Traditional Language Models; Recurrent Neural Network Language Model (RNNLM); BackPropagation Through Time (BPTT); The vanishing gradient problem; A “solution”; A better “solution”; A better “solution” (cont.); Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM); Gated Recurrent Unites, GRU (Cho et al. 2014). Slides cover At a single time step t, A language model computes a probability for a sequence of word, An incorrect but necessary Markov assumption!, Condition the neural network on all previous inputs, Modeling the infinite context (Mikolov et al. 2010-2013), Total error is the sum of each error at time step t, Use the same as the backpropagation algorithm as we use in deep, ∂∂EEtt, Intuition, and Recall the original transition equation."
