  5643,"Scaling Hermeneutics: Qualitative Coding","https://github.com/bvasiles/empirical-methods/blob/master/assets/presentations/luo.pdf",github.com,cs.CL,cs.CL cs.AI cs.LG computer-science large-language-models lecture-notes slides github,null,2026,null,"Scaling Hermeneutics: Qualitative Coding. Slides (PDF), 2026; 13 pages. From the course-materials archive bvasiles/empirical-methods. Sections: Scaling Hermeneutics: Qualitative Coding with LLMs for Reflexive Content Analysis; Paper Summary; Background; The Hybrid Workflow; Hermeneutic Trade-offs; Case Study — W.E.B. Du Bois in the News; What Is the LLM Used For?; Prompting Strategies; Adapting the Codebook for LLMs; How Do the Authors Trust the Results?; Key Findings; Takeaways. Slides cover Previous automation approaches fall short, Phase 1 — Reflexive Content Analysis, Preserved: Human-led codebook refinement; adapting descriptions for LLM, New York Times articles referencing Du Bois, 1970–2023, Does, Chain-of-thought prompt in four steps, Gold standard: 111 passages independently coded by two humans,, Model performance (GPT-4, Per Code + CoT), and Codebook adaptation: Make all implicit assumptions explicit; single word changes."
  5644,Self-reflection in Automated,"https://github.com/bvasiles/empirical-methods/blob/master/assets/presentations/singhal.pdf",github.com,cs.CL,cs.CL cs.AI cs.LG computer-science large-language-models lecture-notes slides github,Anmol Singhal,2026,null,"Self-reflection in Automated. Slides (PDF) by Anmol Singhal, 2026; 10 pages. From the course-materials archive bvasiles/empirical-methods. Sections: Self-reflection in Automated Qualitative Coding; Motivation and Problem Statement; Two-Stage Annotation Pipeline; Methodology; Codebook development and first-stage coding; Error analysis; Prompting for secondary LLM critique; Results; Discussion Points; Thoughts on the Paper. Slides cover Problem, Two-Stage, Step 1: Codebook development and first-stage coding, RQ: How senior members of the Apache Software Foundation, One author audited a random sample of 60 stage-one positive, Sufficiency rule: Critic overturns the positive only if no cited, Eval Phase 3: Classification Performance on 150 Randomly Sampled Passages, Specific division of labor between the two stages of the pipeline, and Multi-stage evaluation process revealed important insights."
  5645,"Muhammad Naeem, Tracy Smith, Lorna Thomas","https://github.com/bvasiles/empirical-methods/blob/master/assets/presentations/wang.pdf",github.com,cs.CL,cs.CL cs.AI cs.LG computer-science large-language-models lecture-notes slides github,Chenjie Wang,2026,null,"Muhammad Naeem, Tracy Smith, Lorna Thomas. Slides (PDF) by Chenjie Wang, 2026; 12 pages. From the course-materials archive bvasiles/empirical-methods. Slides cover The Six-Step AI-Assisted Process, Information provided to ChatGPT before analysis, Step 2: Keyword Selection — AI vs. Manual, Step 3: Coding — AI vs. Manual, 4Rs Framework for Themes: Reciprocal, Recognizable, Responsive, Resourceful, Authors' proposed solutions, and Strengths."
