  5650,"15-experiments-pt3: Part 15: Experiments Pt3","https://github.com/bvasiles/empirical-methods/blob/master/slides/15-experiments-pt3.pdf",github.com,math.ST,math.ST cs.LG math.AG math.OA mathematics computer-science statistics birational-geometry machine-learning operator-algebras lecture-notes slides github,null,2026,null,"15-experiments-pt3: Part 15: Experiments Pt3. Slides (PDF), 2026; 56 pages. From the course-materials archive bvasiles/empirical-methods. Slides cover Readings, The generalization of causal connections, Four Types of Validity, Regression to the Mean, Hypothesis Tests, Aside: P-Value Controversy, Consider Four Consecutive Coin Flips, Is Coin Fair?, Type I and Type II Errors, Numbers and Nonsense, and Selection Bias."
  5651,"16-regression-pt1: Part 16: Regression Pt1","https://github.com/bvasiles/empirical-methods/blob/master/slides/16-regression-pt1.pdf",github.com,math.ST,math.ST stat.ME mathematics statistics perfectoid-spaces lecture-notes slides github,null,2026,null,"16-regression-pt1: Part 16: Regression Pt1. Slides (PDF), 2026; 78 pages. From the course-materials archive bvasiles/empirical-methods. Slides cover Outline for Today, [17-803] Empirical Methods, Spring 2024, Best Model? Minimize Error, Assessing the Accuracy of the Coefficient Estimates, Key idea for empirical research, Let’s make it more realistic, Interaction Effects, Potential Problem: Non-Linearity of the Data, Potential Problem: Non-Constant Variance of Error Terms (“Heteroscedasticity”), Potential Problem: Collinearity, There are two possible models you could fit to this data, Why are low quality diamonds more expensive?, and Now we see the relationship we expect."
  5652,"17-regression-pt2: Part 17: Regression Pt2","https://github.com/bvasiles/empirical-methods/blob/master/slides/17-regression-pt2.pdf",github.com,math.ST,math.ST stat.ME mathematics statistics category-theory perfectoid-spaces lecture-notes slides github,null,2026,null,"17-regression-pt2: Part 17: Regression Pt2. Slides (PDF), 2026; 31 pages. From the course-materials archive bvasiles/empirical-methods. Slides cover [17-803] Empirical Methods, Spring 2024, What happens when you combine a continuous and a categorical variable?, Which model is better for this data?, Why are low quality diamonds more expensive?, Let’s remove that strong linear pattern, Now we see the relationship we expect, The number of flights that leave NYC per day, Modeling the week day effect, Our model seems to fail starting in June, and The model fails to accurately predict the number of flights on Saturday."
