  5724,"Properties, State, Process and Cycle","https://github.com/raman3366/rit.thermodynamics/blob/main/02%20PRESENTATIONS/UNIT%2001/ME23312_Unit_I_02_Properties_State_Process_and_Cycle.pdf",github.com,physics.class-ph,physics.class-ph physics.flu-dyn physics thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer lecture-notes slides github,Dr. Anantha Raman L,2026,null,"Properties, State, Process and Cycle. Slides (PDF) by Dr. Anantha Raman L, 2026; 17 pages. Part of ME23312 — Engineering Thermodynamics: Lecture presentations, lecture notes, and supporting material for the course ME23312 – Engineering Thermodynamics, offered to II Year Mechanical Engineering students during the 2026–27 ODD semester. Slides cover In this presentation, Properties, What a property is, Intensive and extensive properties, Specific properties, State, State of a system, Process, path and cycle, Process, The named processes, Path and cycle, Point functions and path, Point functions and path functions, and Heat and work are not properties."
  5725,"Thermodynamic Equilibrium, Quasi-static and Reversible Processes","https://github.com/raman3366/rit.thermodynamics/blob/main/02%20PRESENTATIONS/UNIT%2001/ME23312_Unit_I_03_Equilibrium_Quasi-static_and_Reversible_Processes.pdf",github.com,physics.class-ph,physics.class-ph physics.flu-dyn physics thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer lecture-notes slides github,Dr. Anantha Raman L,2026,null,"Thermodynamic Equilibrium, Quasi-static and Reversible Processes. Slides (PDF) by Dr. Anantha Raman L, 2026; 17 pages. Part of ME23312 — Engineering Thermodynamics: Lecture presentations, lecture notes, and supporting material for the course ME23312 – Engineering Thermodynamics, offered to II Year Mechanical Engineering students during the 2026–27 ODD semester. Slides cover In this presentation, Thermodynamic equilibrium, What equilibrium means, The three conditions of equilibrium, Why equilibrium matters, The quasi-static process, Sudden versus slow compression, The quasi-static (quasi-equilibrium) process, An idealisation that real processes approach, Reversible and irreversible, Reversible process, Irreversible process, Causes of irreversibility, and Free expansion."
