  6609,"Artificial Intelligence DSE 3252: Part 2: Problem Solving Agents","https://github.com/kartabyakrishna/Data-Science-Engineering/blob/main/6th-Semester/AI/2-Problem%20Solving%20Agents.pdf",github.com,cs.AI,cs.AI cs.CL math.HO cs.MA computer-science mathematics ai-agents large-language-models mathematical-writing-and-practice algorithms lecture-notes survey slides github,"Rohini R Rao [MAHE-MIT]",2024,null,"Artificial Intelligence DSE 3252: Part 2: Problem Solving Agents. Slides (PDF) by Rohini R Rao [MAHE-MIT], 2024; 41 pages. Part of BTech Data Science Complete Syllabus: This is a guide to the complete 4-year BTech Data Science syllabus and course structure for the 2021-2025 batch put together by your senior Kartabya Krishna. Sections: Artificial Intelligence DSE 3252 Problem Solving; Problem Solving Agents; State Space; Example 1 – Vacuum Agent State Transition Diagram; Well-defined problems and solutions; Problem Formulation Example 1 - Vacuum Agent; Problem Formulation Example 2 – 8 puzzle problem; “formulate, search, execute”; Partial Search Tree; Infrastructure for search algorithms; Uninformed search strategies Breadth First Search; Breadth First Search. Slides cover Are goal based agents that use atomic representations, Example 1 – Vacuum Agent, Problem Formulation, Uninformed search strategies, Measuring problem-solving performance, and Instance of graph search which uses LIFO queue."
  6610,"BTech Data Science Complete Syllabus, Agenda: Part 3: Problem Solving Agents - Local Search","https://github.com/kartabyakrishna/Data-Science-Engineering/blob/main/6th-Semester/AI/3-Problem%20Solving%20Agents-Local%20Search.pdf",github.com,cs.AI,cs.AI cs.DS cs.CL math.HO computer-science mathematics algorithms ai-agents large-language-models mathematical-writing-and-practice optimization lecture-notes survey slides github,"Rashmi Laxmikant Malghan [MAHE-MIT]",2024,null,"BTech Data Science Complete Syllabus, Agenda: Part 3: Problem Solving Agents - Local Search. Slides (PDF) by Rashmi Laxmikant Malghan [MAHE-MIT], 2024; 49 pages. From a repository described as: This is a guide to the complete 4-year BTech Data Science syllabus and course structure for the 2021-2025 batch put together by your senior Kartabya Krishna. Sections: Module 3: Beyond Classical Search 3.1 Local search algorithms and optimization problems; Local Search Algorithm - Inspired By Evolutionary Biology & Statistic Physics; Iterative Improvement Algorithms; Local Search Algorithms; Local Search Algorithm; Search Landscape (Two & Three Dimensions); Summary - Local Search And Optimization; Applications of Local Search Algorithm; Hill- Climbing Search (Heuristic Search); Hill- Climbing Search; Example: 8-queens; Example: n-queens. Slides cover Inspired By, Introduction - Hill Climbing, Local Search, (Heuristic Search), Example: n-, Search Space, and Simulated."
