  7869,"Advanced Section #4: Methods of Dimensionality Reduction: Principal Component Analysis (PCA) (Harvard-IACS/2022-CS109B)","https://github.com/Harvard-IACS/2022-CS109B/blob/main/content/a-sections/a-sec03/Adv_Section3_Slides_ConvergingNNs.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG math.OC stat.ML math.MG computer-science mathematics statistics machine-learning convex-analysis combinatorics probability slides github,null,2022,null,"Advanced Section #4: Methods of Dimensionality Reduction: Principal Component Analysis (PCA) (Harvard-IACS/2022-CS109B). Slides (PDF), 2022; 33 pages. Part of 2022-CS109B Repository. Slides cover Convexity, Is This Convex?, Convex Functions, Why do we care about convex functions?, Stochastic Gradient Descent, Subdifferentiation and Subgradients, Convergence of Ruppert-Polyak SGD, SGD vs Batch Gradient Descent, Escaping Saddle Points, SGD with Momentum, RMSprop, Animated Comparison, and Not everything is great with the new algos."
  7870,"CS109B Advanced Topics in Data Science: A - Sec4 Semantic Segmentation","https://github.com/Harvard-IACS/2022-CS109B/blob/main/content/a-sections/a-sec04/a-sec4_semantic_segmentation.pdf",github.com,cs.CV,cs.CV computer-science computer-vision slides github,null,2022,null,"CS109B Advanced Topics in Data Science: A - Sec4 Semantic Segmentation. Slides (PDF), 2022; 30 pages. Part of 2022-CS109B Repository. Slides cover Computer Vision Tasks, Object Detection & Semantic Segmentation, Task: Image Classification using Fully-Connected CNN, Task: From Classification + Localization to Object Detection, Why Object Detection and Semantic Segmentation, How to Measure Quality in Detection and Segmentation?, Object Detection, Sliding Windows, from Single to Multiple Objects, The Evolution of R-CNN: R-CNN, Fast R-CNN, Faster R-CNN, Single-Stage Detection Without Region Proposals: YOLO, SSD, Semantic Segmentation: Classify Every Pixel, Fully-Convolutional Networks, and U-NET: Long Skip Connections."
  7871,"CS109B Data Science 2: Pavlos Protopapas, Mark Glickman: a - sec5 transfer Learning","https://github.com/Harvard-IACS/2022-CS109B/blob/main/content/a-sections/a-sec05/a-sec5_transferLearning_v2.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML computer-science statistics machine-learning slides github,null,2022,null,"CS109B Data Science 2: Pavlos Protopapas, Mark Glickman: a - sec5 transfer Learning. Slides (PDF), 2022; 51 pages. Part of 2022-CS109B Repository. Slides cover CNNs: “Convolution” Operation, New model architectures consistently, Classify Rarest Animals, Classify Cats, Dogs, Chinchillas etc, Transfer Learning To The Rescue, Basic idea of Transfer Learning, Key Idea: Representation Learning, Representation Learning, Traditional Machine Learning vs Transfer Learning, Transfer Learning – fine tuning, and Transfer learning – The details."
