  8418,"CS 400- Operating Systems Syllabus: Process Concept","https://gitlab.com/AyuK03/NIT-Goa-Resources/-/blob/main/Third%20year/Lectures/CS300/CS%20300-%20Module%202.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.OS,cs.OS computer-science operating-systems computer-architecture philosophy-of-mathematics slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"CS 400- Operating Systems Syllabus: Process Concept. Lecture slides (PDF), 2022; 188 pages. Part of Hello There!: Zubin Shah | 20CSE1030 | https://www.linkedin.com/in/zubinshah1/. Slides cover Process Concept, Process Concept (Cont.), Process in Memory, Operations on Processes, Bounded-Buffer – Producer, Communications in Client-Server Systems, Single and Multithreaded Processes, Windows Multithreaded C Program, Signal Handling (Cont.), Critical-Section Handling in OS, Semaphore Usage, Dining-Philosophers Problem, Determining Length of Next CPU, and Example of Multilevel Feedback."
  8419,"CS 400- Operating Systems Syllabus: What is an Operating System?","https://gitlab.com/AyuK03/NIT-Goa-Resources/-/blob/main/Third%20year/Lectures/CS300/CS%20400-%20Module%201.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.OS,cs.OS computer-science operating-systems security-and-privacy slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"CS 400- Operating Systems Syllabus: What is an Operating System?. Lecture slides (PDF), 2022; 70 pages. Part of Hello There!: Zubin Shah | 20CSE1030 | https://www.linkedin.com/in/zubinshah1/. Slides cover What is an Operating System?, Computer System Structure, Four Components of a Computer System, Computer System Organization, I/O Structure, Direct Memory Access Structure, Clustered Systems, Operating-System Operations (cont.), Storage Management, Protection and Security, Operating System Services (Cont.), System Calls, Parameter Passing via Table, and Examples of Windows and Unix System Calls."
  8420,"Hello There!, Operating Systems Notes","https://gitlab.com/AyuK03/NIT-Goa-Resources/-/blob/main/Third%20year/Lectures/CS300/Operating%20Systems%20Notes.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.OS,cs.OS computer-science operating-systems slides gitlab,null,2022,null,"Hello There!, Operating Systems Notes. Lecture slides (PDF), 2022; 111 pages. From a repository described as: Zubin Shah | 20CSE1030 | https://www.linkedin.com/in/zubinshah1/."
  8421,"Hello There!, Concurrency Control","https://gitlab.com/AyuK03/NIT-Goa-Resources/-/blob/main/Third%20year/Lectures/CS301/Concurrency%20Control.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.DC,cs.DC cs.LO cs.OS cs.DB computer-science concurrency operating-systems databases slides gitlab,Dell pc,2022,null,"Hello There!, Concurrency Control. Lecture slides (PDF) by Dell pc, 2022; 11 pages. From a repository described as: Zubin Shah | 20CSE1030 | https://www.linkedin.com/in/zubinshah1/. Slides cover Lock-Based Protocols, Example of a transaction performing locking, Pitfalls of Lock-Based Protocols, The potential for deadlock exists in most locking protocols. Deadlocks are a, The Two-Phase Locking Protocol, Lock Conversions, and Automatic Acquisition of Locks."
