  9202,SPH data visualization with ParaView,"https://github.com/jfavre/Visualization-training/blob/master/slides/Gridless-data-visualization.pdf",github.com,cs.DC,cs.DC cs.PF computer-science high-performance-computing lecture-notes slides github,null,2021,null,"SPH data visualization with ParaView. Slides (PDF), 2021; 22 pages. From a repository described as: This repository contains the material used for the Scientific Visualization course, organized online by the Swiss National Supercomputing Centre (CSCS) on May 17-18, 2021. The course covers the following topics:. Slides cover Data, Grids in VTK, Gadget-2 HDF5 plugin, Available as a shared library plugin on Piz Daint, Does not require a client-side, SPH Interpolators, Remember SPLASH?, Added in VTK in April 2016, Use all particles within a cut-off, See ParaView/ParaView-SMP-Parallel.ipynb, Particle clouds to slices, and Set ParaView to use varying opacity for surfaces."
