  9389,01.Introduction (schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021),"https://github.com/schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021/blob/main/lectures/01.Introduction.pdf",github.com,q-bio.GN,q-bio.GN q-bio.QM quantitative-biology bioinformatics computational-biology survey slides github,MIchael Schatz,2021,null,"01.Introduction (schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021). Lecture slides (PDF) by MIchael Schatz, 2021; 50 pages. Part of EN.601.452 / AS.020.415 Computational Biomedical Research &amp; Advanced Biomedical Research. Slides cover Welcome!, TA: Samantha Zarate, Prerequisites and Resources, Piazza, Schatzlab Overview, Earliest Genomics, Discovery of Chromosomes, The first genetic map, Central Dogma of Molecular Biology, Milestones in DNA Sequencing, Second Generation Sequencing, How much is a petabyte?, How much is a zettabyte?, and Sensors & Metadata."
  9390,"EN.601.452 / AS.020.415 Computational Biomedical Research &amp; Advanced Biomedical Research, 02.sequencing: Part 2","https://github.com/schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021/blob/main/lectures/02.sequencing.pdf",github.com,q-bio.GN,q-bio.GN q-bio.QM quantitative-biology bioinformatics lecture-notes slides github,MIchael Schatz,2021,null,"EN.601.452 / AS.020.415 Computational Biomedical Research &amp; Advanced Biomedical Research, 02.sequencing: Part 2. Lecture slides (PDF) by MIchael Schatz, 2021; 33 pages. From a repository described as: The goal of this course is to prepare undergraduates to understand and perform state-of-the-art biomedical research. This will be accomplished through three main components: (1) classroom-style lectures on cross cutting techniques for biomedical research focusing on data visualization, statistical…. Slides cover Assignment 1: Chromosome Structures, Plotting in Python, Plotting in R / ggplot2, Sensors & Metadata, Second Generation Sequencing, How much is a petabyte?, Sequencing Capacity, How much is a zettabyte?, FASTQC: Is my data any good?, Question?, Paired-end and Mate-pairs, IlluminaSequencing Summary, Typical sequencing coverage, and 2x sequencing."
  9391,"EN.601.452 / AS.020.415 Computational Biomedical Research &amp; Advanced Biomedical Research, 03.assembly: Part 3","https://github.com/schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021/blob/main/lectures/03.assembly.pdf",github.com,q-bio.GN,q-bio.GN q-bio.QM quantitative-biology bioinformatics lecture-notes slides github,MIchael Schatz,2021,null,"EN.601.452 / AS.020.415 Computational Biomedical Research &amp; Advanced Biomedical Research, 03.assembly: Part 3. Lecture slides (PDF) by MIchael Schatz, 2021; 49 pages. From a repository described as: The goal of this course is to prepare undergraduates to understand and perform state-of-the-art biomedical research. This will be accomplished through three main components: (1) classroom-style lectures on cross cutting techniques for biomedical research focusing on data visualization, statistical…. Slides cover Assignment 1: Chromosome Structures, Recap: Sequencing, Second Generation Sequencing, 1x sequencing, 8x sequencing, Pop Quiz!, Why are genomes hard to assemble?, The full tale, Generallyan exponential number of compatible sequences, Contig/Scaffold N50, Pop Quiz 1, and Pop Quiz 2."
  9392,Whole Genome Alignment,"https://github.com/schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021/blob/main/lectures/04.wga.pdf",github.com,q-bio.GN,q-bio.GN q-bio.QM quantitative-biology bioinformatics slides github,MIchael Schatz,2021,null,"Whole Genome Alignment. Lecture slides (PDF) by MIchael Schatz, 2021; 48 pages. Part of EN.601.452 / AS.020.415 Computational Biomedical Research &amp; Advanced Biomedical Research. Slides cover Assignment 1: Chromosome Structures, Assignment 2: Genome Assembly, Halomonas sp. GFAJ-1, Find and decode, Second Generation Sequencing, Read 1: GATTACA, The full tale, Paired-end and Mate-pairs, N50 Length, Goal of WGA, Translocation Inversion Insertion, Pop Quiz 1, and Pop Quiz 2."
  9393,05.humangenome (schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021),"https://github.com/schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021/blob/main/lectures/05.humangenome.pdf",github.com,q-bio.GN,q-bio.GN q-bio.QM quantitative-biology bioinformatics slides github,MIchael Schatz,2021,null,"05.humangenome (schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021). Lecture slides (PDF) by MIchael Schatz, 2021; 51 pages. Part of EN.601.452 / AS.020.415 Computational Biomedical Research &amp; Advanced Biomedical Research. Slides cover Assignment 2: Genome Assembly, Read 1: GATTACA, Pop Quiz 1Assemble these reads using a de Bruijngraph approach (k=3), Pop Quiz 2Assemble these reads using a de Bruijngraph approach (k=3), The human genome, Who is the reference human?, About 8% is missing or incorrect, Let’s finish a human genome, T2T Variants: 1000 Genomes Project, 1000G Mapping & Variants on T2T-CHM13 (Figure 2 -top), and Novel Variants from 1000G on T2T-CHM13 (Fig 4)."
  9394,"Michael Schatz: Lecture 6. Computational Biomedical Research","https://github.com/schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021/blob/main/lectures/06.t2t.pdf",github.com,q-bio.GN,q-bio.GN q-bio.QM quantitative-biology bioinformatics graph-theory lecture-notes slides github,MIchael Schatz,2021,null,"Michael Schatz: Lecture 6. Computational Biomedical Research. Lecture slides (PDF) by MIchael Schatz, 2021; 39 pages. Part of EN.601.452 / AS.020.415 Computational Biomedical Research &amp; Advanced Biomedical Research. Slides cover Assignment 2: Genome Assembly, Assignment 3: Variant Calling, The human genome, Why does it matter?, PacBio Single Molecule Real Time Sequencing, Oxford Nanopore T echnologies (ONT), Oxford Nanopore T echnologies, CsgGbiological pore, “Corrective Lens” for Sequencing, Consensus Accuracy and Coverage, T wo Paradigms for Assembly, Assembly Complexity, CHM13 HiFi assembly graph, and T2T Variants: 1000 Genomes Project."
  9395,07.readmapping - Compatibility Mode,"https://github.com/schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021/blob/main/lectures/07.readmapping.pdf",github.com,q-bio.GN,q-bio.GN cs.DS q-bio.QM quantitative-biology computer-science bioinformatics algorithms book slides github,MIchael Schatz,2021,null,"07.readmapping - Compatibility Mode. Lecture slides (PDF) by MIchael Schatz, 2021; 44 pages. Part of EN.601.452 / AS.020.415 Computational Biomedical Research &amp; Advanced Biomedical Research. Slides cover Assignment 2: Genome Assembly, Assignment 3: Variant Calling, The completesequence of a human genome, Searching for GATTACA, Brute Force Analysis, Lets play the hi/lo game, Searching the Phone Book, Suffix Arrays: Searching the Phone Book, Searching the Index, Bowtie2 Algorithm, Caching and Binary Search, and Learned Index Structures."
  9396,08.editdistance,"https://github.com/schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021/blob/main/lectures/08.editdistance.pdf",github.com,cs.DC,cs.DC cs.DS q-bio.GN cs.LG computer-science quantitative-biology algorithms bioinformatics ml-systems slides github,MIchael Schatz,2021,null,"08.editdistance. Lecture slides (PDF) by MIchael Schatz, 2021; 19 pages. Part of EN.601.452 / AS.020.415 Computational Biomedical Research &amp; Advanced Biomedical Research. Slides cover Assignment 3: Variant Analysis & Mappability, Read Mapping, Personal Genomics, Brute Force Analysis, Searching the Index, Sapling: Accelerating Suffix Array Queries with, Theorem: An alignment of a sequence of length m, Part 2: Edit Distance, Fibonacci Sequence, Bottom-up Fibonacci Sequence, Dynamic Programming, In-exact alignment, Similarity metrics, and AGCACACAàACACACTAin 4 steps."
  9397,09.variantcalling (schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021),"https://github.com/schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021/blob/main/lectures/09.variantcalling.pdf",github.com,math.FA,math.FA cs.DS math.RA math.NA mathematics computer-science functional-analysis algorithms linear-algebra slides github,MIchael Schatz,2021,null,"09.variantcalling (schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021). Lecture slides (PDF) by MIchael Schatz, 2021; 38 pages. Part of EN.601.452 / AS.020.415 Computational Biomedical Research &amp; Advanced Biomedical Research. Slides cover Assignment 3: Variant Analysis & Mappability, Monday’s class, Read Mapping, Similarity metrics, Recurrence Relation for D, Dynamic Programming Matrix, Global Alignment Schematic, Global vs Local Alignment Schematic, Part 2: Variant Calling, The Binomial Distribution, and What is the distribution of tails."
