  9399,"EN.601.452 / AS.020.415 Computational Biomedical Research &amp; Advanced Biomedical Research, 11.annotation: Part 11","https://github.com/schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021/blob/main/lectures/11.annotation.pdf",github.com,q-bio.GN,q-bio.GN q-bio.QM quantitative-biology bioinformatics lecture-notes slides github,MIchael Schatz,2021,null,"EN.601.452 / AS.020.415 Computational Biomedical Research &amp; Advanced Biomedical Research, 11.annotation: Part 11. Lecture slides (PDF) by MIchael Schatz, 2021; 46 pages. From a repository described as: The goal of this course is to prepare undergraduates to understand and perform state-of-the-art biomedical research. This will be accomplished through three main components: (1) classroom-style lectures on cross cutting techniques for biomedical research focusing on data visualization, statistical…. Slides cover Assignment 3: Variant Analysis & Mappability, Monday’s class, Personal Genomics, Structural Variation Sequence Signatures, GFFExample, Getting & Using BEDT ools, BEDT oolsMerge, Plane Sweep to the Rescue!, BEDT oolscommands, and Autism is NOT caused by vaccines."
