  9402,"EN.601.452 / AS.020.415 Computational Biomedical Research &amp; Advanced Biomedical Research, 15.scRNAseq: Part 15","https://github.com/schatzlab/biomedicalresearch2021/blob/main/lectures/15.scRNAseq.pdf",github.com,q-bio.QM,q-bio.QM q-bio.PE quantitative-biology computational-biology lecture-notes slides github,MIchael Schatz,2021,null,"EN.601.452 / AS.020.415 Computational Biomedical Research &amp; Advanced Biomedical Research, 15.scRNAseq: Part 15. Lecture slides (PDF) by MIchael Schatz, 2021; 44 pages. From a repository described as: The goal of this course is to prepare undergraduates to understand and perform state-of-the-art biomedical research. This will be accomplished through three main components: (1) classroom-style lectures on cross cutting techniques for biomedical research focusing on data visualization, statistical…. Slides cover Assignment 4: WDLs, RNA-seq, RNA-seq Challenges, Models for transcript quantification from RNA-seq, Visualization of RNA-Seq results with Volcano Plot, Annotation Summary, Hierarchical Clustering, PCA and t-SNE, Compared to a control, The paradox of averages, A decade of single-cell RNA-seq, and Key Results."
