  10750,"Advanced SQL: 04 — Arrays and User-Defined Functions","https://gitlab.com/anubhavgupta1012/asql-ss20/-/blob/master/lectures/chapter04/advanced-sql-04.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.DB,cs.DB computer-science databases slides gitlab,Torsten Grust,2020,null,"Advanced SQL: 04 — Arrays and User-Defined Functions. Lecture slides (PDF) by Torsten Grust, 2020; 34 pages. Part of Repository zur Vorlesung Advanced SQL: In diesem Repository veröffentlichen wir. Slides cover 1 ┆Arrays: Aliens(?) Inside Table Cells, 2 ┆Array Types, “Simulating” Arrays (Tabular Array Semantics), Example: Tree Encoding (parents[\"] ≡ parent of node \"), Accessing Arrays: Indexing / Slicing, 4 ┆A Bridge Between Arrays and Tables: unnest & array_agg, A Relational Array Programming Pattern, Series and Subscript Generators, Breaking Bad: Parse a Chemical Formula (e.g., C6H5O73−), 6 ┆User-Defined SQL Functions (UDFs), UDFs Can Return Tables, Example UDF: Issue Unique ID, Write Protocol, Table-Generating UDFs: Returning Typed Rows, and LATERAL: SQL's for each-Loop."
  10751,"Advanced SQL: 05 — Window Functions","https://gitlab.com/anubhavgupta1012/asql-ss20/-/blob/master/lectures/chapter05/advanced-sql-05.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.DB,cs.DB computer-science databases information-retrieval slides gitlab,Torsten Grust,2020,null,"Advanced SQL: 05 — Window Functions. Lecture slides (PDF) by Torsten Grust, 2020; 46 pages. Part of Repository zur Vorlesung Advanced SQL: In diesem Repository veröffentlichen wir. Slides cover 1 ┆Window Functions, Window Frame Specifications (Variant: ROWS), Window Frame Specifications: Abbreviations, Q: What is the Chance of Fine Weather on Weekends?, Q: Visible Spots in a Hilly Landscape? — A: MAX Scan!, Looking Left and Right: PARTITION BY, 4 ┆Interlude: Quiz, LAG/LEAD: Row Offsets (Assume: No Partitioning, ORDER BY !), Sessionization (Query Plan), Detecting Landscape Features, Altitude Changes in a Sliding Window, and 8 ┆Numbering and Ranking Rows."
  10752,"Advanced SQL: 06 — Recursion","https://gitlab.com/anubhavgupta1012/asql-ss20/-/blob/master/lectures/chapter06/advanced-sql-06.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.DB,cs.DB cs.FL computer-science databases automata-and-formal-languages condensed-mathematics graph-theory slides gitlab,Torsten Grust,2020,null,"Advanced SQL: 06 — Recursion. Lecture slides (PDF) by Torsten Grust, 2020; 78 pages. Part of Repository zur Vorlesung Advanced SQL: In diesem Repository veröffentlichen wir. Slides cover Computational Limits of SQL, A Giant Step for SQL, Recursion in SQL: WITH RECURSIVE, Semantics of a Self-Referential Query (UNION ALL Variant), Path as Array in Tree %1 (New Rows Trace), Recursive Graph Walks, From All Nodes at the Same Time, From Regular Expression to Finite State Machine (FSM), Emulating Physical Operator Behavior: Loose Index Scans, K-Means: Forgy Initialization (Query Plan), SQL Notes and Grievance (3), 8 ┆Encoding Cellular Automata in SQL, Accessing the Cell Neighborhood — A Solution! $$, and Simulate the Flow of Liquid (in a 1D Landscape)."
  10753,"Advanced SQL: 07 — Procedural SQL","https://gitlab.com/anubhavgupta1012/asql-ss20/-/blob/master/lectures/chapter07/advanced-sql-07.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.DB,cs.DB computer-science databases derived-algebraic-geometry slides gitlab,Torsten Grust,2020,null,"Advanced SQL: 07 — Procedural SQL. Lecture slides (PDF) by Torsten Grust, 2020; 36 pages. Part of Repository zur Vorlesung Advanced SQL: In diesem Repository veröffentlichen wir. Slides cover 1 ┆Scripting Language + SQL = Procedural SQL, Procedural SQL: Less Round-Trips, Less Stitching, Procedural SQL aka Stored Procedures, 2 ┆Block Structure, 3 ┆Variable Declarations, 4 ┆PL/SQL Expressions, Assignment of Single-Row Query Results, “Returning” From a Table Function (RETURNS SETOF τ), 9 ┆Iterated Statements, Leaving/Shortcutting Loops, Raising Exceptions, A DAG of Cell Dependencies, Dependencies, Topologically Sorted, and Extracing Cell References in a Formula (PL/SQL)."
