  12553,"Part2: Bottou - 02 06 2018","https://github.com/joanbruna/MathsDL-spring18/blob/master/lectures/bottou-02.06.2018.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG math.OC cs.DC stat.ML computer-science mathematics statistics machine-learning optimization ml-systems slides github,null,2018,null,"Part2: Bottou - 02 06 2018. Lecture slides (PDF), 2018; 94 pages. From a repository described as: Tutoring Session with Parallel Curricula (optional): Fridays 11am-12:30pm CIWW 101. The first week only it is 10:30am-12pm. Slides cover Optimization Methods for Machine Learning, 1-Setup, Smoothness, Moments, SG with fixed stepsize, SG with diminishing stepsizes, Nonconvex SG with fixed stepsize, Expected risk versus training time, Asymptotic performance of SG is fragile, Parabola, Standard solutions for batch optimization, Alternate Motivation, and A linear layer."
  12554,"MATHEMATICS OF DEEP: LEARNINGJOAN BRUNA , CIMS + CDS, NYU, SPRING’18: COURSE OVERVIEW","https://github.com/joanbruna/MathsDL-spring18/blob/master/lectures/lecture1.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG math.OC math.ST stat.ML computer-science mathematics statistics machine-learning optimization lecture-notes survey slides github,null,2018,null,"MATHEMATICS OF DEEP: LEARNINGJOAN BRUNA , CIMS + CDS, NYU, SPRING’18: COURSE OVERVIEW. Lecture slides (PDF), 2018; 63 pages. From a repository described as: Tutoring Session with Parallel Curricula (optional): Fridays 11am-12:30pm CIWW 101. The first week only it is 10:30am-12pm. Slides cover COURSE OVERVIEW, PART I: GEOMETRY OF DATA, PART II: GEOMETRY OF OPTIMIZATION AND GENERALIZATION, LOGISTICS, WHAT IS THE CURSE OF DIMENSIONALITY?, SUPERVISED LEARNING, CURSES IN EMPIRICAL RISK MINIMIZATION, UNSUPERVISED LEARNING, OPTIMAL TRANSPORT (SNEAK PREVIEW), OPTIMAL TRANSPORT IN MACHINE LEARNING, COVARIANCE ESTIMATION AND PCA, and CURSES IN OPTIMIZATION."
  12555,"MATHEMATICS OF DEEP: LEARNINGJOAN BRUNA , CIMS + CDS, NYU, SPRING’18: OBJECTIVES LECTURE 10","https://github.com/joanbruna/MathsDL-spring18/blob/master/lectures/lecture10.pdf",github.com,cs.LG,cs.LG stat.ML math.OC computer-science statistics mathematics machine-learning optimization lecture-notes slides github,null,2018,null,"MATHEMATICS OF DEEP: LEARNINGJOAN BRUNA , CIMS + CDS, NYU, SPRING’18: OBJECTIVES LECTURE 10. Lecture slides (PDF), 2018; 115 pages. From a repository described as: Tutoring Session with Parallel Curricula (optional): Fridays 11am-12:30pm CIWW 101. The first week only it is 10:30am-12pm. Slides cover OBJECTIVES LECTURE 10, COMMENTS ON [RAGINSKY , RAKHLIN, TELGARSKY], STABLE MANIFOLD, GRADIENT DESCENT AVOIDS STRICT SADDLES, SMOOTH COUNTER-EXAMPLE, TENSOR METHODS, FROM TENSOR FACTORIZATIONS TO DEEP NETS, TENSOR DECOMPOSITIONS AND NEURAL NETS, DEEP NETWORKS AND SPIN GLASSES, ANAL YSIS OF NON-CONVEX LOSS SURFACES, LINEAR VS NON-LINEAR DEEP MODELS, BETWEEN LINEAR AND RELU: POL YNOMIAL NETS, and PARAMETRIC VS MANIFOLD OPTIMIZATION."
