  12589,"1806overview: Help wanted","https://github.com/mitmath/1806/blob/master/notes/1806overview.pdf",github.com,math.RA,math.RA math.NA mathematics linear-algebra lecture-notes survey book slides github,Steven G. Johnson,2018,null,"1806overview: Help wanted. Slides (PDF) by Steven G. Johnson, 2018; 16 pages. From a repository described as: Welcome to MIT 18.06: Linear Algebra! The Spring 2025 course information, materials, and links are recorded below. Slides cover Help wanted, The textbook, Administrative Details, Syllabus and Calendar, What is 18.06 about?, How do we thinkabout linear systems?, Where do big matrices, Engineering & Scientific Modeling, Data analysis, Not just matrices of numbers, and Computer software."
  12590,Intro to FDFD,"https://github.com/mitmath/18369/blob/master/notes/FDFD.pdf",github.com,math.AP,math.AP math.CA math.NA cs.NA mathematics computer-science numerical-analysis pde real-analysis lecture-notes slides github,null,2018,null,"Intro to FDFD. Slides (PDF), 2018; 48 pages. Part of 18.369(J)/8.315(J): Mathematical Methods in Nanophotonics: This is the repository of course materials for the 18.369(J)/8.315(J) course at MIT, taught by Prof. Steven G. Slides cover Why finite difference?, Time-domain, Inaccurate for dispersive materials, Construction of A x= b, Interlaced E and H grid: crucial for 2nd-order error!, Linearize (i, j, k) to n, Repeat for Ampere’s law, Example 2: 90°bend in metallic coaxial waveguide, There are two kinds of methods to solve A x= b, Iterative methods: memory-efficient⇒suitable for 3D, Direct application of BiCGdoes not work, Perfectly matched layer (absorbing boundary cond.), and Convergence rate depends on κ(A)."
  12591,Laser-Math@18.369,"https://github.com/mitmath/18369/blob/master/notes/Laser-Math%4018.369.pdf",github.com,cs.DC,cs.DC cs.LG computer-science ml-systems lecture-notes slides github,Steven G. Johnson,2018,null,"Laser-Math@18.369. Slides (PDF) by Steven G. Johnson, 2018; 51 pages. Part of 18.369(J)/8.315(J): Mathematical Methods in Nanophotonics: This is the repository of course materials for the 18.369(J)/8.315(J) course at MIT, taught by Prof. Steven G. Slides cover What is a laser?, Resonance, Resonance, Really: Lossless, Linear Gain, Loss, Semiclassical theory, Maxwell–Bloch equations, Advantage: timescales!, “Realistic” application to novel lasers, à“just” solve, Benchmark comparison with previous 1d results, Full 3d calculation, and Lasers: Quick Review."
  12592,Course-overview,"https://github.com/mitmath/18S096/blob/master/lectures/lecture1/Course-overview.pdf",github.com,cs.PL,cs.PL computer-science programming-languages lecture-notes survey slides problem-list github,Steven G. Johnson,2018,null,"Course-overview. Lecture slides (PDF) by Steven G. Johnson, 2018; 7 pages. Part of 18.S096, IAP 2018: Performance Computing in a High Level Language: This is the repository for course materials of the class 18.S096 at MIT in 2018, including problem sets and lecture materials. Lectures by Steven G. Slides cover Administrivia, Course goals, Need a language for all three, A new programming language?, and Installing Julia."
  12593,"第二节 简谐运动——其它振动系统: 第二节 摆动 混沌现象","https://github.com/mobyw/SWJTU-Courses/blob/main/%E8%AF%BE%E7%A8%8B%E8%B5%84%E6%96%99/%E5%A4%A7%E5%AD%A6%E7%89%A9%E7%90%86/%E8%AF%BE%E4%BB%B6/zh12-3.pdf",github.com,math.DS,math.DS math.CA mathematics ode-and-dynamical-systems lecture-notes slides github,null,2018,null,"第二节 简谐运动——其它振动系统: 第二节 摆动 混沌现象. Slides (PDF), 2018; 17 pages, in Chinese. From the course-materials archive mobyw/SWJTU-Courses. Subject (translated): ordinary differential equations and dynamical systems. Slides cover 研究摆动的理想模型 —— 单摆和复摆, 一、单摆, 单摆的特点:小角度单摆的周期T与, 二、复摆(物理摆), 计算转动惯量, 2.自学本章各例题并完成书上的习题(对, 第12章习题课, 一弹簧振子沿 x 轴作简谐振动,已知振动物体的最大, 图中水平面光滑。两弹簧完全相同,且最初处于原, 解: 粘上M 以前, M与m粘接过程水平方向动量守恒,即, and 思考和讨论."
  12594,第三节 波函数 薛定谔方程,"https://github.com/mobyw/SWJTU-Courses/blob/main/%E8%AF%BE%E7%A8%8B%E8%B5%84%E6%96%99/%E5%A4%A7%E5%AD%A6%E7%89%A9%E7%90%86/%E8%AF%BE%E4%BB%B6/zh16-2.pdf",github.com,math.ST,math.ST math.PR stat.ME mathematics statistics probability lecture-notes slides github,null,2018,null,"第三节 波函数 薛定谔方程. Slides (PDF), 2018; 18 pages, in Chinese. From the course-materials archive mobyw/SWJTU-Courses. Subject (translated): probability; statistics and statistical inference. Slides cover 1.波函数, 2.波函数的统计解释, 波的相速度 对物质波而言没有物理意义, 将波函数在空间各点的振幅同时增大D倍,则粒, 薛定谔的波动力学,是在德布罗意提出的物质, 薛定谔同时在固体的比热、统计热力学、原子光, and 1.一维自由粒子的薛定谔方程."
  12595,"第十七章 量子力学应用: 结构框图","https://github.com/mobyw/SWJTU-Courses/blob/main/%E8%AF%BE%E7%A8%8B%E8%B5%84%E6%96%99/%E5%A4%A7%E5%AD%A6%E7%89%A9%E7%90%86/%E8%AF%BE%E4%BB%B6/zh17-1.pdf",github.com,math.PR,math.PR mathematics probability lecture-notes slides github,null,2018,null,"第十七章 量子力学应用: 结构框图. Slides (PDF), 2018; 31 pages, in Chinese. From the course-materials archive mobyw/SWJTU-Courses. Subject (translated): probability. Slides cover 第一节 势阱和势垒, 求解问题的思路, 无限深势阱模型:微观粒子被局限于某区域中,并, 得本问题中的薛定谔方程, 4.讨论解的物理意义, 2.求解方程, and 解释放射性α衰变."
  12596,"第二节 原子结构的量子理论: 一、氢原子的量子力学处理方法","https://github.com/mobyw/SWJTU-Courses/blob/main/%E8%AF%BE%E7%A8%8B%E8%B5%84%E6%96%99/%E5%A4%A7%E5%AD%A6%E7%89%A9%E7%90%86/%E8%AF%BE%E4%BB%B6/zh17-2.pdf",github.com,math.PR,math.PR mathematics probability lecture-notes slides github,null,2018,null,"第二节 原子结构的量子理论: 一、氢原子的量子力学处理方法. Slides (PDF), 2018; 27 pages, in Chinese. From the course-materials archive mobyw/SWJTU-Courses. Subject (translated): probability. Slides cover 一、氢原子的量子力学处理方法, 为了使波函数满足归一化条件和标准条件,自然, 概率密度, (1)径向概率分布, (2)角向概率分布, 结论:电子在核外不是按一定的轨道运动的,量子力学不, 3.量子数的物理意义, (2)角量子数l 表征角动量量子化, 1s态(1s能级), and (3)磁量子数ml 表征空间量子化."
