  12714,"Carnegie Mellon: Bryant and O’Hallaron, Computer Systems: A Programmer’s Perspec;ve, Third Edi;on","https://github.com/stellarkey/912_project/blob/master/4%20%E4%B8%93%E4%B8%9A%E7%A7%91%E7%9B%AE/%E8%AE%A1%E7%AE%97%E6%9C%BA%E7%BB%84%E6%88%90/%E8%B5%84%E6%96%99/CMU-CS213%E8%AF%BE%E4%BB%B6/14-ecf-procs.pdf",github.com,cs.DC,cs.DC math.CO cs.LO computer-science mathematics concurrency graph-theory lecture-notes slides github,Randal Bryant,2018,null,"Carnegie Mellon: Bryant and O’Hallaron, Computer Systems: A Programmer’s Perspec;ve, Third Edi;on. Slides (PDF) by Randal Bryant, 2018; 62 pages. From the course-materials archive stellarkey/912_project. Slides cover Excep&onal Control Flow, Today, Control Flow, Excep&ons, Synchronous Excep&ons, Fault Example: Page Fault, Mul&processing: The Illusion, Mul&processing: The (Tradi&onal) Reality, User View of Concurrent Processes, Error-repor&ng func&ons, Termina&ng Processes, Making fork More Nondeterminis&c, and Process Graph Example."
