  14753,A crash course on CUDA programming,"https://gitlab.com/rosana/Deep-Learning-Boot-Camp/-/blob/master/PDF/threads-n-blocks.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.DC,cs.DC cs.PF computer-science high-performance-computing computer-architecture machine-learning ml-systems lecture-notes slides gitlab,Massimo Bernaschi,2015,null,"A crash course on CUDA programming. Lecture slides (PDF) by Massimo Bernaschi, 2015; 24 pages. Part of Deep Learning Winter School, November 2107.: Participation is via a donation to the A.L.S ASSOCIATION for promoting research of the Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis (ALS) disease. Sections: Parallel Programming in CUDA C; Parallel Addition: main(); Parallel Addition: main() (cont); Review; Review (cont); Threads; Parallel Addition (Threads): main(); Using Threads And Blocks; Indexing Arrays With Threads & Blocks; Indexing Arrays: Example; Addition with Threads and Blocks; Parallel Addition (Blocks/Threads). Slides cover GPU computing is about massive parallelism, With add() running in parallel.let’s do vector addition, Block 1, // copy inputs to device, —Host = CPU, Basic device memory management, Terminology: A block can be split into parallel threads, We’ve seen parallel vector addition using, No longer as simple as just using threadIdx.x or blockIdx.x as indices, and In this example, the red entry would have an index of 21."
