  14981,"03-memdefense: Secure Coding","https://gitlab.com/cegilmont/secure-coding-slides/-/blob/master/secure-coding.pdf",gitlab.com,cs.CR,cs.CR computer-science security-and-privacy lecture-notes slides talk gitlab,Michael Hicks,2014,null,"03-memdefense: Secure Coding. Talk slides (PDF) by Michael Hicks, 2014; 16 pages. From a repository described as: Slides from Software Security course on Coursera. Slides cover Secure coding in C, Design vs. Implementation, Rule: Enforce input compliance, General Principle: Robust coding, Rule: Use safe string functions, Replacements, Rule: Don’t forget NUL terminator, Rule: Understand pointer arithmetic, Defend dangling pointers, Rule: Use NULL after free, Manage memory properly, (Better) Rule: Use safe string library, Rule: Favor safe libraries, and Rule: Use a safe allocator."
